# walks over encoded code driven by instruction effects, such as the constant-time check
#
# the constant-time walk reads an encoded function through the set's decode
# dispatch and follows secrecy from the seeds the caller gives through
# registers and memory extents by each row's footprint, refusing a secret
# that reaches a control transfer, an address or an input a row's timing
# depends on (`masc.core.ct`). it reads under the context the function runs
# under, since that is what decides a conditional row: the selection and
# state the caller compiled for, as aarch64 code that sets dit in its
# prologue or an `__arm_streaming` function. a set whose timing is `none`
# refuses before any walk, and one whose timing is not guaranteed is walked
# as any other but asked no row's latency, and code it clears is answered
# unguaranteed (`ct.required`).
#
# secrecy is held per register row of the set's file and per memory extent.
# a row is secret when some bit of it may hold a secret, so every row sharing
# storage with a secret is: a seed or a write taints each row overlapping the
# register it names, as the file's rows state the relation
# (`register.overlapping`), and a read asks its own row alone. a tuple holds
# no storage of its own, so the walk keeps no secrecy for it and asks its
# members for it, as it reads a pair's operand through both halves. a write leaves
# a row it overwrites holding what it writes, as eax's write zeroing the rest
# of rax or w0's of x0, and adds its secret to a row it overlaps and leaves
# part of, as al's within rax or a lane's within its vector register, whose
# version of its value it moves either way.
# an extent is named by the register its address is formed from, the version
# of that register's value, an offset and a length, so two extents are known
# apart only when both are of one version of one register and do not
# overlap, and every other pair may alias. an address a register adds to, as
# an index, an aarch64 register offset or a risc-v stride, is named off its
# base register's value at an offset the walk does not know: as an offset off
# a base stays within its object, it may alias every extent off the same value
# and none it could not before, and holds none whole, so it neither makes one
# public nor overwrites one. an address written back after the access is at
# its base alone.
#
# the walk follows the stack pointer, the register the canonical frame address
# of the architecture the context enters is stated from, as an offset from
# its value on entry, and every register as wide as it as the same: each holds
# a known offset from it or none. a row's relation (`query.affine`) writing a
# register as wide from one of a known offset makes the written one's known,
# as sub sp, sp, #16, mov x29, sp or lea rbp, [rsp + 8], and so does the stack
# pointer's own change a row states (`effect.Stack`), as push and pop. every
# other write leaves the rows it reaches of no known offset, as an alloca's
# sub sp, sp, a0 or a write of esp within rsp, two paths joining with
# different offsets leave none, and a call leaves none anywhere but in the
# registers its model preserves, so the offsets a loop reaches are finite. an extent addressed through a register
# of a known offset is named off the stack pointer's value on entry, its
# offsets added, so a frame slot stays one extent however the prologue moves
# sp and fp, and an access provably clear of every secret one is not aliased.
# one through a register of no known offset falls back to its version.
# an extent addressed by a symbol is named off the symbol's address, so a
# global stays one extent wherever its address is formed. the walk reads the
# address a symbol forms from the sites the caller gives, the fixups its
# builder left in the code, never from a mnemonic: each site's fixup kind
# states the part of the address its field holds (`fixup.Part`), and its
# relocation kind whether it reaches the symbol through its got slot and
# whether a low part names the instruction of its high part. a register a
# row's relation forms from a site's operand holds that part, as auipc's
# pcrel_hi20, adrp's page or x86 lea's rip-relative address, a low part added
# to a register holding the matching high part completes the address, as
# addi's pcrel_lo12 naming the auipc or a load's :lo12:, wherever in the code
# the two are, a copy or an immediate added carries it, and a load of a got
# slot leaves the symbol's address. paths joining with different addresses
# leave none, and an address the sites do not place is placed as any other.
# the caller's symbol handles name objects known apart, and an offset off one
# stays within its object, as a compiler's code does. an extent off a register
# may be a global's bytes, so an access placed off a symbol may alias it,
# unless the walk places it in the frame, off the stack pointer's value on
# entry, which is no global, or the producer states it holds none
# (`Extent.no_global`), as of a copy the caller's frame holds of an argument
# passed by reference, a trusted claim as the seeds and call models are.
# a secret stored where the address is not known, or anything secret at a
# call, whose callee the walk does not read, may be anywhere afterwards,
# but in the memory the call's model keeps.
# only a store of no secret to bytes the walk places exactly, off one
# register's value at an offset and of a length it knows, makes those bytes
# public again, since a store the walk cannot place exactly may miss the
# secret it would overwrite, and a later secret stored where it may alias
# them takes them back. a global's bytes stay as its seed says. data the program never writes, as a
# constant pool's (`Site.constant`), holds only what a seed of its own symbol
# says, whatever any store or call does, and a symbol's got slot, which the
# loader fills before the code runs and no store of the code reaches, holds
# the symbol's address alone. a register's version is
# the offset of the instruction that last wrote it, or of the join that
# merged two, so the states a loop reaches are finite and the worklist over
# instruction starts reaches a fixed point. the walk keeps a state of its own
# only where control may arrive from more than one place: the entry, an
# instruction a jump, branch or catch reaches, and one two instructions fall
# into. a straight run between them is walked in one state changed in place,
# so the walk's storage grows with the places control joins, not with the
# instructions, and the worklist takes the lowest offset first, so a join
# laid out after the paths into it is walked once they have reached it.
#
# an access the walk places off no symbol and in no frame slot, as a load
# through a pointer parameter or one a typed stream pops the address of, may
# reach memory the walk's caller never saw, as memory its own caller holds a
# secret in, so what it reads holds a secret unless the producer states what
# it reads, as its secrecy types state a pointer's pointee: an access seed,
# naming the instruction's offset and the access by its operand or by its
# position in the footprint. what such an access reads then holds a secret
# only when its seed says so, so the value a load writes or pushes, or the old
# value an atomic read-modify-write or compare-exchange returns, takes the
# seed's secrecy joined with the rest of what the instruction reads. a store
# follows its seed wherever it writes, placed or not: a secret stored where
# the seed states none is refused, worded `ct.STORED`, and one where it states
# a secret is placed as any other store, so no secret enters memory its type
# states public and a read stated public never meets one. an access with no
# seed reads a secret, but where a declassify point made what it reads
# public, and a read the walk places off a symbol or in the frame follows its
# extents, whatever its seed states. so a function the walk accepts
# takes every byte it reads outside its frame and its module's globals as its
# accesses state, the obligation a caller's model of it (`Call.stated`) rests
# on.
#
# the producer may state a private frame extent, its own slot whose address
# never escapes, named off the stack pointer's value on entry as the walk
# names every frame slot, so it holds at every instruction however the
# prologue moves sp and fp. no pointer from outside the function reaches a
# fresh frame whose addresses never escaped, and no callee, which was never
# given them, reads or writes it, so no access the walk does not place in the
# frame aliases a private extent. a secret stored where the address is not
# known, a call's memory it does not keep, a secret at any address after a
# call, or an extent held off another register's version or a symbol leaves
# a private extent holding its own secrecy, a load the walk does not place
# reads none of it, where no access seed decides, and a call's join takes
# nothing from it. an access the walk places exactly in the frame, off the
# stack pointer's value on entry at an offset it knows, follows the extent
# rule, private or not, and one in the frame at an offset it does not know,
# as through an index, reaches no private extent. one at an offset it knows
# but of a length it does not, as a string store's of a count in a register,
# reaches a private extent only where it starts within it. the obligation is the
# producer's: every access to a private slot is formed from the stack pointer
# by offsets the walk follows, a private slot is never reached through an
# indexed address or by an access of a length the walk does not know that
# starts outside it, and its address is never stored, passed to a call,
# returned or formed where the walk loses its offset. with no private extent
# stated the walk is as it is without the rule.
#
# the producer may state each frame local whose address escapes, its own slot,
# one object: an access whose address an index decides, off a base whose value
# and whose address before the index both lie within one local, lies within
# that local (`anchored`), as an offset off a base stays within its object. a
# local whose type holds no secret is a typed frame extent: no statement types
# any byte of it secret. a pointer to it is of a type stating its storage public, which never
# casts to one stating it secret, so a store a statement types secret never
# reaches it, and a trusted callee handed such a pointer stores no secret
# through it, as its own walk refused that. so a secret at an address the walk
# does not place in the frame, every store of machine code that puts one there
# typed secret (`ct.UNSTATED`), and the writes of a call that trusts its callee
# leave a typed extent holding what it held, the walk's own stores placed in the
# frame still followed. a secret at an address no statement types, and the
# writes of any callee the model does not trust, reach it as any other extent
# from then on. the obligation is the producer's, as for a private extent.
#
# an inline block's access the walk places in the frame reaches only the
# function's own frame below the stack pointer's value on entry, at an offset
# and of a length the walk knows: its address is the block's, which may reach
# past the function's frame into its caller's by stack pointer arithmetic, so
# any other is taken as placed nowhere, what it reads holding a secret and a
# secret stored there refused. the producer states which instructions are an
# inline block's (`Seed.inline`), every one of each block.
#
# secrecy leaves a value only where the caller declares it public, at a
# declassify point: an instruction offset, a side and a place, as the
# trap guard before a division makes its condition public. a point before an
# instruction makes the place public as that instruction reads it, so what
# the instruction decides and writes from it is public, and the state after
# it keeps the place's own secrecy unless the instruction writes it. a point
# after an instruction makes the place it writes hold no secret from there
# until it is written again, memory until a secret may be stored where it is.
# a point on a register row makes public with it the rows lying within it,
# and after a write the rows that write overwrites, as a point after a write
# of eax makes rax public, while a row holding more than it keeps its secret.
# a point is applied each time its instruction is walked, so one inside a
# loop holds on every pass to the fixed point, and one on a path into a join
# reaches the join only on that path, merged there with what the others hold.
# a point never changes a row's class. a point at an offset where no
# instruction the walk reaches starts, or naming a place its instruction does
# not read before it or write after it, is answered unread.
#
# a secret enters only through the seeds, and an instruction may leave one
# that nothing it reads holds, as a call of a callee given nothing secret
# returning a value the producer declares secret, or a load the walk places
# in the frame or off a symbol. a written seed states it, mirroring a point
# after an instruction: an offset and a place the instruction writes, which
# holds a secret each time the walk reaches it, past the row's effect, a
# call's model and any point at the offset, so it overrides what those leave.
# a register taints every row overlapping it as a write does, and memory is
# held as a secret store's. a call writes what the walk holds it may: every
# row but those its model preserves, and every extent its model writes or does
# not keep. a seed at an offset where no instruction the walk reaches starts,
# or naming a place its instruction does not write, is answered unread.
#
# a call is walked through the callee's model its caller states for the call
# site (`Call`), a trusted claim, and with none every register and every
# address is secret after it when anything is before it. the model's join is
# whether its argument registers, the memory it names read or any memory it
# does not keep may hold a secret. the registers it preserves keep what they
# held, the stack pointer what it held before the call instruction, as the
# callee's return undoes what the call pushes, the registers it writes take
# the join, and those it states neither are as with no model. with a secret
# join every byte it does not keep may hold one after it, globals included,
# and so does every extent it writes. a secret reaching the callee through an
# argument register or a read extent the model does not state it accepts, or
# through memory it does not keep and no accepted read holds, refuses the call,
# worded `ct.UNCHECKED`, so a callee not checked constant time accepts none.
# a secret at an address the walk does not place, or in an extent it places
# off a register's value and neither in the frame nor off a symbol, or within
# a secret global (`typed_held`), that every statement of it types secret is
# not one: a store of machine code there is stated secret or
# refused, and a trusted callee's own walk checked its stores so, so it sits
# in storage of a secret type, which any callee reaches through that type
# alone, as it reaches what such storage held before the function began.
# a model may claim its callee reads memory it does not keep only through
# accesses its own walk takes the stated secrecy of (`Call.stated`): a secret
# at any address or in a held extent it neither keeps nor names read then
# joins the call and is accepted, never refused, so a secret join leaves it
# and everything the callee may write secret after the call. its arguments
# and reads join and refuse as any model's. the claim is the producer's, of
# the same proof as acceptance, a callee checked constant time against that
# obligation, and the walk does not check it.
# a tail call ends its path, its target not followed as no call's is, once
# what chooses its callee is checked as any transfer's target is. it is a jump
# whose row states a function as its target, as wasm return_call, or past the
# code's ends, or one a model or a site (`Site.leaves`) states it of, as one
# row of a machine set jumps within a function and out of it. a model at an
# offset where no call or tail call the walk reaches
# starts, or one naming a register the file has no row of, writing one it
# preserves or reading zero, preserving no stack pointer, or accepting what it
# does not name read, or naming a popped value past what its call pops, is
# answered unread.
#
# code of a typed stream passes its values on an operand stack and in the
# entries of its index spaces, as wasm's locals and globals, and nests its
# control in blocks a branch names by depth. the walk first reads such code
# once in its own order, as the stream's readers do, observing each
# instruction on the stream the context holds, which the caller has entered
# into the function the code is the body of. that read resolves through the
# stream's hooks how many values each type of each signature stands for under
# the labels open there, and matches each block's opening with its split and
# its close by the structure the effects state, so a branch to a block goes to
# its close, or a loop's to its start. secrecy is then held per value of the
# operand stack, the bottom first, and per index space entry, and follows the
# signatures and the footprints: a value an instruction pops at a depth its
# effect names is an address, a count of elements, a condition or what chooses
# a target, a branch carries the values its label's type names down to its
# block's height, a block's params pass into it as they are, an entry written
# through an operand takes what is written, and every value an instruction
# pushes takes whether anything it reads is secret. control joins only at one
# height of the stack. a call with no model leaves what it pushes, every entry
# and every address secret when anything is, and a value pushed as the
# polymorphic stack ends the code control reaches there.
#
# a call of a typed stream is modeled as one of machine code is, the same record
# under the same claims, but a stream has no registers: the row's signature
# states what the call pops, so every value of it is an argument the model need
# not name, and one holding a secret joins the call, refusing it worded
# `ct.UNCHECKED` unless the model accepts that position (`Call.accepted_popped`). an
# entry of a space the set states as a function's own (`stream.Hooks.locals`) and
# the stack below what the call pops are out of any callee's reach, so they keep
# what they hold whatever the model says, and what the call pushes takes the
# join. every other entry is memory a callee reaches, as wasm's globals: one
# holding a secret joins the call, refusing it unless the model states its
# callee's reads, and a secret join leaves each secret. the memory of
# a stream is linear and its accesses are placed nowhere, so an extent of a model
# may be off a local's value (`Extent.entry`), standing where a machine extent is
# off a register's. such an extent is known only while the local holds that value:
# a write of the local leaves what was held off it at an address the walk does not
# place, and what a model kept or a point made public off it known no longer, so
# the local needs no version, and a join of two paths holds each path's extents
# off the value the local has on that path.
#
# a catching block's clauses are edges from what raises in its body, a throw or
# a call, whose callee may, to the labels they name. every clause of every
# catching block open around it is reached, out to the first that takes every
# throw: which clause takes a tag is the runtime's, as two imported tags may be
# one, so none is ruled out. each edge cuts the stack to the label's block and
# leaves the clause's values, each secret when anything the raising instruction
# reads is, what it left in the entries and memory going with it. an exception
# held in a value is one value, so one holding a secret is secret whole, and
# what it decides where it is thrown from there is a secret choice of target.

use std.types.bool.bool;
use std.types.bool.false;
use std.types.bool.true;
use std.types.error.err;
use std.types.option.opt;
use std.types.result.res;
use std.types.size.usize;
use std.types.string.str;

use A: std.allocator;
use std.collections.slice.Slice;
use std.collections.vector;
use std.math.bits;

use mink_arch: mink.catalog.arch;
use mink.model.reloc;

use masc.codec;
use masc.core.compress;
use masc.core.config;
use masc.core.constraint;
use masc.core.ct;
use masc.core.dispatch;
use masc.core.effect;
use masc.core.field;
use masc.core.fixup;
use masc.core.footprint;
use masc.core.index;
use masc.core.operand;
use masc.core.quantity;
use masc.core.query;
use masc.core.register;
use masc.core.requirement;
use masc.core.row;
use masc.core.set;
use masc.core.state;
use masc.core.stream;
use mswitch: masc.core.switch;

# a memory extent from a register's value or a symbol's address plus an offset
# ---
# base:      the register holding the address, register.NONE for one off a symbol or an absolute address
# symbol:    the caller's handle of the symbol whose address it is off, as a site names it, operand.NO_SYMBOL for none. an
#            extent names a base or a symbol, never both
# offset:    added to it
# length:    the bytes it covers
# no_global: the producer's claim, trusted as a seed is, that none of its bytes is a global's, as a copy the caller's
#            frame holds of an argument passed by reference, so the walk keeps it apart from every access it places
#            off a symbol. never set on one off a symbol. false keeps the rule that one off a register may alias a global
# entry:     in a call model or a written seed at a call of a typed stream, the local holding the address, as `base`
#            names a register, none for any other. an entry of a space the set states as a function's own, as wasm's
#            locals, named with neither a base nor a symbol
pub rec Extent {
    base:      register.Id;
    symbol:    u32;
    offset:    i64;
    length:    u64;
    no_global: bool;
    entry:     opt[Entry];
}

# the bytes of a global, off a symbol's address
# ---
# symbol: the caller's handle of the symbol, as a site names it, never operand.NO_SYMBOL
# offset: added to its address
# length: the bytes it covers, 0 for a length the caller does not know
pub rec Global {
    symbol: u32;
    offset: i64;
    length: u64;
}

# an entry of one of a typed stream's index spaces, as a wasm function's param is a local
# ---
# space: the set-local index space (`operand.Typed.space`)
# index: the entry's index in it
pub rec Entry {
    space: u16;
    index: u32;
}

# a frame slot: an extent off the value its base register holds where an instruction starts, as a spill slot off sp or
# fp once the prologue has moved them
# ---
# at:     where the instruction starts
# extent: the slot
pub rec Slot {
    at:     u64;
    extent: Extent;
}

# where a secret is when the code starts, or for a frame slot from where its instruction starts, or from where an
# instruction leaves one, or whether one is in what an access reads
# ---
# register: a register's value
# memory:   the bytes of an extent off a register's value on entry, or of an absolute address, never off a symbol or an
#           entry
# entry:    the value of an index space entry of a typed stream
# frame:    the bytes of a frame slot, which hold a secret each time the walk reaches its instruction, before it runs
# symbol:   the bytes of a global, secret for the whole function: a load overlapping them reads a secret, and a store of a
#           public value never makes them public, as no store does
# access:   the secrecy of what one memory access of one instruction reads, which the walk takes in place of the extents
#           it holds when it does not place the access off a symbol or in the frame
# private:  a frame extent no access the walk does not place in the frame reaches, for the whole function, which states
#           no secret of its own
# after:    a place an instruction writes, which holds a secret each time the walk reaches it, once it has run
# within:   the frame range one memory access of one instruction reaches, which the walk places it in
# pointer:  an instruction loading a pointer whose pointee the producer states, which every access off the address it
#           loads takes as an access seed's statement
# fixed:    a register holding no secret at entry, as every function holds it, in which no instruction of the code may
#           leave one, refused worded `ct.FIXED`
# switch:   where an instruction starts that is the code's own switch of the timing mode, the one instruction that may
#           write the state a switch of the set reads or sets, any other refused worded `ct.SWITCHED`
# local:    a frame local whose address escapes, one object, which an access through a pointer into it stays within, and
#           whether its type holds no secret, so a secret every statement types secret and a trusted callee's writes do
#           not reach it
# inline:   where an instruction of an inline block starts, whose accesses the walk places in the frame only below the
#           stack pointer's value on entry, at an offset and of a length it knows
# saved:    bytes of the function's own frame only its frame code writes, a register save's slot, which the epilogue
#           restores the register from
pub tag Seed: u8 {
    register: register.Id;
    memory:   Extent;
    entry:    Entry;
    frame:    Slot;
    symbol:   Global;
    access:   Access;
    private:  Private;
    after:    Written;
    within:   Within;
    pointer:  Pointer;
    fixed:    register.Id;
    switch:   u64;
    local:    Local;
    inline:   u64;
    saved:    Private;
}

# the producer's statement that an instruction loads a pointer of a type that states its pointee's secrecy, as an
# inline block's `mov rax, {s}` loads the value of a `*^u64` local. where the instruction writes one register, which it
# does not read, from the one memory access it makes, every access the walk places off that register's value at any
# offset, and off no symbol and in no frame slot, reads and writes as `secret` states where no access seed decides: a
# store of a secret through it is refused worded `ct.STORED` when it is not. a trusted claim as an access seed is
# ---
# at:     where the instruction starts
# secret: whether what the pointer reaches holds a secret
pub rec Pointer {
    at:     u64;
    secret: bool;
}

# the producer's statement that every byte one memory access of an instruction reaches lies within a range of the
# function's own frame, as each access of a loop a copy or fill of a frame slot was made into reaches the range the
# copy or fill moved, which the walk cannot place from the address an index moves. named off the stack pointer's value
# on entry, as the walk names every frame slot. the walk places the access there in place of its address, known only
# to lie within it (`Held.within`), so a store holds the whole range when it may write a secret and makes none of it
# public, and a load reads what the range holds
# ---
# at:     where the instruction starts
# access: the access
# offset: the range's first byte, added to the stack pointer's value on entry
# length: the bytes of the range, never 0
pub rec Within {
    at:     u64;
    access: Accessor;
    offset: i64;
    length: u64;
}

# the producer's statement that bytes of the function's own frame are private: its own slot whose address never
# escapes, so a pointer from outside the function, a callee or memory the walk does not place never reaches it. named
# off the stack pointer's value on entry, as the walk names every frame slot, so it holds at every instruction however
# the prologue moves sp and fp
# ---
# offset: added to the stack pointer's value on entry, as -24 for a slot 24 bytes below it
# length: the bytes it covers, never 0
pub rec Private {
    offset: i64;
    length: u64;
}

# the producer's statement of a frame local whose address escapes: its own slot, one object, named off the stack
# pointer's value on entry as the walk names every frame slot, and whether the type of what it holds holds no secret,
# which the walk then takes as a typed frame extent
# ---
# offset: added to the stack pointer's value on entry
# length: the bytes it covers, never 0
# public: whether its type holds no secret
pub rec Local {
    offset: i64;
    length: u64;
    public: bool;
}

# which memory access of an instruction an access seed names
# ---
# operand: each access of the operand it is through, by the operand's position: a memory operand, or a register
#          operand an access's address is in, as a register machine's. the position is of the instruction as it was
#          written, so one the builder compressed is named as built, by its base row (`compress.written`), as the
#          listing prints it, and an access seed on `sd`'s base names `c.sdsp`'s sp
# index:   the access by its position in the instruction's footprint (`footprint.Footprint.memory`), for one no operand
#          names, as a wasm load whose address it pops
pub tag Accessor: u8 {
    operand: u8;
    index:   u32;
}

# the producer's statement of what one memory access of an instruction reads, as its secrecy types state a load through
# a pointer. it holds each time the walk reaches its instruction, for an access the walk places off no symbol and in no
# frame slot, the extent rule standing for one it does
# ---
# at:     where the instruction starts
# access: the access
# secret: whether what it reads may hold a secret. what an atomic read-modify-write or compare-exchange returns is what
#         it reads. a store through it of a value that may hold a secret is refused when it is not, worded
#         `ct.STORED`
pub rec Access {
    at:     u64;
    access: Accessor;
    secret: bool;
}

# the producer's statement that an instruction leaves a secret, whatever it reads, as a call of a callee given nothing
# secret returns one, or a load the walk places reads one no extent holds. it mirrors a `Declassify` on side `after`: it
# holds each time the walk reaches the instruction, past the row's effect, a call's model and any declassify point
# there, so it overrides what they leave
# ---
# at:    where the instruction starts
# place: what holds the secret, a place the instruction writes as a point after it names one. a register taints each row
#        overlapping it as a write does. a call writes every register but a program counter and those its model
#        preserves, every extent its model writes or does not keep, and with no model every extent, and in code of a
#        typed stream with no model every entry, and with one every entry but a function's own
pub rec Written {
    at:    u64;
    place: Place;
}

# seeds as a pointer to the caller's rows and a count
pub rec Secrets {
    at:  *Seed;
    len: u32;
}

# what a declassify point makes public
# ---
# register: the value of a register row of the set's file, a row as footprints name it, so x86's zf and not rflags
# memory:   the bytes of an extent, of a known length, off the register an access of the instruction is formed from, or
#           off a symbol an access of it is placed by
# entry:    the value of an index space entry of a typed stream
# value:    a value of a typed stream's operand stack, by depth from its top, 0 the top
# frame:    the bytes of a frame slot off a register's value where the instruction starts, of a known length, which an
#           access of the instruction through any register holds whole once the walk places both
pub tag Place: u8 {
    register: register.Id;
    memory:   Extent;
    entry:    Entry;
    value:    u32;
    frame:    Extent;
}

# which side of its instruction a declassify point is on
# ---
# before: the instruction reads the place as public, which holds what it held after the instruction unless the
#         instruction writes it, as a branch reads a guard's condition
# after:  the instruction writes the place and it holds no secret from there until it is written again, as a compare
#         leaves its result, or a spill the slot it stores
pub tag Side: u8 {
    before;
    after;
}

# where a value becomes public: a declassify point, which removes the secret from one value at one place and never
# makes a row's timing independent of its inputs
# ---
# at:     where the instruction starts
# length: the bytes of the instruction, which the one decoded at `at` must take, so a point never stands on another
#         instruction than its own
# side:   which side of it
# place:  what it makes public, a place the instruction reads for a point before it and writes for one after it. a
#         register after it only where its write keeps no bits above it. the walk does not check that the
#         instruction copies one read, so a point after one computed of several publishes all of them: mirl's
#         selection never fuses a declassify into another operation, which its points rest on
pub rec Declassify {
    at:     u64;
    length: u64;
    side:   Side;
    place:  Place;
}

# declassify points as a pointer to the caller's rows and a count, in any order, more than one at an offset allowed
pub rec Declassified {
    at:  *Declassify;
    len: u32;
}

# no declassify point
pub val NO_DECLASSIFIED: Declassified = Declassified{at: nil, len: 0};

# registers as a pointer to the caller's ids and a count
pub rec Registers {
    at:  *register.Id;
    len: u32;
}

# no register
pub val NO_REGISTERS: Registers = Registers{at: nil, len: 0};

# extents as a pointer to the caller's rows and a count, each off the value its base register or local holds where the
# call starts, as a frame slot off sp or fp, or off no register for an address
pub rec Extents {
    at:  *Extent;
    len: u32;
}

# no extent
pub val NO_EXTENTS: Extents = Extents{at: nil, len: 0};

# what the caller states of the callee of one call site, a trusted claim the walk reads in place of the callee it does
# not see. what it accepts a secret in is sound only of a callee checked constant time in those, or one the toolchain
# proves so, and the walk refuses the call when a secret reaches the callee through anything else. the join of a call
# is whether its arguments, the extents it reads and any memory it does not keep may hold a secret, which is what the
# callee may compute from. a callee that takes a secret buffer through a pointer but no secret length accepts the
# buffer's extent and not the length's register
#
# one record states a call of either form, a form naming only what its code has. machine code passes arguments in
# registers the walk cannot tell from any other, so a model of it names `arguments` and `accepted` and leaves
# `accepted_popped` none. a typed stream has no registers and its signature states what a call passes, so every value
# the call pops is an argument, a model of its code names only those it accepts, and no register in any of its lists.
# every other field means the same of both, its extents off a local where machine extents are off a register
# ---
# at:              where the call starts: a call, or a tail call, a jump whose target the walk does not follow, as it
#                  follows no call's, and after which the path ends. in code of a typed stream a tail call is one its row
#                  states, as return_call
# accepted:        the argument registers the callee is checked to take a secret in, each one `arguments` names, none for
#                  a callee not checked
# accepted_reads:  the extents of `reads` the callee is checked to take a secret in, each one `reads` names, none for a
#                  callee not checked
# accepted_popped: the values of what the call pops the callee is checked to take a secret in, none for a callee not
#                  checked: bit n the value at depth n from the top of what it pops and the last bit every value past
#                  it, as `ct.Inputs` is to name a popped value. what chooses the callee of an indirect call counts,
#                  at depth 0 where it is on top, and a secret there is refused as any target's is. each names a value
#                  the call pops. a callee ignoring a param is modeled by accepting it, a claim of the same proof
# preserved:       the registers holding after the call what they held once the call instruction ran, its link written,
#                  each with the rows lying within it. the stack pointer is one, holding what it held before the call
#                  instruction, as the callee's return undoes what the call pushes. a program counter's row, as x86's rip,
#                  holds what the call instruction left, the return point the walk goes on from. none on a typed stream,
#                  whose locals and lower stack no callee reaches
# arguments:       the registers the callee reads its arguments from
# reads:           the memory the callee may read that the model keeps, as a buffer in the caller's frame a pointer argument
#                  reaches. memory it does not keep is read whatever this names
# stated:          whether the callee reads memory this does not name only through accesses its own walk takes the stated
#                  secrecy of, so a secret it may reach there joins the call and is accepted. a claim of the same proof
#                  as acceptance, the callee checked constant time against that obligation, which the producer states
#                  only with that proof and the walk does not check
# written:         the registers the callee leaves its results in or clobbers, each secret after the call but the rows of
#                  `results`. a register stated neither preserved nor written is secret after the call when anything is
#                  before it, as with no model
# results:         the result pieces the callee's declaration states, each in a register `written` names, NO_RESULTS for a
#                  call of no declared callee. where the call trusts its callee (`stated`), checked to leave them as the
#                  declaration states them, a public piece's register and every row sharing storage with it are public
#                  after the call and a secret piece's secret, a claim of the same proof as acceptance. else each takes
#                  the join
# writes:          the memory the callee may write, which takes the join, the kept memory it writes included
# kept:            the memory the callee leaves as it was but where `writes` names. every other byte may be written with the
#                  join, globals included, a global of a typed stream being every entry of a space that is not a
#                  function's own
# pointed:         the argument registers holding a pointer the callee's declaration states reaches storage holding no
#                  secret, which it reads as public: the frame local such a pointer points into, as `reads` names it,
#                  holds no secret where the call starts, or the call is refused, worded `ct.POINTED`. a claim of the same
#                  proof as acceptance
# keeps:           whether the callee writes no memory, so every byte holds after the call what it held before, `writes`
#                  and `kept` stating none, as the page probe a prologue calls. a claim of the same proof as acceptance
pub rec Call {
    at:              u64;
    accepted:        Registers;
    accepted_reads:  Extents;
    accepted_popped: operand.Positions;
    preserved:       Registers;
    arguments:       Registers;
    reads:           Extents;
    stated:          bool;
    written:         Registers;
    results:         Results;
    writes:          Extents;
    kept:            Extents;
    pointed:         Registers;
    keeps:           bool;
}

# a piece of a result a function's declaration states, left in a register at its return. a public piece's register
# holds no secret in any bit, those past the piece the convention leaves undefined included
# ---
# register: the register it is left in
# secret:   whether the declaration states a secret byte in it
pub rec Result {
    register: register.Id;
    secret:   bool;
}

# result pieces as a pointer to the caller's rows and a count, and the bytes of a result returned by reference the
# declaration states public
# ---
# memory: extents off the register the result's address arrives in, each bytes the declaration states public, which
#         every return and tail call leaves holding no secret the function put there, its own walk taking the register's
#         value on entry, and a call that trusts its callee leaves holding what they held before it, the buffer's
#         bytes the caller passes the address of. NO_EXTENTS for a result returned by value
pub rec Results {
    at:     *Result;
    len:    u32;
    memory: Extents;
}

# no result piece stated, so a call's results take the join and a return is held to nothing
pub val NO_RESULTS: Results = Results{at: nil, len: 0, memory: NO_EXTENTS};

# call models as a pointer to the caller's rows and a count, in any order, one at an offset
pub rec Calls {
    at:  *Call;
    len: u32;
}

# no call model, so every call leaves every register and every address secret when anything is
pub val NO_CALLS: Calls = Calls{at: nil, len: 0};

# a symbolic operand of the code the caller encoded, the fixup its builder left there, which the walk places a
# symbol's address by
# ---
# at:       where its instruction starts
# operand:  the operand it fills, of the instruction as it was written, its base row for one the builder compressed, as
#           an access seed's
# leaves:   of a jump's target, whether its symbol is no label of this code, so the jump is a tail call, whose field the
#           linker has yet to fill. false for a branch to a label of this code left to the linker to relax, whose field
#           holds the distance the builder laid out
# fixup:    the set-local fixup kind
# symbol:   the caller's handle of its symbol. two handles name objects known apart, so a caller resolves a symbol an
#           equate or an alias names to the handle of what it names
# addend:   what the operand adds to the symbol, as `sym+8` states 8, before the builder measures it from where its
#           relocation does
# partner:  for a kind whose relocation names a partner (`reloc.PARTNER`), where the instruction starts whose site's
#           address it takes, as risc-v's pcrel_lo12 names the label of its auipc. 0 for any other
# constant: whether its symbol is code or data the program never writes, as a constant pool's, so no store and no
#           callee reaches it and it holds only what a seed of its own symbol says
pub rec Site {
    at:       u64;
    operand:  u8;
    leaves:   bool;
    fixup:    operand.FixupKind;
    symbol:   u32;
    addend:   i64;
    partner:  u64;
    constant: bool;
}

# sites as a pointer to the caller's rows and a count, in ascending order of offset
pub rec Sites {
    at:  *Site;
    len: u32;
}

# no site, so no address is placed by a symbol
pub val NO_SITES: Sites = Sites{at: nil, len: 0};

# encoded code of one function, the bytes the caller encoded. code of a typed stream is the instructions of the
# function's body, read under a context whose stream the caller has entered into that function
# ---
# set:   the instruction set it is encoded in
# data:  its bytes
# len:   how many
# sites: the fixups the builder left in it, NO_SITES for none
pub rec Code {
    set:   *set.Set;
    data:  *u8;
    len:   usize;
    sites: Sites;
}

# a secret the walk found where constant-time code may hold none
# ---
# offset:  where the instruction that refuses it starts
# refusal: the one refusal record, worded once
pub rec Finding {
    offset:  u64;
    refusal: ct.Refusal;
}

# code the walk could not follow
# ---
# message: why, as bytes no row decodes or a transfer to where no code is
# offset:  where
pub rec Unread {
    message: str;
    offset:  u64;
}

# what the walk finds of a function
# ---
# clear:        no secret reaches what it may not
# refused:      the first secret that does
# unread:       the code cannot be followed, so nothing is decided
# unguaranteed: no secret reaches a control transfer or an address, and the set cannot guarantee any instruction's
#               timing, so no row's latency was asked, which the caller warns of, worded `ct.UNGUARANTEED`, and never
#               refuses
pub tag Verdict: u8 {
    clear;
    refused: Finding;
    unread:  Unread;
    unguaranteed;
}

pub val UNDECODED:    str = "bytes no row decodes under the context";
pub val UNDECIDED:    str = "an instruction whose footprint its values and the configuration in force do not decide";
pub val NOWHERE:      str = "a transfer to where no code is";
pub val INDIRECT:     str = "a jump to a target a register holds, which the walk cannot follow";
pub val UNSEEDABLE:   str = "a seed names a register the set's file has no row of, an entry its stream does not hold, a frame slot at an offset where no instruction the walk reaches starts, an access at one past the code, memory or a slot off a symbol or an entry, a global of no symbol, a private, typed or saved extent of no length or in code with no call frames, an inline seed at one past the code or in code of a typed stream, or a written seed at an offset where no instruction the walk reaches starts or naming a place its instruction does not write";
pub val UNTYPED:      str = "a stack type of a signature the stream does not resolve to a count of values";
pub val UNBALANCED:   str = "a value popped past the bottom of the operand stack or its block's, a popped value named past what the instruction pops, or control joining at two heights of the stack";
pub val UNSTRUCTURED: str = "blocks the code does not close in order, a depth past every block open, or code past its body's block";
pub val TIMED:        str = "code of a typed stream whose set classifies its rows' timing, which no class states over the values a row pops";
pub val MISPLACED:    str = "a declassify point at an offset where no instruction the walk reaches starts, or where one starts of another length than the point states";
pub val UNTOUCHED:    str = "a declassify point naming a place the instruction at its offset does not read before it or write after it, or memory off a symbol it states holds no global's bytes";
pub val UNCALLED:     str = "a call model at an offset where no call or tail call the walk reaches starts, or a second model at one";
pub val UNANCHORED:   str = "a call model whose preserved registers omit the stack pointer";
pub val UNWRITTEN:    str = "a call model naming a register the set's file has no row of, an extent off both a register and a symbol, off a symbol and stated to hold no global's bytes, or off an entry with another base or that is no function's own, or as written one reading zero or sharing storage with one it names preserved";
pub val UNACCEPTED:   str = "a call model accepting a secret in a register it names no argument, or in an extent it names no read";
pub val UNPOPPED:     str = "a call model naming a popped value past what its call pops";
pub val UNACCESSED:   str = "an access seed at an offset within an instruction, or naming a memory access the instruction at its offset does not make";
pub val UNSITED:      str = "a site out of ascending order, at one past the code, at an offset within an instruction, or naming an operand past its instruction's";

# the version of a register's value on entry
val ENTRY: u64 = 0;

# the register file of a set that names no register, as a typed stream's
val NO_FILE: register.File = register.File{
    quantities:     quantity.NO_QUANTITIES,
    bindings:       quantity.NO_BINDINGS,
    slot_count:     0,
    classes:        nil,
    class_count:    0,
    class_names:    index.NO_ENTRIES,
    registers:      nil,
    register_count: 0,
    aliases:        nil,
    alias_count:    0,
    names:          index.NO_ENTRIES,
    columns:        nil,
    column_count:   0,
    lying:          nil,
    lying_first:    nil,
    views:          nil,
    dense:          nil,
    dense_pages:    nil,
    dense_rows:     nil,
};

# an extent that may hold a secret
# ---
# base:    the register row its address is formed from, the stack pointer's for one of a register of a known offset, the
#          index of the local holding it in code of a typed stream, which has no rows, effect.NO_ROW for an address
#          neither forms
# space:   of one off a local, its index space
# version: the version of that register's value, ENTRY for one of a register of a known offset
# symbol:  with base effect.NO_ROW, the symbol whose address it is off, operand.NO_SYMBOL for an address the walk does
#          not place
# slot:    whether it is off the address of the symbol's got slot rather than the symbol's
# offset:  added to it
# length:  the bytes it covers, 0 for a length the walk does not know
# indexed: whether a register decides its offset, as an index or a stride, so it is known only to lie off its base's
#          value, at an offset and of a length the walk does not know, both 0
# apart:   whether it is of an extent stated to hold no global's bytes (`Extent.no_global`), never with a symbol
# within:  of an access a within seed places, whether it is known only to lie within the extent, not to cover it,
#          which no extent held or known public is
rec Held {
    base:    u32;
    space:   u16;
    version: u64;
    symbol:  u32;
    slot:    bool;
    offset:  i64;
    length:  u64;
    indexed: bool;
    apart:   bool;
    within:  bool;
}

# what a register row holds of a symbol's address, as the sites of the instructions writing it place it
# ---
# piece:     fixup.WHOLE for the address, fixup.HIGH for its high part a low part completes, fixup.NO_PIECE for none
# symbol:    the symbol
# offset:    added to its address
# slot:      whether it is of the symbol's got slot rather than the symbol
# partnered: for a high part, whether a low part completes it only by naming its instruction as its partner, as
#            risc-v's pcrel_hi20, else by naming the same symbol and offset, as aarch64's page
# site:      for a high part, where the instruction that formed it starts
rec Formed {
    piece:     fixup.Piece;
    symbol:    u32;
    offset:    i64;
    slot:      bool;
    partnered: bool;
    site:      u64;
}

val UNFORMED: Formed = Formed{piece: fixup.NO_PIECE, symbol: operand.NO_SYMBOL, offset: 0, slot: false, partnered: false, site: 0};

# a register row given a symbol's address or a part of one by the instruction walked
rec Forming {
    row:    u32;
    formed: Formed;
}

# the value a register holds as an offset from one version of a register's value, the stack pointer's on entry among
# them, or as a number of its own
# ---
# known:   whether the walk knows it
# offset:  the offset, or the number, when it does
# number:  whether it is the number `offset`, which no register moves, as a large offset risc-v's lui builds
# root:    the register row the offset is from, when it is not a number
# version: the version of that row's value
rec Frame {
    known:   bool;
    offset:  i64;
    number:  bool;
    root:    u32;
    version: u64;
}

val UNKNOWN: Frame = Frame{known: false, offset: 0, number: false, root: effect.NO_ROW, version: ENTRY};

# whether frame `f` places a register's value off the stack pointer's on entry
fun on_stack(w: *Walk, f: Frame) bool {
    ret f.known && !f.number && f.root == w.stack && f.version == ENTRY;
}

# an extent the walk does not place
val UNPLACED: Held = Held{base: effect.NO_ROW, version: ENTRY, symbol: operand.NO_SYMBOL, slot: false, offset: 0, length: 0, indexed: false, apart: false};

# a register given a known value by the instruction walked
# ---
# row:   its row
# frame: the value
rec Moved {
    row:   u32;
    frame: Frame;
}

# a register the instruction walked writes as a stated function of what it reads, so its secrecy is its inputs' and
# not all the instruction reads
# ---
# row:    its row
# secret: whether any input of its value may hold a secret
rec Derived {
    row:    u32;
    secret: bool;
}

# a register row as it was where a call starts
# ---
# row:     its row
# taint:   whether it may hold a secret
# version: its version
# frame:   its offset from the stack pointer's value on entry
rec Saved {
    row:     u32;
    taint:   bool;
    version: u64;
    frame:   Frame;
}

# what is secret where an instruction starts
# ---
# taint:     the register rows that may hold a secret in some bit, one bit per row, every row overlapping one that does
#            included
# versions:  the version of each register row's value
# frames:    the offset of each register row's value from the stack pointer's on entry
# formed:    what each register row's value holds of a symbol's address
# held:      the extents that may hold a secret, no two of one register's version or one symbol overlapping or meeting
#            where `joins` would make them one
# public:    the extents a declassify point after an instruction made public, or a store of no secret placed exactly in the
#            frame, which hold no secret whatever `held` and `anywhere` say until a secret may be stored there
# anywhere:  whether a secret may be at any address but those `spared` holds
# untyped:   with `anywhere`, whether that secret may be at an address no statement types secret, so a callee whose reads
#            are not stated may reach it through storage its type calls public: not where every store of a secret the
#            walk does not place was stated secret, as each of machine code is, or a trusted callee's, checked so
# untrusted: whether a callee whose model does not trust it may have written memory it reached while a secret may have
#            been there, so what it wrote is typed by no statement and a typed frame extent holds what any other does
# spared:    the extents a call model kept, which hold what `held` and `public` say even when `anywhere` is set, empty
#            unless it is
# config:    the configuration state in force, none when not known
# stack:     a typed stream's operand stack, the bottom first, whether each value may hold a secret
# entries:   the keys of the index space entries that may hold a secret, by `key`, ascending, or with `except` the
#            entries known to hold none
# except:    whether every entry `entries` does not name may hold a secret, as after a call
# pointed:   the register values a pointer seed's statement holds for, each loaded from a slot no inline block's store
#            may have rewritten, or moved from one such by a relation (`carry_pointers`)
# rebound:   the frame extents an inline block's store wrote, whose pointer no longer holds what a binding states of it
# unbound:   whether an inline block's store the walk does not place in the frame, or a call writing memory, may have
#            rewritten any frame slot that is not private
# written:   the frame extents a store of the function's own placed exactly there wrote, whatever it stored, which no
#            store it does not place unwrites
rec Point {
    taint:     vector.Vector[u64];
    versions:  vector.Vector[u64];
    frames:    vector.Vector[Frame];
    formed:    vector.Vector[Formed];
    held:      vector.Vector[Held];
    public:    vector.Vector[Held];
    anywhere:  bool;
    untyped:   bool;
    untrusted: bool;
    spared:    vector.Vector[Held];
    config:    opt[config.State];
    stack:     vector.Vector[bool];
    entries:   vector.Vector[u64];
    except:    bool;
    pointed:   vector.Vector[Pointed];
    rebound:   vector.Vector[Held];
    unbound:   bool;
    written:   vector.Vector[Held];
}

# a memory access of one instruction, placed as the walk names extents
# ---
# reads:   whether it reads
# writes:  whether it writes
# operand: the memory operand whose access it is, field.NO_OPERAND for one an effect states through a pointer or none
# at:      the extent it touches
# row:     the register row its address is formed from, effect.NO_ROW for none
# rebased: what naming it off the stack pointer added to its offset from that row's value, 0 when it is not
# named:   the operand an access seed names it by: the one its footprint states it through, or its memory operand,
#          field.NO_OPERAND for none
# index:   its position in the footprint's accesses, NO_ACCESS for a memory operand the footprint states none of
# seeded:  whether an access seed states what it reads, which the walk takes for one it does not place
# secret:  with `seeded`, whether what it reads may hold a secret
rec Touch {
    reads:   bool;
    writes:  bool;
    operand: u8;
    at:      Held;
    row:     u32;
    rebased: i64;
    named:   u8;
    index:   u32;
    seeded:  bool;
    secret:  bool;
}

# a pointer seed, with the register its instruction loads the pointer into once the walk has read the instruction
# ---
# at:     where the instruction starts
# row:    the register row it writes the pointer into, effect.NO_ROW until the walk reads it, or where it writes other
#         than one register from one access
# secret: whether what the pointer reaches holds a secret
rec Pointing {
    at:     u64;
    row:    u32;
    secret: bool;
}

# a register value a pointer seed's statement holds for under a state
# ---
# row:     the register row
# version: the version of its value the statement is of
# secret:  whether what the pointer reaches holds a secret
rec Pointed {
    row:     u32;
    version: u64;
    secret:  bool;
}

# what the walk's ordered read of a typed stream found of the instruction starting at one offset
# ---
# len:     its bytes
# counts:  where in `Walk.counts` the counts of its signature's types start, its pops' then its pushes', each how many
#          values the type stands for, 0 for the polymorphic stack
# targets: where in `Walk.targets` the blocks its depths name start
# depths:  how many
# block:   the block it opens, splits or closes, NO_BLOCK for none
# catcher: the innermost catching block open around it, NO_BLOCK for none
# stuck:   whether it pushes the polymorphic stack, so control does not go on past it
rec Shape {
    len:     usize;
    counts:  u32;
    targets: u32;
    depths:  u32;
    block:   u32;
    catcher: u32;
    stuck:   bool;
}

# a catch clause of a catching block
# ---
# block:  the block whose label it takes control to
# values: how many values it leaves on that label's stack
rec Clause {
    block:  u32;
    values: u32;
}

# a structured block of a typed stream's code
# ---
# open:    where the instruction opening it starts, NO_OFFSET for the function's body
# body:    where its first instruction starts
# split:   where the instruction splitting it into two arms starts, NO_OFFSET for none
# close:   where the instruction closing it starts, NO_OFFSET while it is open
# base:    the height of the operand stack below its params
# params:  how many values pass into it
# results: how many values it leaves
# loops:   whether its label is its start, else its close
# catcher: the innermost catching block open around what its body holds, itself when it catches, NO_BLOCK for none
# outer:   the innermost catching block open around it, NO_BLOCK for none
# clauses: where in `Walk.clauses` its catch clauses start
# catches: how many
# every:   whether one of them takes every throw, so nothing its body raises goes further out
rec Block {
    open:    usize;
    body:    usize;
    split:   usize;
    close:   usize;
    base:    u32;
    params:  u32;
    results: u32;
    loops:   bool;
    catcher: u32;
    outer:   u32;
    clauses: u32;
    catches: u32;
    every:   bool;
}

# the walk's storage
# ---
# code:     the code walked
# timed:    whether each row's latency is asked, false for a set whose timing is not guaranteed
# ctx:      the context it runs under, which decodes, takes footprints and picks the stack row and architecture
# timing:   the context a row's timing is classified under, ctx itself where the caller assumes no timing promise
# file:     the set's register file, NO_FILE for a set that names no register
# words:    the words a set over the file's rows spans
# stream:   the set's typed stream hooks, nil for a machine set
# locals:   the keys of the entries the function holds of the spaces the hooks state as a function's own, ascending
# points:   the state at each instruction start reached, by index into `states`, NO_POINT for none, THROUGH for one
#           a run falls into, which holds no state of its own
# states:   the states
# queued:   the instruction starts whose state changed and are not walked since, one bit per offset
# low:      no offset below it is queued
# heads:    the instruction start of the run each one THROUGH holds was last walked in
# fell:     the instruction each one THROUGH holds was last fallen into from
# next:     the instruction the instruction walked falls into within its run, NO_OFFSET for none
# pre:      the state where the instruction walked starts, filled only where a seed or declassify point after it reads
#           it
# named:    the rows the operands of the instruction walked name, one bit per row
# touches:  the memory accesses of the instruction walked
# shaped:   what the ordered read found of each instruction start of a typed stream, by index into `shapes`, NO_POINT
#           for none
# shapes:   what it found
# counts:   the counts of the shapes' signatures
# targets:  the blocks the shapes' depths name, by index into `blocks`
# blocks:   the blocks of a typed stream's code, the function's body first
# clauses:  the catch clauses of its catching blocks
# carried:  the values a branch of the instruction walked carries to its label, the deepest first
# popped:   the values the instruction walked pops, the deepest first
# public:   the caller's declassify points
# declared: the first declassify point at each offset, by index into `public`, NO_POINT for none
# chain:    the next declassify point at the offset of each, NO_POINT for none
# overlaps: the rows each row of the file shares storage with
# stack:    the stack pointer's row, effect.NO_ROW for a set whose code has no call frames
# moved:    the registers the instruction walked gives a known offset
# derived:  the registers it writes as a stated function of what it reads, with their inputs' secrecy
# secrets:  the caller's seeds
# sown:     the first frame seed at each offset, by index into `secrets`, NO_POINT for none
# sowing:   the next seed of its kind, frame, access or written, at the offset of each seed, NO_POINT for none
# stated:   the first access seed at each offset, by index into `secrets`, NO_POINT for none
# after:    the first written seed at each offset, by index into `secrets`, NO_POINT for none
# private:  the private extents the seeds state, off the stack pointer's value on entry, those that overlap or meet
#           joined into one, as only which bytes they cover is asked
# objects:  the frame locals the seeds state, each as stated
# typed:    those of them whose type holds no secret, held as the private extents are
# calls:    the caller's call models
# results:  the result pieces the function's declaration states, which every return and tail call leaves as stated
# called:   the call model at each offset, by index into `calls`, NO_POINT for none
# keeping:  the rows the call model of the instruction walked preserves, one bit per row
# writing:  the rows it writes, one bit per row
# kept:     the extents it keeps, placed where the call starts
# accepted: the extents the call model of the instruction walked accepts a secret in, placed where the call starts
# wrote:    the extents it writes, placed there
# returned: of a call's result returned by reference, the bytes its declaration states public that held no secret
#           where the call starts, placed there, which it leaves so
# saved:    the stack pointer's rows as they were where the call starts
# arch:     the architecture the context enters, whose bindings a site's relocation kind is read under, nil for none
# sited:    the first site at each offset, by index into `code.sites`, NO_POINT for none
# forming:  the registers the instruction walked gives a symbol's address or a part of one
# expanded: the set's compressions indexed by shorter row, which a compressed instruction is read as written through
# written:  per operand of the instruction walked as it was written, before compression, the operand of the row decoded
#           it takes its value through, field.NO_OPERAND for none, by which a seed's or a site's operand is read
# at:       where the instruction walked starts
# pointing: the pointer seeds
# fixing:   the rows of registers the seeds state no instruction may leave a secret in, one bit per row
# moding:   the rows of registers holding the state a switch of the set reads, one bit per row
# switches: where the code's own switches of the timing mode start
# inlined:  where the instructions of inline blocks start
# saves:    the frame extents the seeds state only the frame code writes, off the stack pointer's value on entry
# stating:  the pointer statements the instruction walked makes of the registers it writes, taken under the state where
#           it starts
rec Walk {
    a:        *A.Allocator;
    code:     *Code;
    timed:    bool;
    ctx:      *state.Context;
    timing:   *state.Context;
    file:     *register.File;
    words:    usize;
    stream:   *stream.Hooks;
    locals:   vector.Vector[u64];
    points:   vector.Vector[u32];
    states:   vector.Vector[Point];
    queued:   vector.Vector[u64];
    low:      usize;
    heads:    vector.Vector[u32];
    fell:     vector.Vector[usize];
    next:     usize;
    pre:      Point;
    named:    vector.Vector[u64];
    touches:  vector.Vector[Touch];
    shaped:   vector.Vector[u32];
    shapes:   vector.Vector[Shape];
    counts:   vector.Vector[u32];
    targets:  vector.Vector[u32];
    blocks:   vector.Vector[Block];
    clauses:  vector.Vector[Clause];
    carried:  vector.Vector[bool];
    popped:   vector.Vector[bool];
    public:   *Declassified;
    declared: vector.Vector[u32];
    chain:    vector.Vector[u32];
    overlaps: register.Overlaps;
    stack:    u32;
    moved:    vector.Vector[Moved];
    derived:  vector.Vector[Derived];
    secrets:  *Secrets;
    results:  *Results;
    sown:     vector.Vector[u32];
    sowing:   vector.Vector[u32];
    stated:   vector.Vector[u32];
    after:    vector.Vector[u32];
    private:  vector.Vector[Held];
    objects:  vector.Vector[Held];
    typed:    vector.Vector[Held];
    calls:    *Calls;
    called:   vector.Vector[u32];
    keeping:  vector.Vector[u64];
    writing:  vector.Vector[u64];
    kept:     vector.Vector[Held];
    accepted: vector.Vector[Held];
    wrote:    vector.Vector[Held];
    returned: vector.Vector[Held];
    saved:    vector.Vector[Saved];
    arch:     *mink_arch.Arch;
    sited:    vector.Vector[u32];
    forming:  vector.Vector[Forming];
    state:    Point;
    lifted:   Point;
    expanded: compress.Expansions;
    written:  [operand.MAX_OPERANDS]u8;
    at:       usize;
    pointing: vector.Vector[Pointing];
    fixing:   vector.Vector[u64];
    moding:   vector.Vector[u64];
    switches: vector.Vector[u64];
    inlined:  vector.Vector[u64];
    saves:    vector.Vector[Held];
    stating:  vector.Vector[Pointed];
}

val NO_POINT:  u32   = 0xFFFF_FFFF;
val THROUGH:   u32   = 0xFFFF_FFFE;
val NO_BLOCK:  u32   = 0xFFFF_FFFF;
val NO_OFFSET: usize = 0xFFFF_FFFF_FFFF_FFFF;
val NO_ACCESS: u32   = 0xFFFF_FFFF;

fun bit_of(words: *u64, row: u32) bool {
    ret (words[row / 64] & (1::u64 << (row % 64)::u64)) != 0;
}

fun set_bit(words: *u64, row: u32, on: bool) {
    val mask: u64 = 1::u64 << (row % 64)::u64;
    if (on) { words[row / 64] = words[row / 64] | mask; }
    or      { words[row / 64] = words[row / 64] & ~mask; }
}

fun failed[T](e: A.Error) res[T, A.Error] {
    ret res[T, A.Error].err{e};
}

# the key of entry `index` of space `space`, in the order the keys of a point's entries keep
fun key(space: u16, index: u32) u64 {
    ret (space::u64 << 32) | index::u64;
}

# where `k` is in the ascending `keys`, or where it would go
# ---
# held: whether it is there
# at:   its position, or the position it would take
rec Found {
    held: bool;
    at:   usize;
}

fun find_key(keys: *vector.Vector[u64], k: u64) Found {
    var lo: usize = 0;
    var hi: usize = keys.len;
    for (lo < hi) {
        val mid: usize = lo + (hi - lo) / 2;
        if (keys.data[mid] < k) { lo = mid + 1; }
        or                      { hi = mid; }
    }
    ret Found{held: lo < keys.len && keys.data[lo] == k, at: lo};
}

# `k` added to the ascending `keys` unless they hold it
fun insert_key(keys: *vector.Vector[u64], k: u64) err[A.Error] {
    val f: Found = find_key(keys, k);
    if (f.held) { ret err[A.Error].ok{}; }
    val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u64](keys, k);
    if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
    var i: usize = keys.len - 1;
    for (i > f.at) {
        keys.data[i] = keys.data[i - 1];
        i            = i - 1;
    }
    keys.data[f.at] = k;
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# `k` taken out of the ascending `keys` when they hold it
fun remove_key(keys: *vector.Vector[u64], k: u64) {
    val f: Found = find_key(keys, k);
    if (!f.held) { ret; }
    var i: usize = f.at;
    for (i + 1 < keys.len) {
        keys.data[i] = keys.data[i + 1];
        i            = i + 1;
    }
    vector.truncate[u64](keys, keys.len - 1);
}

# whether entry `k` may hold a secret under `p`
fun entry_secret(p: *Point, k: u64) bool {
    ret find_key(?p.entries, k).held != p.except;
}

# entry `k` made to hold a secret under `p` or none
fun set_entry(p: *Point, k: u64, secret: bool) err[A.Error] {
    if (secret != p.except) { ret insert_key(?p.entries, k); }
    remove_key(?p.entries, k);
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# whether some entry may hold a secret under `p`
fun any_entry(p: *Point) bool {
    ret p.except || p.entries.len > 0;
}

# whether entry `k` is the function's own, so no callee reaches it
fun is_local(w: *Walk, k: u64) bool {
    ret find_key(?w.locals, k).held;
}

# whether an entry a callee reaches may hold a secret under `p`
fun shared_entry(w: *Walk, p: *Point) bool {
    if (p.except) { ret true; }
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < p.entries.len) {
        if (!is_local(w, p.entries.data[i])) { ret true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# every entry a callee reaches made to hold a secret under `p`, the function's own holding what they held
fun share_entries(w: *Walk, p: *Point) err[A.Error] {
    var known: vector.Vector[u64] = vector.init[u64](w.a);
    var i:     usize              = 0;
    for (i < w.locals.len) {
        if (!entry_secret(p, w.locals.data[i])) {
            val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u64](?known, w.locals.data[i]);
            if (sel pushed.err) {
                vector.dnit[u64](?known);
                ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err};
            }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    vector.dnit[u64](?p.entries);
    p.entries = known;
    p.except  = true;
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# a point holding nothing, its lists empty
fun empty(a: *A.Allocator) Point {
    ret Point{
        taint:     vector.init[u64](a),
        versions:  vector.init[u64](a),
        frames:    vector.init[Frame](a),
        formed:    vector.init[Formed](a),
        held:      vector.init[Held](a),
        public:    vector.init[Held](a),
        anywhere:  false,
        untyped:   false,
        untrusted: false,
        spared:    vector.init[Held](a),
        config:    opt[config.State].none{},
        stack:     vector.init[bool](a),
        entries:   vector.init[u64](a),
        except:    false,
        pointed:   vector.init[Pointed](a),
        rebound:   vector.init[Held](a),
        written:   vector.init[Held](a),
        unbound:   false,
    };
}

# room in a point for `words` taint words and `count` registers
fun sized(p: *Point, words: usize, count: usize) err[A.Error] {
    val taint: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.reserve[u64](?p.taint, words);
    if (sel taint.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{taint.err}; }
    val versions: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.reserve[u64](?p.versions, count);
    if (sel versions.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{versions.err}; }
    val frames: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.reserve[Frame](?p.frames, count);
    if (sel frames.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{frames.err}; }
    val formed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.reserve[Formed](?p.formed, count);
    if (sel formed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{formed.err}; }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# a point of `w`'s file holding nothing secret, every register at its entry version and the operand stack empty
fun blank(w: *Walk) res[Point, A.Error] {
    var p:     Point        = empty(w.a);
    val count: usize        = w.file.register_count::usize;
    val room:  err[A.Error] = sized(?p, w.words, count);
    if (sel room.err) {
        drop(?p);
        ret failed[Point](room.err);
    }
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < w.words) {
        vector.push[u64](?p.taint, 0);
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < count) {
        vector.push[u64](?p.versions, ENTRY);
        var f: Frame = UNKNOWN;
        if (i == w.stack::usize) { f = Frame{known: true, offset: 0, number: false, root: w.stack, version: ENTRY}; }
        vector.push[Frame](?p.frames, f);
        vector.push[Formed](?p.formed, UNFORMED);
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret res[Point, A.Error].ok{p};
}

fun drop(p: *Point) {
    vector.dnit[u64](?p.taint);
    vector.dnit[u64](?p.versions);
    vector.dnit[Frame](?p.frames);
    vector.dnit[Formed](?p.formed);
    vector.dnit[Held](?p.held);
    vector.dnit[Held](?p.public);
    vector.dnit[Held](?p.spared);
    vector.dnit[bool](?p.stack);
    vector.dnit[u64](?p.entries);
    vector.dnit[Pointed](?p.pointed);
    vector.dnit[Held](?p.rebound);
    vector.dnit[Held](?p.written);
}

fun listed[T](v: *vector.Vector[T]) Slice[T] {
    ret Slice[T]{data: v.data, size: v.len};
}

fun refill[T](into: *vector.Vector[T], from: *vector.Vector[T]) err[A.Error] {
    vector.truncate[T](into, 0);
    val put: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.extend[T](into, listed[T](from));
    if (sel put.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{put.err}; }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# `into` made the same as `from`, its lists' storage reused
fun assign(into: *Point, from: *Point) err[A.Error] {
    into.anywhere  = from.anywhere;
    into.untyped   = from.untyped;
    into.untrusted = from.untrusted;
    into.config    = from.config;
    into.except    = from.except;
    into.unbound   = from.unbound;
    val taint: err[A.Error] = refill[u64](?into.taint, ?from.taint);
    if (sel taint.err) { ret taint; }
    val versions: err[A.Error] = refill[u64](?into.versions, ?from.versions);
    if (sel versions.err) { ret versions; }
    val frames: err[A.Error] = refill[Frame](?into.frames, ?from.frames);
    if (sel frames.err) { ret frames; }
    val formed: err[A.Error] = refill[Formed](?into.formed, ?from.formed);
    if (sel formed.err) { ret formed; }
    val held: err[A.Error] = refill[Held](?into.held, ?from.held);
    if (sel held.err) { ret held; }
    val public: err[A.Error] = refill[Held](?into.public, ?from.public);
    if (sel public.err) { ret public; }
    val spared: err[A.Error] = refill[Held](?into.spared, ?from.spared);
    if (sel spared.err) { ret spared; }
    val stack: err[A.Error] = refill[bool](?into.stack, ?from.stack);
    if (sel stack.err) { ret stack; }
    val pointed: err[A.Error] = refill[Pointed](?into.pointed, ?from.pointed);
    if (sel pointed.err) { ret pointed; }
    val rebound: err[A.Error] = refill[Held](?into.rebound, ?from.rebound);
    if (sel rebound.err) { ret rebound; }
    val written: err[A.Error] = refill[Held](?into.written, ?from.written);
    if (sel written.err) { ret written; }
    ret refill[u64](?into.entries, ?from.entries);
}

# a copy of `from`
fun copy(w: *Walk, from: *Point) res[Point, A.Error] {
    var p:    Point        = empty(w.a);
    val done: err[A.Error] = assign(?p, from);
    if (sel done.err) {
        drop(?p);
        ret failed[Point](done.err);
    }
    ret res[Point, A.Error].ok{p};
}

fun same(x: *Held, y: *Held) bool {
    ret x.base == y.base && x.space == y.space && x.version == y.version && x.symbol == y.symbol && x.slot == y.slot && x.offset == y.offset && x.length == y.length && x.indexed == y.indexed && x.apart == y.apart && x.within == y.within;
}

# whether a site of the code walked names `symbol` as one the program never writes (`Site.constant`)
fun constant_symbol(w: *Walk, symbol: u32) bool {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < w.code.sites.len) {
        val st: *Site = ?w.code.sites.at[i];
        if (st.symbol == symbol && st.constant) { ret true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# whether `h` is off a symbol's address
fun symbolic(h: *Held) bool {
    ret h.base == effect.NO_ROW && h.symbol != operand.NO_SYMBOL;
}

# whether the walk places `h` in the frame, off the stack pointer's value on entry
fun in_frame(w: *Walk, h: *Held) bool {
    ret w.stack != effect.NO_ROW && h.base == w.stack && h.version == ENTRY;
}

# whether the walk places `h`: off a register's value or a symbol's address
fun located(h: *Held) bool {
    ret h.base != effect.NO_ROW || h.symbol != operand.NO_SYMBOL;
}

# whether the walk places every byte of `h` at an offset and of a length it knows off one register's value, so a store
# there leaves exactly those bytes holding what it wrote. an extent off a symbol is not, as a global's seed holds for the
# whole function, and nor is one an access is known only to lie within
fun exact(h: *Held) bool {
    ret h.base != effect.NO_ROW && h.symbol == operand.NO_SYMBOL && !h.indexed && !h.within && h.length != 0;
}

# `h` added to what `p` holds, as `holds` adds it
fun hold(w: *Walk, p: *Point, h: Held) err[A.Error] {
    val res_held: res[bool, A.Error] = holds(w, p, h);
    if (sel res_held.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{res_held.err}; }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# `h` added to what `p` holds unless an extent it holds already holds every byte of it, and joined into one it
# overlaps or meets of the same register's version or symbol, which together hold exactly the bytes the two did, so a
# run of stores holds one extent and not one per store. one an access is known only to lie within is held whole
# ---
# ret: whether what `p` holds changed
fun holds(w: *Walk, p: *Point, given: Held) res[bool, A.Error] {
    var h: Held = given;
    h.within = false;
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < p.held.len) {
        val g: *Held = ?p.held.data[i];
        if (same(g, ?h) || (g.apart == h.apart && inside(?h, g))) { ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{false}; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < p.held.len) {
        if (joins(w, ?p.held.data[i], ?h)) {
            widen(?p.held.data[i], ?h);
            absorb(w, ?p.held, i, true);
            ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{true};
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Held](?p.held, h);
    if (sel pushed.err) { ret failed[bool](pushed.err); }
    ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{true};
}

# whether `g` and `h` join into one extent holding exactly their bytes: both placed off one register's version or one
# symbol at offsets and of lengths the walk knows, overlapping or meeting, alike in every other respect, and alike in
# lying within the private extents or not, so whatever is asked of the one is asked of both bytes alike
fun joins(w: *Walk, g: *Held, h: *Held) bool {
    if (!meets(g, h))       { ret false; }
    if (w.private.len == 0) { ret true; }
    val private: bool = is_private(w, g);
    if (private != is_private(w, h)) { ret false; }
    if (!private)                    { ret true; }
    var u: Held = @g;
    widen(?u, h);
    ret is_private(w, ?u);
}

# whether `g` and `h` are placed off one register's version or one symbol at offsets and of lengths the walk knows,
# overlap or meet, and are alike in every other respect, so one extent holds exactly the bytes of both
fun meets(g: *Held, h: *Held) bool {
    if (!located(g) || g.indexed || h.indexed || g.length == 0 || h.length == 0) { ret false; }
    if (g.base != h.base || g.space != h.space || g.version != h.version)        { ret false; }
    if (g.symbol != h.symbol || g.slot != h.slot || g.apart != h.apart)          { ret false; }
    ret g.offset <= h.offset + h.length::i64 && h.offset <= g.offset + g.length::i64;
}

# `h` added to the extents of `v` whose bytes alone matter, joined into one it meets
fun gather(v: *vector.Vector[Held], h: Held) err[A.Error] {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < v.len) {
        if (meets(?v.data[i], ?h)) {
            widen(?v.data[i], ?h);
            absorb(nil, v, i, false);
            ret err[A.Error].ok{};
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    val res_pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Held](v, h);
    if (sel res_pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{res_pushed.err}; }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# `g` grown to hold every byte of `h` as well, the two overlapping or meeting
fun widen(g: *Held, h: *Held) {
    var start: i64 = g.offset;
    var end:   i64 = g.offset + g.length::i64;
    if (h.offset < start)               { start = h.offset; }
    if (h.offset + h.length::i64 > end) { end = h.offset + h.length::i64; }
    g.offset = start;
    g.length = (end - start)::u64;
}

# every other extent of `v` that the one at `at` now overlaps or meets joined into it, as `joins` joins held extents
# where `held`, else as `meets` does
fun absorb(w: *Walk, v: *vector.Vector[Held], at: usize, held: bool) {
    var into: usize = at;
    var j:    usize = 0;
    for (j < v.len) {
        var one: bool = false;
        if (j != into) {
            if (held) { one = joins(w, ?v.data[into], ?v.data[j]); }
            or        { one = meets(?v.data[into], ?v.data[j]); }
        }
        if (one) {
            widen(?v.data[into], ?v.data[j]);
            val last: usize = v.len - 1;
            v.data[j] = v.data[last];
            if (into == last) { into = j; }
            vector.truncate[Held](v, last);
            j = 0;
        }
        or { j = j + 1; }
    }
}

# whether `held` and `at` may share a byte: only extents of one version of one register, or off one symbol, both of
# known offset and length, are known apart, when they do not overlap, and extents off two symbols or a symbol and its
# got slot always are, as are one off a symbol and one in the frame or stated to hold no global's bytes
fun may_alias(w: *Walk, held: *Held, at: *Held) bool {
    if (symbolic(held) && (at.apart || in_frame(w, at)))   { ret false; }
    if (symbolic(at) && (held.apart || in_frame(w, held))) { ret false; }
    if (symbolic(held) && symbolic(at)) {
        if (held.symbol != at.symbol || held.slot != at.slot)                 { ret false; }
        if (held.indexed || at.indexed || held.length == 0 || at.length == 0) { ret true; }
        ret held.offset < at.offset + at.length::i64 && at.offset < held.offset + held.length::i64;
    }
    if (held.base != at.base || held.space != at.space || held.version != at.version || held.base == effect.NO_ROW) { ret true; }
    if (held.indexed || at.indexed || held.length == 0 || at.length == 0)                                           { ret true; }
    ret held.offset < at.offset + at.length::i64 && at.offset < held.offset + held.length::i64;
}

# whether every byte of `inner` is one of `outer`: both of one version of one register, or off one symbol, and of known
# offset and length
fun inside(inner: *Held, outer: *Held) bool {
    if (inner.indexed || outer.indexed) { ret false; }
    if (symbolic(inner) || symbolic(outer)) {
        if (!symbolic(inner) || !symbolic(outer) || inner.symbol != outer.symbol || inner.slot != outer.slot) { ret false; }
        if (inner.length == 0 || outer.length == 0)                                                           { ret false; }
        ret inner.offset >= outer.offset && inner.offset + inner.length::i64 <= outer.offset + outer.length::i64;
    }
    if (inner.base != outer.base || inner.space != outer.space || inner.version != outer.version || inner.base == effect.NO_ROW) { ret false; }
    if (inner.length == 0 || outer.length == 0)                                                                                  { ret false; }
    ret inner.offset >= outer.offset && inner.offset + inner.length::i64 <= outer.offset + outer.length::i64;
}

# `h` known only to lie off its base's value, as a register deciding its offset leaves it, unless it is placed nowhere
fun off_unknown(h: *Held) {
    if (!located(h)) { ret; }
    h.indexed = true;
    h.offset  = 0;
    h.length  = 0;
}

# the extents `p` knows public taken out where a secret stored at `at` may reach them, every one for an address the walk
# does not place but a private one
fun unpublish(w: *Walk, p: *Point, at: *Held) {
    var kept: usize = 0;
    var i:    usize = 0;
    for (i < p.public.len) {
        if ((located(at) && !may_alias(w, ?p.public.data[i], at)) || privately_apart(w, ?p.public.data[i], at)) {
            p.public.data[kept] = p.public.data[i];
            kept                = kept + 1;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    vector.truncate[Held](?p.public, kept);
}

# whether every byte of `at` is one of an extent a call model kept under `p`
fun is_spared(p: *Point, at: *Held) bool {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < p.spared.len) {
        if (inside(at, ?p.spared.data[i])) { ret true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# whether every byte of `at` is one of a private extent of `w`, so no access the walk does not place exactly in the
# frame reaches it. the bytes may lie across several, as a load of a pair reads two adjacent save slots
fun is_private(w: *Walk, at: *Held) bool {
    ret covered(at, ?w.private);
}

# whether every byte of `at` is one of an extent of `of`, the bytes possibly across several
fun covered(at: *Held, of: *vector.Vector[Held]) bool {
    if (of.len == 0 || at.length == 0) { ret false; }
    var from: i64   = at.offset;
    val end:  i64   = at.offset + at.length::i64;
    var i:    usize = 0;
    for (i < of.len) {
        val rest: Held  = Held{base: at.base, space: at.space, version: at.version, symbol: at.symbol, slot: at.slot, offset: from, length: (end - from)::u64, indexed: at.indexed, apart: at.apart};
        val p:    *Held = ?of.data[i];
        if (inside(?rest, p)) { ret true; }
        var first: Held = rest;
        first.length = 1;
        if (inside(?first, p)) {
            from = p.offset + p.length::i64;
            i    = 0;
        }
        or { i = i + 1; }
    }
    ret false;
}

# whether the walk places `h` in the frame where it may reach `slot`: off the stack pointer's value on entry at an
# offset it knows, of a length it knows or of one it does not starting within `slot`
fun framed(w: *Walk, h: *Held, slot: *Held) bool {
    if (w.stack == effect.NO_ROW || h.base != w.stack || h.version != ENTRY || h.indexed) { ret false; }
    if (h.length != 0)                                                                    { ret true; }
    var first: Held = @h;
    first.length = 1;
    ret inside(?first, slot);
}

# whether `x` and `y` are known apart by a private extent: one lies within one and the walk does not place the other
# in the frame where it may reach it, so whatever else may alias the two may not
fun privately_apart(w: *Walk, x: *Held, y: *Held) bool {
    if (w.private.len == 0) { ret false; }
    ret (is_private(w, x) && !framed(w, y, x)) || (is_private(w, y) && !framed(w, x, y));
}

# whether every byte of `at` is one of a typed frame extent of `w` that holds what its statement says under `p`: no
# secret at an address the walk does not place is typed by no statement, and no callee it does not trust may have
# written it since a secret could be there. a secret every statement types secret sits in storage of a secret type,
# which no pointer to a typed extent's storage reaches, as `*T` never casts to `*^T`, and a trusted callee's own walk
# refused a secret stored through a pointer its type states public, so neither reaches the extent
fun is_typed(w: *Walk, p: *Point, at: *Held) bool {
    if (w.typed.len == 0 || p.untyped || p.untrusted) { ret false; }
    ret covered(at, ?w.typed);
}

# whether held extent `held` holds none of the bytes of `at` by the typed frame extents: `at` lies within them and the
# walk does not place `held` in the frame, so in machine code a secret every statement types secret was stored there,
# or a trusted callee's write put it there, neither of which reaches a typed extent. one it places in the frame is the
# walk's own and holds what it holds
fun typed_apart(w: *Walk, p: *Point, held: *Held, at: *Held) bool {
    ret !in_frame(w, held) && is_typed(w, p, at);
}

# whether held extent `h` is storage a statement types secret under `p`, in machine code: off a symbol within a global
# a symbol seed states secret, or placed off a register's value and not in the frame. a store of the function's own put
# a secret there only where its access was stated secret, and a trusted callee's or a seed's only where the declaration
# types it so. what a callee it does not trust writes there is anywhere untyped where the walk cannot place it so
# (`modeled`). any callee reaches such storage only through the types that state it, which sema holds a callee it does
# not trust to (a secret type is never passed to one, and no function branches, indexes or divides on a secret), so a
# secret there does not refuse its call, as one in storage of a secret type before the function began does not. the
# frame is never such storage, as a spill or a slot no seed states holds what no type states
fun typed_held(w: *Walk, p: *Point, h: *Held) bool {
    if (w.stream != nil || p.untyped || !located(h)) { ret false; }
    if (symbolic(h))                                 { ret secret_global(w, h); }
    ret !in_frame(w, h);
}

# whether memory under `p` may hold a secret a callee may read: at any address, or in a held extent that is neither
# private nor storage a statement types secret, which a callee reaches only through its secret type (`typed_held`)
fun memory_secret(w: *Walk, p: *Point) bool {
    if (p.anywhere) { ret true; }
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < p.held.len) {
        if (!is_private(w, ?p.held.data[i]) && !typed_held(w, p, ?p.held.data[i])) { ret true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# the extents `p` knows public kept only where they are private, as a secret made possible at every address the walk
# does not place in the frame leaves them
fun keep_private(w: *Walk, p: *Point) {
    var kept: usize = 0;
    var i:    usize = 0;
    for (i < p.public.len) {
        if (is_private(w, ?p.public.data[i])) {
            p.public.data[kept] = p.public.data[i];
            kept                = kept + 1;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    vector.truncate[Held](?p.public, kept);
}

# a secret made possible at any address in `p`, none spared, at one no statement types secret
fun everywhere(p: *Point) {
    p.anywhere = true;
    p.untyped  = true;
    vector.truncate[Held](?p.spared, 0);
}

# a secret made possible at any address in `p`, none spared, by a store a statement types secret or by a trusted
# callee, whose own walk checked its stores so. code of a typed stream states no store, so there it may be at any
fun everywhere_typed(w: *Walk, p: *Point) {
    p.anywhere = true;
    if (w.stream != nil) { p.untyped = true; }
    vector.truncate[Held](?p.spared, 0);
}

# whether `h` is off the value of entry `k`, or of any entry for none
fun off_entry(h: *Held, k: opt[u64]) bool {
    if (h.base == effect.NO_ROW) { ret false; }
    if (sel k.none)              { ret true; }
    ret key(h.space, h.base) == k.some;
}

# the extents of `v` not off the value of entry `k`, whose order they keep
# ---
# ret: whether one was
fun drop_off(v: *vector.Vector[Held], k: opt[u64]) bool {
    var left: usize = 0;
    var i:    usize = 0;
    for (i < v.len) {
        if (!off_entry(?v.data[i], k)) {
            v.data[left] = v.data[i];
            left         = left + 1;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    val dropped: bool = left != v.len;
    vector.truncate[Held](v, left);
    ret dropped;
}

# entry `k` given a new value under `p`, or any entry for none, so nothing is known any longer off the one it held: what
# was held off it is at an address the walk does not place, and what was kept or made public off it is known no longer
fun rewritten(p: *Point, k: opt[u64]) {
    val publics: bool = drop_off(?p.public, k);
    val spared:  bool = drop_off(?p.spared, k);
    if (drop_off(?p.held, k)) { everywhere(p); }
}

# the extents `spared` holds narrowed to the bytes `by` holds as well: each of either lying within one of the other,
# so what both spare and no more
# ---
# ret: whether `spared` changed
fun narrow(w: *Walk, spared: *vector.Vector[Held], by: *vector.Vector[Held]) res[bool, A.Error] {
    var kept: vector.Vector[Held] = vector.init[Held](w.a);
    var i:    usize               = 0;
    for (i < spared.len) {
        var k: usize = 0;
        for (k < by.len) {
            if (inside(?spared.data[i], ?by.data[k])) {
                val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Held](?kept, spared.data[i]);
                if (sel pushed.err) {
                    vector.dnit[Held](?kept);
                    ret failed[bool](pushed.err);
                }
                k = by.len;
            }
            or { k = k + 1; }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < by.len) {
        var within: bool  = false;
        var held:   bool  = false;
        var k:      usize = 0;
        for (k < spared.len) {
            if (inside(?by.data[i], ?spared.data[k])) { within = true; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        k = 0;
        for (k < kept.len) {
            if (same(?by.data[i], ?kept.data[k])) { held = true; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        if (within && !held) {
            val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Held](?kept, by.data[i]);
            if (sel pushed.err) {
                vector.dnit[Held](?kept);
                ret failed[bool](pushed.err);
            }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    var changed: bool = kept.len != spared.len;
    i = 0;
    for (i < kept.len && !changed) {
        var k:     usize = 0;
        var found: bool  = false;
        for (k < spared.len) {
            if (same(?kept.data[i], ?spared.data[k])) { found = true; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        if (!found) { changed = true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    vector.dnit[Held](spared);
    @spared = kept;
    ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{changed};
}

# whether the bytes of `at` may hold a secret under `p`. a private extent holds none a secret at any address puts there,
# an extent the walk does not place in the frame none a private one holds, a typed one none a secret every statement
# types secret puts at an address the walk does not place in the frame (`typed_apart`), and data the program never
# writes none but what a seed of its own symbol holds, a symbol's got slot, which the loader alone writes, among them
fun secret_at(w: *Walk, p: *Point, at: *Held) bool {
    if (made_public(p, at)) { ret false; }
    if (symbolic(at) && (at.slot || constant_symbol(w, at.symbol))) {
        var k: usize = 0;
        for (k < p.held.len) {
            if (symbolic(?p.held.data[k]) && may_alias(w, ?p.held.data[k], at)) { ret true; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        ret false;
    }
    if (p.anywhere && !is_spared(p, at) && !is_private(w, at) && !is_typed(w, p, at)) { ret true; }
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < p.held.len) {
        if (may_alias(w, ?p.held.data[i], at) && !privately_apart(w, ?p.held.data[i], at) && !typed_apart(w, p, ?p.held.data[i], at)) { ret true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# the entries of `from` merged into `into`'s, so the entries either may hold a secret in may in the join
# ---
# ret: whether `into`'s changed
fun merge_entries(w: *Walk, into: *Point, from: *Point) res[bool, A.Error] {
    var changed: bool  = false;
    var i:       usize = 0;
    if (!from.except) {
        # what from holds secret is secret in the join: added to into's secrets, or taken from what into knows public
        for (i < from.entries.len) {
            val k:      u64  = from.entries.data[i];
            val before: bool = entry_secret(into, k);
            if (!before) {
                val set: err[A.Error] = set_entry(into, k, true);
                if (sel set.err) { ret failed[bool](set.err); }
                changed = true;
            }
            i = i + 1;
        }
        ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{changed};
    }
    # from holds every entry secret but those it knows public, so the join knows public only what both do
    var kept: vector.Vector[u64] = vector.init[u64](w.a);
    for (i < from.entries.len) {
        val k: u64 = from.entries.data[i];
        if (!entry_secret(into, k)) {
            val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u64](?kept, k);
            if (sel pushed.err) {
                vector.dnit[u64](?kept);
                ret failed[bool](pushed.err);
            }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    changed = !into.except || kept.len != into.entries.len;
    vector.dnit[u64](?into.entries);
    into.entries = kept;
    into.except  = true;
    ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{changed};
}

# `from`, reaching the point at `to` from the instruction at `pred`, merged into it: `to`'s join is the version of a
# register the two disagree on, a register's offset the two disagree on is known no longer, and an extent `from` holds
# off a version the code back to `to` makes again is held known only to lie off that version's value (`renewed`)
# ---
# ret: whether the point at `to` changed, none when the two hold operand stacks of different heights
# the frame bytes written on both paths into `into.written`: each byte both lists cover, whether it changed
fun written_both(w: *Walk, into: *Point, from: *Point) res[bool, A.Error] {
    var both: vector.Vector[Held] = vector.init[Held](w.a);
    fin { vector.dnit[Held](?both); }
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < into.written.len) {
        val x: Held  = into.written.data[i];
        var k: usize = 0;
        for (k < from.written.len) {
            val y:     Held = from.written.data[k];
            var start: i64  = x.offset;
            var end:   i64  = x.offset + x.length::i64;
            if (y.offset > start)               { start = y.offset; }
            if (y.offset + y.length::i64 < end) { end = y.offset + y.length::i64; }
            if (end > start) {
                var piece: Held = x;
                piece.offset = start;
                piece.length = (end - start)::u64;
                val err_both: err[A.Error] = gather(?both, piece);
                if (sel err_both.err) { ret failed[bool](err_both.err); }
            }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    var same_all: bool = both.len == into.written.len;
    i = 0;
    for (same_all && i < both.len) {
        if (!covered(?into.written.data[i], ?both)) { same_all = false; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    if (same_all) { ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{false}; }
    val err_refilled: err[A.Error] = refill[Held](?into.written, ?both);
    if (sel err_refilled.err) { ret failed[bool](err_refilled.err); }
    ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{true};
}

fun merge(w: *Walk, into: *Point, from: *Point, pred: usize, to: usize) res[opt[bool], A.Error] {
    if (into.stack.len != from.stack.len) { ret res[opt[bool], A.Error].ok{opt[bool].none{}}; }
    var changed: bool  = false;
    var i:       usize = 0;
    for (i < w.words) {
        val both: u64 = into.taint.data[i] | from.taint.data[i];
        if (both != into.taint.data[i]) { changed = true; }
        into.taint.data[i] = both;
        i                  = i + 1;
    }
    val joined: u64 = to::u64 * 2 + 2;
    i = 0;
    for (i < into.versions.len) {
        if (into.versions.data[i] != from.versions.data[i] && into.versions.data[i] != joined) {
            into.versions.data[i] = joined;
            changed               = true;
        }
        val f:     *Frame = ?into.frames.data[i];
        val other: Frame  = from.frames.data[i];
        if (f.known && (!other.known || other.offset != f.offset || other.number != f.number || other.root != f.root || other.version != f.version)) {
            @f      = UNKNOWN;
            changed = true;
        }
        val fo: *Formed = ?into.formed.data[i];
        if (fo.piece != fixup.NO_PIECE && !same_form(fo, ?from.formed.data[i])) {
            @fo     = UNFORMED;
            changed = true;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < from.held.len) {
        var h: Held = from.held.data[i];
        if (renewed(h.version, pred, to)) { off_unknown(?h); }
        val res_held: res[bool, A.Error] = holds(w, into, h);
        if (sel res_held.err) { ret failed[opt[bool]](res_held.err); }
        if (res_held.ok)      { changed = true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    # a byte is known public in the join only when it is on both paths: an extent of either whose every byte the other
    # knows public, however the two paths' stores cut the bytes, as a frame byte nothing public covers reads as unwritten
    var publics: vector.Vector[Held] = vector.init[Held](w.a);
    fin { vector.dnit[Held](?publics); }
    val res_both: err[A.Error] = refill[Held](?publics, ?into.public);
    if (sel res_both.err) { ret failed[opt[bool]](res_both.err); }
    var kept: usize = 0;
    i = 0;
    for (i < into.public.len) {
        if (covered(?into.public.data[i], ?from.public)) {
            into.public.data[kept] = into.public.data[i];
            kept                   = kept + 1;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    if (kept != into.public.len) {
        vector.truncate[Held](?into.public, kept);
        changed = true;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < from.public.len) {
        val h: *Held = ?from.public.data[i];
        if (covered(h, ?publics) && !covered(h, ?into.public)) {
            val res_public: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Held](?into.public, @h);
            if (sel res_public.err) { ret failed[opt[bool]](res_public.err); }
            changed = true;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    if (from.anywhere && !into.anywhere) {
        into.anywhere = true;
        changed       = true;
        i             = 0;
        for (i < from.spared.len) {
            val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Held](?into.spared, from.spared.data[i]);
            if (sel pushed.err) { ret failed[opt[bool]](pushed.err); }
            i = i + 1;
        }
    }
    or (from.anywhere) {
        val narrowed: res[bool, A.Error] = narrow(w, ?into.spared, ?from.spared);
        if (sel narrowed.err) { ret failed[opt[bool]](narrowed.err); }
        if (narrowed.ok)      { changed = true; }
    }
    if (from.untyped && !into.untyped) {
        into.untyped = true;
        changed      = true;
    }
    if (from.untrusted && !into.untrusted) {
        into.untrusted = true;
        changed        = true;
    }
    val res_written: res[bool, A.Error] = written_both(w, into, from);
    if (sel res_written.err) { ret failed[opt[bool]](res_written.err); }
    if (res_written.ok)      { changed = true; }
    # a pointer statement holds in the join only where it holds on both paths, and a slot rewritten on either may be
    var stated: usize = 0;
    i = 0;
    for (i < into.pointed.len) {
        val x: Pointed = into.pointed.data[i];
        if (stated_of(from, ?x)) {
            into.pointed.data[stated] = x;
            stated                    = stated + 1;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    if (stated != into.pointed.len) {
        vector.truncate[Pointed](?into.pointed, stated);
        changed = true;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < from.rebound.len) {
        val res_rebound: res[bool, A.Error] = rebind(into, from.rebound.data[i]);
        if (sel res_rebound.err) { ret failed[opt[bool]](res_rebound.err); }
        if (res_rebound.ok)      { changed = true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    if (from.unbound && !into.unbound) {
        into.unbound = true;
        changed      = true;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < into.stack.len) {
        if (from.stack.data[i] && !into.stack.data[i]) {
            into.stack.data[i] = true;
            changed            = true;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    val entries: res[bool, A.Error] = merge_entries(w, into, from);
    if (sel entries.err) { ret failed[opt[bool]](entries.err); }
    if (entries.ok)      { changed = true; }
    var keep: bool = true;
    if (sel into.config.some) {
        keep = false;
        if (sel from.config.some) { keep = from.config.some.bits == into.config.some.bits; }
    }
    if (!keep) {
        into.config = opt[config.State].none{};
        changed     = true;
    }
    ret res[opt[bool], A.Error].ok{opt[bool].some{changed}};
}

# whether an extent held off a register's value of `version`, carried from the instruction at `from` into the one at
# `to`, may be of a value the walk will name by the same version again: the edge goes back, `to` at or before `from`,
# so the code between may run again, and the version is one an instruction or a join from `to` through `from` makes
# (`apply`, `merge`), which each pass makes anew though the register holds another value then. the entry's version
# never is, nor is any on an edge that goes forward, and every path that runs an instruction again goes back across
# it, so such an extent is known only to lie off a value of that version once it has crossed the edge
fun renewed(version: u64, from: usize, to: usize) bool {
    if (version == ENTRY || from == NO_OFFSET || to > from) { ret false; }
    var made: u64 = (version - 1) / 2;
    if ((version & 1) == 0) { made = (version - 2) / 2; }
    ret made >= to::u64 && made <= from::u64;
}

# the state `p` reaching the instruction at `to` from the one at `from`, NO_OFFSET for the entry: its point made or
# merged into, and `to` queued when it changed. an instruction a run fell into gets a point of its own, and the run is
# walked again to bring what falls into it there. an extent held off a version the code back to `to` makes again is
# carried known only to lie off that version's value (`renewed`)
# ---
# ret: false when the point at `to` holds an operand stack of another height than `p`
fun reach(w: *Walk, p: *Point, from: usize, to: usize) res[bool, A.Error] {
    val at: u32 = w.points.data[to];
    if (at == NO_POINT || at == THROUGH) {
        val made: res[Point, A.Error] = copy(w, p);
        if (sel made.err) { ret failed[bool](made.err); }
        var k: usize = 0;
        for (k < made.ok.held.len) {
            if (renewed(made.ok.held.data[k].version, from, to)) { off_unknown(?made.ok.held.data[k]); }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        w.points.data[to] = w.states.len::u32;
        val kept: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Point](?w.states, made.ok);
        if (sel kept.err)  { ret failed[bool](kept.err); }
        if (at == THROUGH) { queue(w, w.heads.data[to]::usize); }
    }
    or {
        val merged: res[opt[bool], A.Error] = merge(w, ?w.states.data[at], p, from, to);
        if (sel merged.err)     { ret failed[bool](merged.err); }
        if (sel merged.ok.none) { ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{false}; }
        if (!merged.ok.some)    { ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{true}; }
    }
    queue(w, to);
    ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{true};
}

# the instruction at `to` queued to be walked
fun queue(w: *Walk, to: usize) {
    w.queued.data[to / 64] = w.queued.data[to / 64] | (1::u64 << (to % 64)::u64);
    if (to < w.low) { w.low = to; }
}

# the lowest instruction start queued, taken off the queue, none when none is
fun dequeue(w: *Walk) opt[usize] {
    var k: usize = w.low / 64;
    for (k < w.queued.len) {
        val word: u64 = w.queued.data[k];
        if (word != 0) {
            val at: usize = k * 64 + bits.ctz(word)::usize;
            w.queued.data[k] = word & (word - 1);
            w.low            = at;
            ret opt[usize].some{at};
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    w.low = w.code.len;
    ret opt[usize].none{};
}

# `p`, the state the instruction at `at` leaves, falling into the next at `to`: merged into its point where it has
# one, else carried into it in place as the next of the run, the run reached again where another instruction fell
# into it before
fun falls_into(w: *Walk, p: *Point, at: usize, to: usize) res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] {
    val there: u32 = w.points.data[to];
    if (there != NO_POINT && (there != THROUGH || w.fell.data[to] != at)) { ret goes(w, p, at, to); }
    w.points.data[to] = THROUGH;
    w.heads.data[to]  = w.heads.data[at];
    w.fell.data[to]   = at;
    w.next            = to;
    ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{opt[Verdict].none{}};
}

fun row_index(w: *Walk, reg: register.Id) opt[u32] {
    if (reg == register.NONE) { ret opt[u32].none{}; }
    ret register.index_of(w.file, reg);
}

# whether register `reg` may hold a secret under `p`: its row, or any member of a tuple
fun tainted(w: *Walk, p: *Point, reg: register.Id) bool {
    val at: opt[u32] = row_index(w, reg);
    if (sel at.none) { ret false; }
    ret secret_row(w, p, at.some);
}

# whether row `at` may hold a secret under `p`: its own bit, or a tuple's members'
fun secret_row(w: *Walk, p: *Point, at: u32) bool {
    val r: *register.Register = ?w.file.registers[at];
    if (!register.tuple(r)) { ret bit_of(p.taint.data, at); }
    var k: u32 = 0;
    for (k < r.members.len) {
        if (bit_of(p.taint.data, r.members.at[k])) { ret true; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# whether row `at` holds storage the walk keeps secrecy of: neither reading zero nor a tuple, whose members hold its
fun stored(w: *Walk, at: u32) bool {
    val r: *register.Register = ?w.file.registers[at];
    ret (r.flags & register.ZERO) == 0 && !register.tuple(r);
}

# the stack pointer's row: the register the canonical frame address of the first architecture of the code's set the
# context enters is stated from, effect.NO_ROW when none has call frames
fun stack_row(file: *register.File, code: *Code, ctx: *state.Context) u32 {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < code.set.arches.len) {
        val a: *set.Arch = ?code.set.arches.at[i];
        if (a.frame != nil && state.admits(ctx, a.enters)) {
            if (file.register_count == 0) { ret effect.NO_ROW; }
            val row: opt[u32] = register.index_of(file, a.frame.cfa_register);
            if (sel row.some) { ret row.some; }
            ret effect.NO_ROW;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret effect.NO_ROW;
}

# the architecture of the code's set the context enters, its first, nil for none
fun arch_of(code: *Code, ctx: *state.Context) *mink_arch.Arch {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < code.set.arches.len) {
        val a: *set.Arch = ?code.set.arches.at[i];
        if (state.admits(ctx, a.enters)) { ret a.arch; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret nil;
}

# whether register row `row` holds storage of its own as wide as the stack pointer's, so the value it holds may be a
# known offset from it
fun wide(w: *Walk, row: u32) bool {
    if (w.stack == effect.NO_ROW || row >= w.file.register_count) { ret false; }
    val r:  *register.Register = ?w.file.registers[row];
    val sp: *register.Register = ?w.file.registers[w.stack];
    val rw: quantity.Scaled    = w.file.classes[r.class].width;
    val sw: quantity.Scaled    = w.file.classes[sp.class].width;
    ret stored(w, row) && rw.fixed == sw.fixed && rw.per == sw.per && rw.scale == sw.scale && r.count.fixed == 1 && r.count.per == 0;
}

# the extent of `length` bytes at `offset` off the value register row `row` holds under `p`: off the stack pointer's
# value on entry when the walk knows the row's offset from it, else off that version of the row's value
fun rebase(w: *Walk, p: *Point, row: u32, offset: i64, length: u64) Held {
    val f: Frame = value_of(w, p, row);
    if (f.known && !f.number) { ret Held{base: f.root, version: f.version, symbol: operand.NO_SYMBOL, slot: false, offset: f.offset + offset, length: length, indexed: false, apart: false}; }
    ret Held{base: row, version: p.versions.data[row], symbol: operand.NO_SYMBOL, slot: false, offset: offset, length: length, indexed: false, apart: false};
}

# the value register row `row` holds under `p`: a register reading zero holds the number 0, and one the walk knows no
# offset of is its own version's value at offset 0
fun value_of(w: *Walk, p: *Point, row: u32) Frame {
    if ((w.file.registers[row].flags & register.ZERO) != 0) { ret Frame{known: true, offset: 0, number: true, root: effect.NO_ROW, version: ENTRY}; }
    val f: Frame = p.frames.data[row];
    if (f.known) { ret f; }
    ret Frame{known: true, offset: 0, number: false, root: row, version: p.versions.data[row]};
}

# the registers `ins` writes as a stated function of what it reads into `w.derived`, with their inputs' secrecy under
# `p`, and those it gives a known value into `w.moved`: each relation of its row, whose register written holds the one
# it reads plus what an operand adds where no site fills it, as the base an access writes back, the value read's
# (`value_of`) moved by the number where the relation states it and both are as wide as the stack pointer, a register
# added to a number, a number shifted or negated added to a register, a number an immediate builds, a number combined
# with an immediate, and the stack pointer's own change its effect states, its value before plus the delta's operand,
# but where an operand names the stack pointer
fun moves(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *codec.Decoded, fp: *footprint.Footprint) err[A.Error] {
    vector.truncate[Moved](?w.moved, 0);
    vector.truncate[Derived](?w.derived, 0);
    val e:      *effect.Effect = ins.inst.row.effect;
    val values: operand.Values = operand.Values{at: ins.inst.values, len: ins.inst.count};
    var i:      u32            = 0;
    for (i < e.relations.len) {
        val rel: *effect.Relation = ?e.relations.at[i];
        i = i + 1;
        # a number a site fills is no value until the link
        if (relation_sited(w, rel)) { cnt; }
        if (sel rel.holds.number) {
            val opt_number: opt[effect.Affine] = query.numbered(w.file, rel, values);
            if (sel opt_number.none) { cnt; }
            val written: opt[u32] = row_index(w, opt_number.some.to);
            if (sel written.none) { cnt; }
            val err_derived: err[A.Error] = derive(w, written.some, false);
            if (sel err_derived.err) { ret err_derived; }
            if (w.stack != effect.NO_ROW && wide(w, written.some)) {
                val res_pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Moved](?w.moved, Moved{row: written.some, frame: Frame{known: true, offset: opt_number.some.by, number: true, root: effect.NO_ROW, version: ENTRY}});
                if (sel res_pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{res_pushed.err}; }
            }
            cnt;
        }
        val ends: opt[query.Ends] = query.ends(w.file, rel, values);
        if (sel ends.none) { cnt; }
        val to:   opt[u32] = row_index(w, ends.some.to);
        val from: opt[u32] = row_index(w, ends.some.from);
        if (sel to.none)   { cnt; }
        if (sel from.none) { cnt; }
        var secret: bool = secret_row(w, p, from.some);
        if (ends.some.added != register.NONE && tainted(w, p, ends.some.added)) { secret = true; }
        val derived: err[A.Error] = derive(w, to.some, secret);
        if (sel derived.err)                                                      { ret derived; }
        if (w.stack == effect.NO_ROW || !wide(w, to.some) || !wide(w, from.some)) { cnt; }
        val f: Frame = value_of(w, p, from.some);
        if (!f.known) { cnt; }
        if (sel rel.holds.combined) {
            # a combination keeps a number a number and leaves anything else no value the walk knows
            if (!f.number) { cnt; }
            val opt_combined: opt[i64] = query.combine(?rel.holds.combined, values, f.offset);
            if (sel opt_combined.none) { cnt; }
            val res_combined: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Moved](?w.moved, Moved{row: to.some, frame: Frame{known: true, offset: opt_combined.some, number: true, root: effect.NO_ROW, version: ENTRY}});
            if (sel res_combined.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{res_combined.err}; }
            cnt;
        }
        if (ends.some.added != register.NONE) {
            # register plus register, the added one shifted and negated as the relation states: an offset from a
            # register plus a number, or two numbers. a shift or a negation moves only a number
            if (!sel rel.holds.offset) { cnt; }
            val o:     effect.Offset = rel.holds.offset;
            val added: opt[u32]      = row_index(w, ends.some.added);
            if (sel added.none)       { cnt; }
            if (!wide(w, added.some)) { cnt; }
            val opt_bits: opt[u64] = query.shift_bits(?o, values);
            if (sel opt_bits.none) { cnt; }
            val g:      Frame = value_of(w, p, added.some);
            val scaled: bool  = opt_bits.some != 0 || o.negated;
            if (scaled && !g.number)    { cnt; }
            if (!f.number && !g.number) { cnt; }
            var by: u64 = g.offset::u64 << opt_bits.some;
            if (o.negated) { by = 0 - by; }
            var sum: Frame = f;
            if (f.number) { sum = g; }
            sum.offset = (f.offset::u64 + by + o.constant::u64)::i64;
            val res_summed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Moved](?w.moved, Moved{row: to.some, frame: sum});
            if (sel res_summed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{res_summed.err}; }
            cnt;
        }
        val got: opt[effect.Affine] = query.affine(w.file, rel, values);
        if (sel got.none) { cnt; }
        var moved: Frame = f;
        moved.offset = f.offset + got.some.by;
        val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Moved](?w.moved, Moved{row: to.some, frame: moved});
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
    }
    if (w.stack == effect.NO_ROW) { ret err[A.Error].ok{}; }
    val st: effect.Stack = fp.stack;
    if (sel st.delta) {
        val f:      Frame = p.frames.data[w.stack];
        var bytes:  i64   = st.delta.bytes::i64;
        var known:  bool  = on_stack(w, f);
        var stated: bool  = true;
        var secret: bool  = secret_row(w, p, w.stack);
        if (st.delta.operand != field.NO_OPERAND) {
            known  = false;
            stated = false;
            if (st.delta.operand::u32 < ins.inst.count) {
                val v: operand.Value = ins.inst.values[st.delta.operand];
                if (sel v.immediate) {
                    bytes  = bytes + v.immediate;
                    known  = on_stack(w, f);
                    stated = true;
                }
                or (sel v.register) {
                    secret = secret || tainted(w, p, v.register);
                    stated = true;
                }
            }
        }
        # an operand naming the stack pointer may write it from data, as x86 `pop rsp`
        var op: u32 = 0;
        for (stated && op < ins.inst.count) {
            val v: operand.Value = ins.inst.values[op];
            if (sel v.register) {
                val at: opt[u32] = row_index(w, v.register);
                if (sel at.some) {
                    val sharing: res[bool, A.Error] = shares(w, at.some, w.stack);
                    if (sel sharing.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{sharing.err}; }
                    if (sharing.ok)      { stated = false; }
                }
            }
            op = op + 1;
        }
        if (stated) {
            val derived: err[A.Error] = derive(w, w.stack, secret);
            if (sel derived.err) { ret derived; }
        }
        if (known) {
            val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Moved](?w.moved, Moved{row: w.stack, frame: Frame{known: true, offset: f.offset + bytes, number: false, root: w.stack, version: ENTRY}});
            if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
        }
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# row `row` into `w.derived` as written from inputs of which any is secret when `secret` is, one a relation and the
# stack's delta both write taking either's
fun derive(w: *Walk, row: u32, secret: bool) err[A.Error] {
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < w.derived.len) {
        if (w.derived.data[k].row == row) {
            w.derived.data[k].secret = w.derived.data[k].secret || secret;
            ret err[A.Error].ok{};
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Derived](?w.derived, Derived{row: row, secret: secret});
    if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# whether register row `row` the instruction walked writes takes secrecy of its own: its inputs' where `w.derived`
# holds it, else `value`, whether anything the instruction reads is secret
fun written_secret(w: *Walk, row: u32, value: bool) bool {
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < w.derived.len) {
        if (w.derived.data[k].row == row) { ret w.derived.data[k].secret; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret value;
}

# the rows a register value of operand `op` covers marked in `into`, and whether any of them is secret under `p`. a
# grouped value covers the registers its operand's groups do, an address register one
fun mark_register(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *codec.Decoded, op: u8, reg: register.Id, grouped: bool, cfg: config.Configured, into: *u64) bool {
    val at: opt[u32] = row_index(w, reg);
    if (sel at.none) { ret false; }
    var count: u32 = 1;
    if (grouped) {
        val covers: query.Answer[u32] = footprint.covers(ins.inst.row, op, w.ctx, cfg);
        if (sel covers.decided) {
            if (covers.decided > 1) { count = covers.decided; }
        }
    }
    var secret: bool = false;
    var k:      u32  = 0;
    for (k < count && at.some + k < w.file.register_count) {
        set_bit(into, at.some + k, true);
        if (secret_row(w, p, at.some + k)) { secret = true; }
        # a tuple's members are the operand's registers as much as the tuple is
        val r: *register.Register = ?w.file.registers[at.some + k];
        var j: u32                = 0;
        for (j < r.members.len) {
            set_bit(into, r.members.at[j], true);
            j = j + 1;
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret secret;
}

# whether a register value of operand `op` is secret under `p`, its rows marked in `into`: a register, every member of
# a list, and a memory value's address registers, which are marked but are no data of the operand
fun operand_secret(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *codec.Decoded, op: u8, cfg: config.Configured, into: *u64) bool {
    val v: operand.Value = ins.inst.values[op];
    if (sel v.register) { ret mark_register(w, p, ins, op, v.register, true, cfg, into); }
    if (sel v.list) {
        var secret: bool = false;
        var i:      u32  = 0;
        for (i < v.list.len) {
            val m: operand.Value = v.list.at[i];
            if (sel m.register && mark_register(w, p, ins, op, m.register, false, cfg, into)) { secret = true; }
            i = i + 1;
        }
        ret secret;
    }
    if (sel v.id) {
        val state: opt[register.Id] = constraint.state_of(w.file, ?ins.inst.row.operands.at[op], v.id);
        if (sel state.some) { ret mark_register(w, p, ins, op, state.some, false, cfg, into); }
        ret false;
    }
    # the address registers are named, and a secret in them is refused as an address, not as the operand's data
    if (sel v.memory) {
        mark_register(w, p, ins, op, v.memory.base, false, cfg, into);
        mark_register(w, p, ins, op, v.memory.index, false, cfg, into);
    }
    ret false;
}

# whether some register of operand `op`'s value is secret under `p`, its address registers included
fun names_secret(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *codec.Decoded, op: u8) bool {
    if (op == field.NO_OPERAND || op::u32 >= ins.inst.count) { ret false; }
    val v: operand.Value = ins.inst.values[op];
    if (sel v.register) { ret tainted(w, p, v.register); }
    if (sel v.memory)   { ret tainted(w, p, v.memory.base) || tainted(w, p, v.memory.index); }
    if (sel v.list) {
        var i: u32 = 0;
        for (i < v.list.len) {
            val m: operand.Value = v.list.at[i];
            if (sel m.register && tainted(w, p, m.register)) { ret true; }
            i = i + 1;
        }
    }
    ret false;
}

# whether the value the instruction pops at depth `pop` less one may hold a secret under `p`, which holds the
# instruction's pops on top of its stack. none for 0, and the ordered read holds every depth to what the instruction pops
fun popped_secret(p: *Point, pop: u8) bool {
    if (pop == 0) { ret false; }
    ret p.stack.data[p.stack.len - pop::usize];
}

# the bytes access width `width` covers, 0 when the walk does not know them: a width scaling with a quantity, or a
# count no element fixes
fun bytes_of(width: *effect.Width) u64 {
    val count: effect.Count = width.count;
    if (!sel count.one || width.element.per != 0 || width.element.fixed == 0) { ret 0; }
    ret (width.element.fixed::u64 + 7) / 8;
}

# the extent an address of `ins` touches, from the operand that is or holds it plus the immediates of the further
# operands `forming` names, or the register row `base` when none, plus the access's own `offset`, named off the stack
# pointer when the walk knows that register's offset from it, or off a symbol's address when the sites place it there
# (`address_formed`), as a high part the operand's register holds and the low part a site fills in a further operand
# complete (`completed`), as risc-v's and aarch64's loads through a got slot. an address a register adds to, as a memory operand's index, a further operand that is no
# immediate, as a risc-v stride, or an index the access states with `indexed`, as xlat's al, is placed off its base
# register's value at an offset the walk does not know, and off no symbol. a memory operand written back after the
# access is at its base alone. one a site fills that the sites do not place, whose number is no address until the link,
# is placed nowhere
fun placed(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *codec.Decoded, op: u8, base: u32, forming: operand.Positions, offset: i64, length: u64, indexed: bool, touch: *Touch) {
    touch.operand   = field.NO_OPERAND;
    touch.at        = UNPLACED;
    touch.at.offset = offset;
    touch.at.length = length;
    var formed:  Formed = UNFORMED;
    var high:    Formed = UNFORMED;
    var sited:   bool   = false;
    var added:   i64    = 0;
    var unbound: bool   = indexed;
    if (op != field.NO_OPERAND && op::u32 < ins.inst.count) {
        val v: operand.Value = ins.inst.values[op];
        sited = has_site(w, op);
        if (sel v.memory) {
            touch.operand = op;
            val m: operand.Address = v.memory;
            if (m.mode != operand.POSTINDEX && m.mode != operand.POSTINDEX_REGISTER) {
                touch.at.offset = touch.at.offset + m.disp;
                if (m.index != register.NONE) { unbound = true; }
            }
            val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, m.base);
            if (sel row.some) { touch.at.base = row.some; }
            formed = address_formed(w, p, ins, op);
        }
        or (sel v.register) {
            val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, v.register);
            if (sel row.some) {
                touch.at.base = row.some;
                formed        = whole_of(p.formed.data[row.some]);
                high          = p.formed.data[row.some];
            }
        }
        or (sel v.relative) { formed = address_formed(w, p, ins, op); }
        var k: u32 = 0;
        for (k < ins.inst.count && k < 32) {
            if ((forming & (1::u32 << k)) != 0) {
                val f:  operand.Value = ins.inst.values[k];
                val st: opt[*Site]    = site_at(w, k::u8);
                if (sel st.some) {
                    sited  = true;
                    formed = completed(w, high, st.some);
                    high   = UNFORMED;
                }
                or (sel f.immediate) {
                    touch.at.offset = touch.at.offset + f.immediate;
                    added           = added + f.immediate;
                }
                or { unbound = true; }
            }
            k = k + 1;
        }
    }
    or {
        touch.at.base = base;
        if (base != effect.NO_ROW) { formed = whole_of(p.formed.data[base]); }
    }
    if (unbound) { formed = UNFORMED; }
    touch.row     = touch.at.base;
    touch.rebased = 0;
    if (formed.piece == fixup.WHOLE) {
        touch.at  = Held{base: effect.NO_ROW, version: ENTRY, symbol: formed.symbol, slot: formed.slot, offset: formed.offset + offset + added, length: length, indexed: false, apart: false};
        touch.row = effect.NO_ROW;
        ret;
    }
    if (sited) {
        touch.at.base = effect.NO_ROW;
        touch.row     = effect.NO_ROW;
    }
    if (touch.at.base != effect.NO_ROW) {
        val h: Held = rebase(w, p, touch.at.base, touch.at.offset, touch.at.length);
        touch.rebased = h.offset - touch.at.offset;
        touch.at      = h;
    }
    if (unbound) {
        if (!anchored(w, touch)) { off_unknown(?touch.at); }
        touch.rebased = 0;
    }
}

# touch `t`, whose address a register decides the offset of, placed within the stated frame local its base's value
# points into, known only to lie within it, as an offset off a base stays within its object and a local is one object.
# both the base's value and the address before the register adds to it must lie within the one local, as a base the
# stack pointer holds points at no one object and a displacement may lead off its base's. false where they do not,
# which leaves it to `off_unknown`
fun anchored(w: *Walk, t: *Touch) bool {
    if (w.objects.len == 0 || !in_frame(w, ?t.at)) { ret false; }
    val from: i64   = t.rebased;
    val at:   i64   = t.at.offset;
    var i:    usize = 0;
    for (i < w.objects.len) {
        val x: *Held = ?w.objects.data[i];
        if (from >= x.offset && from < x.offset + x.length::i64 && at >= x.offset && at < x.offset + x.length::i64) {
            t.at = Held{base: w.stack, version: ENTRY, symbol: operand.NO_SYMBOL, slot: false, offset: x.offset, length: x.length, indexed: false, apart: false, within: true};
            ret true;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# the operand of the row decoded that operand `op` of the instruction walked as it was written names, field.NO_OPERAND for
# none: a caller names an operand of the instruction it built, which the builder may have compressed, as an access
# seed on `sd`'s base names `c.sdsp`'s sp
fun built(w: *Walk, op: u8) u8 {
    if (op::u32 >= operand.MAX_OPERANDS) { ret field.NO_OPERAND; }
    ret w.written[op];
}

# the site the caller states for operand `op` of the row decoded of the instruction walked, none for none
fun site_at(w: *Walk, op: u8) opt[*Site] {
    val at: usize = w.at;
    if (at >= w.sited.len) { ret opt[*Site].none{}; }
    var i: u32 = w.sited.data[at];
    for (i != NO_POINT && i < w.code.sites.len) {
        val st: *Site = ?w.code.sites.at[i];
        if (st.at != at::u64)           { ret opt[*Site].none{}; }
        if (built(w, st.operand) == op) { ret opt[*Site].some{st}; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret opt[*Site].none{};
}

# whether a site fills operand `op` of the instruction walked
fun has_site(w: *Walk, op: u8) bool {
    val st: opt[*Site] = site_at(w, op);
    ret sel st.some;
}

# the capabilities of the relocation kind site `st`'s fixup kind is bound to on the architecture the walk runs under,
# none for a kind bound to none there, as a local kind
fun site_caps(w: *Walk, st: *Site) opt[reloc.Caps] {
    if (w.arch == nil) { ret opt[reloc.Caps].none{}; }
    val all: fixup.Bindings = w.code.set.bindings;
    var i:   u32            = 0;
    for (i < all.len) {
        val b: *fixup.Binding = ?all.at[i];
        if (b.fixup == st.fixup && fixup.binds(b, w.arch)) { ret opt[reloc.Caps].some{reloc.caps(b.kind)}; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret opt[reloc.Caps].none{};
}

# `f` when it is a symbol's address, else UNFORMED
fun whole_of(f: Formed) Formed {
    if (f.piece == fixup.WHOLE) { ret f; }
    ret UNFORMED;
}

# whether `x` and `y` hold one part of one address
fun same_form(x: *Formed, y: *Formed) bool {
    ret x.piece == y.piece && x.symbol == y.symbol && x.offset == y.offset && x.slot == y.slot && x.partnered == y.partnered && x.site == y.site;
}

# what the operand site `st` fills holds of its symbol's address alone, by the part its fixup kind holds: the address,
# a high part, or UNFORMED for a low part, which completes a high one, or a kind the set states no part of
fun site_formed(w: *Walk, st: *Site) Formed {
    if (st.symbol == operand.NO_SYMBOL) { ret UNFORMED; }
    val piece: fixup.Piece     = fixup.piece_of(w.code.set.parts, st.fixup);
    val caps:  opt[reloc.Caps] = site_caps(w, st);
    if (sel caps.none) { ret UNFORMED; }
    val slot: bool = (caps.some & reloc.GOT) != 0;
    if (piece == fixup.WHOLE) { ret Formed{piece: fixup.WHOLE, symbol: st.symbol, offset: st.addend, slot: slot, partnered: false, site: 0}; }
    if (piece == fixup.HIGH) {
        val partnered: bool = (caps.some & reloc.PC) != 0 && (caps.some & reloc.PAGE) == 0;
        ret Formed{piece: fixup.HIGH, symbol: st.symbol, offset: st.addend, slot: slot, partnered: partnered, site: st.at};
    }
    ret UNFORMED;
}

# the address high part `high` and the low part site `st` fills make, UNFORMED unless they are of one address: a low
# part naming a partner completes the high part its partner's instruction formed, and any other one of the same symbol,
# addend and slot that no partner completes
fun completed(w: *Walk, high: Formed, st: *Site) Formed {
    if (high.piece != fixup.HIGH || fixup.piece_of(w.code.set.parts, st.fixup) != fixup.LOW) { ret UNFORMED; }
    val caps: opt[reloc.Caps] = site_caps(w, st);
    if (sel caps.none) { ret UNFORMED; }
    if ((caps.some & reloc.PARTNER) != 0) {
        if (!high.partnered || high.site != st.partner) { ret UNFORMED; }
    }
    or {
        val slot: bool = (caps.some & reloc.GOT) != 0;
        if (high.partnered || high.symbol != st.symbol || high.offset != st.addend || high.slot != slot) { ret UNFORMED; }
    }
    ret Formed{piece: fixup.WHOLE, symbol: high.symbol, offset: high.offset, slot: high.slot, partnered: false, site: 0};
}

# the symbol's address the address operand `op` of `ins` forms under `p`, UNFORMED for none the sites place: a site of
# the address whole in a relative operand or an address of no base, as a rip-relative or absolute one, a site of a
# low part added to a base register holding its high part, or a base register holding an address plus a displacement
# no site fills. an address with an index or written back after the access is placed by no symbol
fun address_formed(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *codec.Decoded, op: u8) Formed {
    if (op == field.NO_OPERAND || op::u32 >= ins.inst.count) { ret UNFORMED; }
    val v:  operand.Value = ins.inst.values[op];
    val st: opt[*Site]    = site_at(w, op);
    if (sel v.relative) {
        if (sel st.some) { ret whole_of(site_formed(w, st.some)); }
        ret UNFORMED;
    }
    if (!sel v.memory) { ret UNFORMED; }
    val m: operand.Address = v.memory;
    if (m.index != register.NONE)                                                                { ret UNFORMED; }
    if (m.mode != operand.OFFSET && m.mode != operand.PREINDEX && m.mode != operand.RELATIVE_PC) { ret UNFORMED; }
    if (m.base == register.NONE || m.mode == operand.RELATIVE_PC) {
        if (sel st.some) { ret whole_of(site_formed(w, st.some)); }
        ret UNFORMED;
    }
    val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, m.base);
    if (sel row.none) { ret UNFORMED; }
    var f: Formed = p.formed.data[row.some];
    if (sel st.some)            { ret completed(w, f, st.some); }
    if (f.piece != fixup.WHOLE) { ret UNFORMED; }
    f.offset = f.offset + m.disp;
    ret f;
}

# the register a relation of `ins` writes, register.NONE for none it names
fun related_to(w: *Walk, ins: *codec.Decoded, rel: *effect.Relation) register.Id {
    if (sel rel.to.operand) {
        if (rel.to.operand::u32 >= ins.inst.count) { ret register.NONE; }
        val v: operand.Value = ins.inst.values[rel.to.operand];
        if (sel v.register) { ret v.register; }
        ret register.NONE;
    }
    if (sel rel.to.row) {
        if (rel.to.row >= w.file.register_count) { ret register.NONE; }
        ret register.id_of(?w.file.registers[rel.to.row]);
    }
    ret register.NONE;
}

# what relation `rel` of `ins` leaves its register holding of a symbol's address under `p`: what a site of the operand
# it forms its value from holds, the address a lea's operand forms, a low part a site fills added to the high part its
# register holds, or an address its register holds plus a number no site fills, as a copy or an add of an immediate
fun relation_formed(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *codec.Decoded, rel: *effect.Relation) Formed {
    if (sel rel.holds.formed) {
        val st: opt[*Site] = site_at(w, rel.holds.formed);
        if (sel st.some) { ret site_formed(w, st.some); }
        ret UNFORMED;
    }
    if (sel rel.holds.number) {
        val opt_site: opt[*Site] = site_at(w, rel.holds.number.operand);
        if (sel opt_site.some) { ret site_formed(w, opt_site.some); }
        ret UNFORMED;
    }
    if (!sel rel.holds.offset) { ret UNFORMED; }
    val o: effect.Offset = rel.holds.offset;
    if (sel o.from.base) { ret whole_of(address_formed(w, p, ins, o.from.base)); }
    var from: register.Id = register.NONE;
    if (sel o.from.operand) {
        if (o.from.operand::u32 < ins.inst.count) {
            val v: operand.Value = ins.inst.values[o.from.operand];
            if (sel v.register) { from = v.register; }
        }
    }
    or (sel o.from.row) {
        if (o.from.row < w.file.register_count) { from = register.id_of(?w.file.registers[o.from.row]); }
    }
    val src: opt[u32] = row_index(w, from);
    if (sel src.none) { ret UNFORMED; }
    var f: Formed = p.formed.data[src.some];
    if (sel o.by.immediate) {
        val st: opt[*Site] = site_at(w, o.by.immediate);
        if (sel st.some) {
            val values: operand.Values = operand.Values{at: ins.inst.values, len: ins.inst.count};
            if (o.negated || !query.unshifted(?o, values) || o.constant != 0) { ret UNFORMED; }
            ret completed(w, f, st.some);
        }
    }
    if (f.piece != fixup.WHOLE) { ret UNFORMED; }
    val values: operand.Values     = operand.Values{at: ins.inst.values, len: ins.inst.count};
    val got:    opt[effect.Affine] = query.affine(w.file, rel, values);
    if (sel got.none) { ret UNFORMED; }
    f.offset = f.offset + got.some.by;
    ret f;
}

# whether a site fills an operand relation `rel` adds, starts from or builds its number from, whose number is no value
# until the link
fun relation_sited(w: *Walk, rel: *effect.Relation) bool {
    if (sel rel.holds.number)   { ret has_site(w, rel.holds.number.operand); }
    if (sel rel.holds.combined) { ret has_site(w, rel.holds.combined.operand); }
    if (!sel rel.holds.offset)  { ret false; }
    val o: effect.Offset = rel.holds.offset;
    if (sel o.by.immediate) {
        if (has_site(w, o.by.immediate)) { ret true; }
    }
    if (sel o.by.displacement) {
        if (has_site(w, o.by.displacement)) { ret true; }
    }
    if (sel o.from.base) {
        if (has_site(w, o.from.base)) { ret true; }
    }
    ret false;
}

# the row of the one register operand `ins` writes, none for none or more than one
fun written_row(w: *Walk, ins: *codec.Decoded) opt[u32] {
    val r:     *operand.Operand = ins.inst.row.operands.at;
    var found: u32              = effect.NO_ROW;
    var count: u32              = 0;
    var op:    u32              = 0;
    for (op < ins.inst.count) {
        val v: operand.Value = ins.inst.values[op];
        if (sel v.register) {
            if ((r[op].role & operand.WRITE) != 0) {
                count = count + 1;
                found = row_or_none(w, v.register);
            }
        }
        op = op + 1;
    }
    if (count != 1 || found == effect.NO_ROW) { ret opt[u32].none{}; }
    ret opt[u32].some{found};
}

# the registers `ins` gives a symbol's address or a part of one under `p` into `w.forming`: each its row's relations
# write as wide as the stack pointer, and the one register a load of a got slot alone writes, which takes the slot's
# symbol's address. read where the instruction starts, once `w.touches` holds its touches
fun formings(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *codec.Decoded) err[A.Error] {
    vector.truncate[Forming](?w.forming, 0);
    if (w.code.sites.len == 0) { ret err[A.Error].ok{}; }
    val e: *effect.Effect = ins.inst.row.effect;
    var i: u32            = 0;
    for (i < e.relations.len) {
        val rel: *effect.Relation = ?e.relations.at[i];
        val row: opt[u32]         = row_index(w, related_to(w, ins, rel));
        if (sel row.some) {
            if (wide(w, row.some)) {
                val f: Formed = relation_formed(w, p, ins, rel);
                if (f.piece != fixup.NO_PIECE) {
                    val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Forming](?w.forming, Forming{row: row.some, formed: f});
                    if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
                }
            }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    if (w.forming.len != 0 || w.touches.len != 1) { ret err[A.Error].ok{}; }
    val t: *Touch = ?w.touches.data[0];
    if (!t.reads || t.writes || !symbolic(?t.at) || !t.at.slot || t.at.offset != 0) { ret err[A.Error].ok{}; }
    val row: opt[u32] = written_row(w, ins);
    if (sel row.some) {
        if (wide(w, row.some)) {
            val f:      Formed              = Formed{piece: fixup.WHOLE, symbol: t.at.symbol, offset: 0, slot: false, partnered: false, site: 0};
            val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Forming](?w.forming, Forming{row: row.some, formed: f});
            if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
        }
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# the bytes the access of memory operand `o` holding address `m` covers, its width of one value, 0 when the walk does
# not know them: a width the operand does not state, more than one value, or an element broadcast from part of it
fun operand_bytes(o: *operand.Operand, m: operand.Address) u64 {
    if (o.width == 0 || o.quantity != operand.ONE || m.broadcast != 0) { ret 0; }
    ret (o.width::u64 + 7) / 8;
}

# the refusal of a secret in what decides an access's count `count` under `p`: the register at its row, its operand or
# the value it pops, naming the operand when one decides it. none for a count nothing the instruction reads decides
fun count_secret(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *codec.Decoded, count: effect.Count) opt[ct.Refusal] {
    var secret: bool = false;
    var op:     u8   = field.NO_OPERAND;
    if (sel count.register) { secret = bit_of(p.taint.data, count.register); }
    or (sel count.operand) {
        op     = count.operand;
        secret = names_secret(w, p, ins, op);
    }
    or (sel count.popped) { secret = popped_secret(p, count.popped + 1); }
    if (!secret)          { ret opt[ct.Refusal].none{}; }
    ret opt[ct.Refusal].some{ct.refusal(ct.MEMORY, op)};
}

# the refusal of a secret in the index `x` of an access adds to its address under `p`: the register at its row or its
# operand, naming the operand when one holds it. none for no index, or one of no form the walk knows, which it places
# nowhere
fun index_secret(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *codec.Decoded, x: *effect.Index) opt[ct.Refusal] {
    if (sel x.register) {
        if (x.register.at != effect.NO_ROW && bit_of(p.taint.data, x.register.at)) { ret opt[ct.Refusal].some{ct.refusal(ct.MEMORY, field.NO_OPERAND)}; }
    }
    if (sel x.operand) {
        val op: u8 = x.operand.at::u8;
        if (names_secret(w, p, ins, op)) { ret opt[ct.Refusal].some{ct.refusal(ct.MEMORY, op)}; }
    }
    ret opt[ct.Refusal].none{};
}

fun found(r: ct.Refusal) res[opt[ct.Refusal], A.Error] {
    ret res[opt[ct.Refusal], A.Error].ok{opt[ct.Refusal].some{r}};
}

# whether the walk places the extent `h` in an object it names: off a symbol's address, or in the frame off the stack
# pointer's value on entry
fun pinned(w: *Walk, h: *Held) bool {
    ret symbolic(h) || in_frame(w, h);
}

# whether access seed `a` names touch `t`
fun names_touch(w: *Walk, a: *Access, t: *Touch) bool {
    if (sel a.access.operand) {
        val op: u8 = built(w, a.access.operand);
        ret op != field.NO_OPERAND && op == t.named;
    }
    if (sel a.access.index) { ret a.access.index == t.index; }
    ret false;
}

# touch `t` of the instruction walked seeded by the access seeds naming it, secret when any of them is, placed or not:
# a store follows its seed wherever it writes, and a read the walk places follows its extents (`reads_secret`). one no
# access seed names, which the walk places off no symbol and in no frame slot, takes the statement a pointer seed makes
# under `p` of the register value it is off (`pointee`)
fun take_seed(w: *Walk, p: *Point, t: *Touch) {
    var i: u32 = w.stated.data[w.at];
    for (i != NO_POINT) {
        val sd: Seed = w.secrets.at[i];
        if (sel sd.access) {
            var a: Access = sd.access;
            if (names_touch(w, ?a, t)) {
                t.seeded = true;
                if (a.secret) { t.secret = true; }
            }
        }
        i = w.sowing.data[i];
    }
    if (t.seeded || pinned(w, ?t.at)) { ret; }
    val opt_pointee: opt[bool] = pointee(p, ?t.at);
    if (sel opt_pointee.some) {
        t.seeded = true;
        t.secret = opt_pointee.some;
    }
}

# what a pointer seed states under `p` of the memory extent `h` is off: the secrecy it states when `h` is off a register
# value `p` holds the statement for, none for any other
fun pointee(p: *Point, h: *Held) opt[bool] {
    if (h.base == effect.NO_ROW || h.symbol != operand.NO_SYMBOL) { ret opt[bool].none{}; }
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < p.pointed.len) {
        val x: *Pointed = ?p.pointed.data[k];
        if (x.row == h.base && x.version == h.version) { ret opt[bool].some{x.secret}; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret opt[bool].none{};
}

# the statements `ins`, at `at`, makes under `r` of the registers it writes, into `w.stating`: the one a pointer seed
# at `at` states of the register it resolved, where its slot holds what the binding states (`bound_intact`), and one for
# each register it writes as a relation of its row states it, from a register whose value under `r` a pointer seed
# states plus what a public operand adds, as the base an access writes back or an offset added to the pointer: an
# address off it reaches the storage the seed's does, as an access off the seeded value at that offset or index would,
# the language leaving one past that storage undefined
fun carry_pointers(w: *Walk, r: *Point, at: usize, ins: *codec.Decoded) err[A.Error] {
    vector.truncate[Pointed](?w.stating, 0);
    if (w.pointing.len == 0) { ret err[A.Error].ok{}; }
    val version: u64   = at::u64 * 2 + 1;
    var k:       usize = 0;
    for (k < w.pointing.len) {
        val x: *Pointing = ?w.pointing.data[k];
        k = k + 1;
        if (x.at != at::u64 || x.row == effect.NO_ROW || !bound_intact(w, r, ?w.touches.data[0].at)) { cnt; }
        val res_stated: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Pointed](?w.stating, Pointed{row: x.row, version: version, secret: x.secret});
        if (sel res_stated.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{res_stated.err}; }
    }
    val e:      *effect.Effect = ins.inst.row.effect;
    val values: operand.Values = operand.Values{at: ins.inst.values, len: ins.inst.count};
    var i:      u32            = 0;
    for (i < e.relations.len) {
        val rel: *effect.Relation = ?e.relations.at[i];
        i = i + 1;
        if (sel rel.holds.number) { cnt; }
        val ends: opt[query.Ends] = query.ends(w.file, rel, values);
        if (sel ends.none) { cnt; }
        val to:   opt[u32] = row_index(w, ends.some.to);
        val from: opt[u32] = row_index(w, ends.some.from);
        if (sel to.none)                                                        { cnt; }
        if (sel from.none)                                                      { cnt; }
        if (!wide(w, to.some) || !wide(w, from.some))                           { cnt; }
        if (ends.some.added != register.NONE && tainted(w, r, ends.some.added)) { cnt; }
        val source: Held      = Held{base: from.some, version: r.versions.data[from.some], symbol: operand.NO_SYMBOL, slot: false, offset: 0, length: 0, indexed: false, apart: false};
        val stated: opt[bool] = pointee(r, ?source);
        if (sel stated.none) { cnt; }
        val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Pointed](?w.stating, Pointed{row: to.some, version: version, secret: stated.some});
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# the register row each pointer seed at `at` names resolved from `ins`, once `w.touches` holds its touches: the one
# register it writes and does not read, as wide as the stack pointer, where its one access reads and writes nothing.
# an instruction of any other shape leaves the seed naming no row, so it states nothing
fun resolve_pointers(w: *Walk, at: usize, ins: *codec.Decoded) {
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < w.pointing.len) {
        val x: *Pointing = ?w.pointing.data[k];
        k = k + 1;
        if (x.at != at::u64 || x.row != effect.NO_ROW)                                  { cnt; }
        if (w.touches.len != 1 || !w.touches.data[0].reads || w.touches.data[0].writes) { cnt; }
        val r:     *operand.Operand = ins.inst.row.operands.at;
        var found: u32              = effect.NO_ROW;
        var count: u32              = 0;
        var op:    u32              = 0;
        for (op < ins.inst.count) {
            val v: operand.Value = ins.inst.values[op];
            if (sel v.register) {
                if ((r[op].role & operand.WRITE) != 0) {
                    count = count + 1;
                    val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, v.register);
                    if ((r[op].role & operand.READ) == 0) {
                        if (sel row.some) { found = row.some; }
                    }
                }
            }
            op = op + 1;
        }
        if (count == 1 && found != effect.NO_ROW && wide(w, found)) { x.row = found; }
    }
}

# whether the slot `slot` a binding's pointer is loaded from holds under `p` what the binding states of it: no inline
# block's store the walk places in the frame may have written it, and none it does not place, nor a call writing memory,
# may have reached it, which a private slot is out of reach of. the compiler's own stores of the slot store a value of
# the local's type, an inline block's any value
fun bound_intact(w: *Walk, p: *Point, slot: *Held) bool {
    if (p.unbound && !is_private(w, slot)) { ret false; }
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < p.rebound.len) {
        if (may_alias(w, ?p.rebound.data[i], slot)) { ret false; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret true;
}

# whether `p` holds the pointer statement `x` already
fun stated_of(p: *Point, x: *Pointed) bool {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < p.pointed.len) {
        val y: *Pointed = ?p.pointed.data[i];
        if (y.row == x.row && y.version == x.version && y.secret == x.secret) { ret true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# the pointer statements of `p` after the instruction walked at `at`, as `apply` left it: those it makes (`w.stating`)
# added, each kept once its register is written again, as an extent off a register a relation moved from it is named
# off the value it was moved from, the frame extents an inline block's store wrote rebound, or every slot that is not
# private for one the walk does not place in the frame, as for a call `callee` that writes memory, and a rebound extent
# a store of the compiler's own covers exactly bound again, as it stores a value of its local's type
fun state_pointers(w: *Walk, p: *Point, at: usize, fp: *footprint.Footprint, callee: *Call) err[A.Error] {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < w.stating.len) {
        if (stated_of(p, ?w.stating.data[i])) {
            i = i + 1;
            cnt;
        }
        val res_stated: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Pointed](?p.pointed, w.stating.data[i]);
        if (sel res_stated.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{res_stated.err}; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    val inline: bool = inlined(w, at);
    i = 0;
    for (i < w.touches.len) {
        val t: *Touch = ?w.touches.data[i];
        i = i + 1;
        if (!t.writes)                     { cnt; }
        if (inline && !in_frame(w, ?t.at)) { p.unbound = true; }
        or (inline) {
            val res_rebound: res[bool, A.Error] = rebind(p, t.at);
            if (sel res_rebound.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{res_rebound.err}; }
        }
        or (in_frame(w, ?t.at) && exact(?t.at)) {
            var left: usize = 0;
            var n:    usize = 0;
            for (n < p.rebound.len) {
                if (!inside(?p.rebound.data[n], ?t.at)) {
                    p.rebound.data[left] = p.rebound.data[n];
                    left                 = left + 1;
                }
                n = n + 1;
            }
            vector.truncate[Held](?p.rebound, left);
        }
    }
    if (fp.control.transfer == effect.CALL && (callee == nil || !callee.keeps)) { p.unbound = true; }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# `h` added to the frame extents `p` holds rebound, unless one holds every byte of it already
# ---
# ret: whether they changed
fun rebind(p: *Point, h: Held) res[bool, A.Error] {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < p.rebound.len) {
        if (same(?p.rebound.data[i], ?h) || inside(?h, ?p.rebound.data[i])) { ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{false}; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    val err_gathered: err[A.Error] = gather(?p.rebound, h);
    if (sel err_gathered.err) { ret failed[bool](err_gathered.err); }
    ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{true};
}

# whether touch `t` of an inline block's instruction writes a slot the frame code saves a register in, which the epilogue
# restores into the register its caller keeps a value in. a touch past the function's own frame, or at an offset or of
# a length the walk does not know, is placed nowhere already (`confine`)
fun lands_on_frame(w: *Walk, t: *Touch) bool {
    if (!t.writes || !in_frame(w, ?t.at)) { ret false; }
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < w.saves.len) {
        if (may_alias(w, ?w.saves.data[i], ?t.at)) { ret true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# whether touch `t`, which the walk places in the frame and no access seed states, reads bytes below the stack
# pointer's value on entry the function has not written, which may hold what an earlier call left, a secret among it:
# where no store of the function's own placed exactly there wrote them, nor a declassify point made them public. an inline
# block's touch past the function's own frame is placed nowhere already (`confine`), and what the convention passes
# above it, its incoming arguments, is seeded as its declaration states. an access the producer states reads what its
# extents hold, as the type it reads through says what the bytes are
fun unwritten(p: *Point, t: *Touch) bool {
    if (t.seeded)                         { ret false; }
    if (t.at.indexed || t.at.length == 0) { ret true; }
    if (t.at.offset >= 0)                 { ret false; }
    var below: Held = t.at;
    if (t.at.offset + t.at.length::i64 > 0) { below.length = (0 - t.at.offset)::u64; }
    ret !covered(?below, ?p.written) && !covered(?below, ?p.public);
}

# whether a store of a secret through touch `t`, which no access seed or pointer seed states, is refused: one the walk
# places in the frame follows the extent rule, as one off a symbol does into a global a seed states secret, and every
# other is memory whose secrecy nothing states, which a type may call public
fun unstated(w: *Walk, t: *Touch) bool {
    if (in_frame(w, ?t.at)) { ret false; }
    if (symbolic(?t.at))    { ret !secret_global(w, ?t.at); }
    ret true;
}

# whether every byte of `at`, off a symbol, lies in a global a symbol seed states secret, one of no stated length
# covering every byte off its symbol
fun secret_global(w: *Walk, at: *Held) bool {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < w.secrets.len) {
        val sd: Seed = w.secrets.at[i];
        i = i + 1;
        if (sel sd.symbol) {
            val g: Global = sd.symbol;
            if (g.symbol != at.symbol || at.slot)                                                                                 { cnt; }
            if (g.length == 0)                                                                                                    { ret true; }
            if (at.length != 0 && !at.indexed && at.offset >= g.offset && at.offset + at.length::i64 <= g.offset + g.length::i64) { ret true; }
        }
    }
    ret false;
}

# register row `row` and every row sharing storage with it marked in `into`, one bit per row
fun mark_overlapping(w: *Walk, row: u32, into: *u64) err[A.Error] {
    set_bit(into, row, true);
    val span: res[register.Span, A.Error] = register.overlapping(?w.overlaps, row);
    if (sel span.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{span.err}; }
    var k: u32 = 0;
    for (k < span.ok.count) {
        set_bit(into, w.overlaps.rows.data[span.ok.first + k], true);
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# the rows of each register a switch of the set reads its state from marked in `w.moding`, the timing mode's state
fun index_modes(w: *Walk) err[A.Error] {
    val all: mswitch.Switches = w.code.set.switches;
    var i:   u32              = 0;
    for (i < all.len) {
        val reads: mswitch.Steps = all.at[i].read;
        var n:     u32           = 0;
        for (n < reads.len) {
            val step: *mswitch.Step = ?reads.at[n];
            var o:    u32           = 0;
            for (o < step.values.len) {
                val src: mswitch.Source = step.values.at[o];
                if (sel src.value) {
                    val v: operand.Value = src.value;
                    if (sel v.register) {
                        val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, v.register);
                        if (sel row.some) {
                            val err_marked: err[A.Error] = mark_overlapping(w, row.some, w.moding.data);
                            if (sel err_marked.err) { ret err_marked; }
                        }
                    }
                }
                o = o + 1;
            }
            n = n + 1;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# whether `ins` at `at` changes the timing mode where it is none of the code's own switches of it: it writes a register
# a switch of the set reads the state from, or it is of a row a switch's set takes and given another immediate than the
# set gives it there, as `msr dit, #0` where the set is `msr dit, #1`
fun switches_mode(w: *Walk, at: usize, ins: *codec.Decoded, fp: *footprint.Footprint) bool {
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < w.switches.len) {
        if (w.switches.data[k] == at::u64) { ret false; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    var word: usize = 0;
    for (word < w.words) {
        if (((fp.written.data[word] | fp.clobbers.data[word]) & w.moding.data[word]) != 0) { ret true; }
        word = word + 1;
    }
    val all: mswitch.Switches = w.code.set.switches;
    var i:   u32              = 0;
    for (i < all.len) {
        val sets: mswitch.Steps = all.at[i].set;
        var n:    u32           = 0;
        for (n < sets.len) {
            val step: *mswitch.Step = ?sets.at[n];
            n = n + 1;
            if (row.at(w.code.set.codec.rows, step.row) != ins.inst.row) { cnt; }
            var o: u32 = 0;
            for (o < step.values.len && o < ins.inst.count) {
                val src: mswitch.Source = step.values.at[o];
                if (sel src.value) {
                    val v: operand.Value = src.value;
                    val g: operand.Value = ins.inst.values[o];
                    if (sel v.immediate) {
                        if (!(sel g.immediate))         { ret true; }
                        if (g.immediate != v.immediate) { ret true; }
                    }
                }
                o = o + 1;
            }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# whether `ins` leaves a secret in `p` in a row of a register the seeds state no instruction may leave one in, one it
# writes or clobbers
fun leaves_fixed(w: *Walk, p: *Point, fp: *footprint.Footprint) bool {
    var word: usize = 0;
    for (word < w.words) {
        if (((fp.written.data[word] | fp.clobbers.data[word]) & w.fixing.data[word] & p.taint.data[word]) != 0) { ret true; }
        word = word + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# touch `t` of the instruction walked placed in the frame range a within seed naming it states, known only to lie within
# it, or exactly there when the range is no longer than what it touches, in place of where its address places it
fun take_within(w: *Walk, t: *Touch) {
    var i: u32 = w.stated.data[w.at];
    for (i != NO_POINT) {
        val sd: Seed = w.secrets.at[i];
        if (sel sd.within) {
            var a: Access = Access{at: sd.within.at, access: sd.within.access, secret: false};
            if (names_touch(w, ?a, t)) {
                val whole: bool = t.at.length != 0 && t.at.length >= sd.within.length;
                t.at      = Held{base: w.stack, version: ENTRY, symbol: operand.NO_SYMBOL, slot: false, offset: sd.within.offset, length: sd.within.length, indexed: false, apart: false, within: !whole};
                t.rebased = 0;
            }
        }
        i = w.sowing.data[i];
    }
}

# touch `t` of the instruction walked, where it is an inline block's, taken as placed nowhere when the walk places it in
# the frame other than below the stack pointer's value on entry, at an offset and of a length it knows: the block may
# form an address past the function's own frame into its caller's, which the function was never handed, so what it
# reads there holds a secret and a secret it stores there is refused (`unstated`), as of memory nothing states
fun confine(w: *Walk, t: *Touch) {
    if (!in_frame(w, ?t.at) || !inlined(w, w.at))                                                 { ret; }
    if (!t.at.indexed && !t.at.within && t.at.length != 0 && t.at.offset + t.at.length::i64 <= 0) { ret; }
    t.at      = UNPLACED;
    t.rebased = 0;
}

# whether an inline seed names the instruction starting at `at`
fun inlined(w: *Walk, at: usize) bool {
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < w.inlined.len) {
        if (w.inlined.data[k] == at::u64) { ret true; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# whether each access seed and within seed at the instruction walked names one of its touches, placed or not
fun accessed(w: *Walk) bool {
    var i: u32 = w.stated.data[w.at];
    for (i != NO_POINT) {
        val sd: Seed = w.secrets.at[i];
        if (sel sd.access || sel sd.within) {
            var a: Access = Access{at: 0, access: Accessor.index{NO_ACCESS}, secret: false};
            if (sel sd.access) { a = sd.access; }
            if (sel sd.within) { a = Access{at: sd.within.at, access: sd.within.access, secret: false}; }
            var found: bool  = false;
            var k:     usize = 0;
            for (k < w.touches.len) {
                if (names_touch(w, ?a, ?w.touches.data[k])) { found = true; }
                k = k + 1;
            }
            if (!found) { ret false; }
        }
        i = w.sowing.data[i];
    }
    ret true;
}

# whether touch `t` reads what may hold a secret under `p`: what the extents say for one the walk places, whatever its
# seed states, else what its access seed states, else a secret but where a declassify point made it public
fun reads_secret(w: *Walk, p: *Point, t: *Touch) bool {
    if (!t.reads) { ret false; }
    if (pinned(w, ?t.at)) {
        if (secret_at(w, p, ?t.at)) { ret true; }
        ret in_frame(w, ?t.at) && unwritten(p, t);
    }
    if (t.seeded) { ret t.secret; }
    ret !made_public(p, ?t.at);
}

# whether every byte of `at` is of an extent a declassify point made public under `p`
fun made_public(p: *Point, at: *Held) bool {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < p.public.len) {
        if (inside(at, ?p.public.data[i])) { ret true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# whether a relation of `ins` takes memory operand `op` as the address it writes, as lea's, which forms the address and
# accesses nothing there
fun forms_only(ins: *codec.Decoded, op: u8) bool {
    val e: *effect.Effect = ins.inst.row.effect;
    if (e == nil) { ret false; }
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < e.relations.len) {
        val h: effect.Holds = e.relations.at[i].holds;
        if (sel h.offset) {
            val from: effect.Source = h.offset.from;
            if (sel from.base) {
                if (from.base == op) { ret true; }
            }
        }
        or (sel h.formed) {
            if (h.formed == op) { ret true; }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# the memory accesses of `ins` gathered into `w.touches`: each its footprint states, then each memory operand none of
# them names and no relation takes as the address it forms, as lea's. a secret in what forms an address or a value
# popped as one, or in what decides its count of elements, is refused, a lea's included
fun touches(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *codec.Decoded, fp: *footprint.Footprint) res[opt[ct.Refusal], A.Error] {
    vector.truncate[Touch](?w.touches, 0);
    val r: *operand.Operand = ins.inst.row.operands.at;
    var i: u32              = 0;
    for (i < fp.memory.len) {
        val acc:  *effect.Access = ?fp.memory.at[i];
        var role: operand.Role   = acc.role;
        if (role == operand.NONE && acc.operand != field.NO_OPERAND && acc.operand::u32 < ins.inst.count) { role = r[acc.operand].role; }
        var t: Touch = Touch{reads: (role & operand.READ) != 0, writes: (role & operand.WRITE) != 0, operand: field.NO_OPERAND, at: UNPLACED, row: effect.NO_ROW, rebased: 0, named: acc.operand, index: i, seeded: false, secret: false};
        placed(w, p, ins, acc.operand, acc.base, acc.forming, acc.offset, bytes_of(?acc.width), !sel acc.index.none, ?t);
        take_seed(w, p, ?t);
        take_within(w, ?t);
        confine(w, ?t);
        val indexed: opt[ct.Refusal] = index_secret(w, p, ins, ?acc.index);
        if (sel indexed.some)                                                          { ret found(indexed.some); }
        if (names_secret(w, p, ins, acc.operand))                                      { ret found(ct.refusal(ct.MEMORY, acc.operand)); }
        if (acc.base != effect.NO_ROW && bit_of(p.taint.data, acc.base))               { ret found(ct.refusal(ct.MEMORY, field.NO_OPERAND)); }
        if (acc.governor != field.NO_OPERAND && names_secret(w, p, ins, acc.governor)) { ret found(ct.refusal(ct.MEMORY, acc.governor)); }
        if (popped_secret(p, acc.pop))                                                 { ret found(ct.refusal(ct.MEMORY, field.NO_OPERAND)); }
        val counted: opt[ct.Refusal] = count_secret(w, p, ins, acc.width.count);
        if (sel counted.some) { ret found(counted.some); }
        var k: u32 = 0;
        for (k < ins.inst.count && k < 32) {
            if ((acc.forming & (1::u32 << k)) != 0 && names_secret(w, p, ins, k::u8)) { ret found(ct.refusal(ct.MEMORY, k::u8)); }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Touch](?w.touches, t);
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret failed[opt[ct.Refusal]](pushed.err); }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    var op: u32 = 0;
    for (op < ins.inst.count) {
        val v: operand.Value = ins.inst.values[op];
        if (sel v.memory) {
            var stated: bool = false;
            var k:      u32  = 0;
            for (k < fp.memory.len) {
                if (fp.memory.at[k].operand::u32 == op) { stated = true; }
                k = k + 1;
            }
            if (names_secret(w, p, ins, op::u8)) { ret found(ct.refusal(ct.MEMORY, op::u8)); }
            if (!stated && !forms_only(ins, op::u8)) {
                val role: operand.Role = r[op].role;
                var t:    Touch        = Touch{reads: (role & operand.READ) != 0, writes: (role & operand.WRITE) != 0, operand: field.NO_OPERAND, at: UNPLACED, row: effect.NO_ROW, rebased: 0, named: op::u8, index: NO_ACCESS, seeded: false, secret: false};
                placed(w, p, ins, op::u8, effect.NO_ROW, 0, 0, operand_bytes(?r[op], v.memory), false, ?t);
                take_seed(w, p, ?t);
                take_within(w, ?t);
                confine(w, ?t);
                val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Touch](?w.touches, t);
                if (sel pushed.err) { ret failed[opt[ct.Refusal]](pushed.err); }
            }
        }
        op = op + 1;
    }
    ret res[opt[ct.Refusal], A.Error].ok{opt[ct.Refusal].none{}};
}

# the latency refusal of a secret in an input of `ins`, none when its timing depends on no input holding one under the
# walk's timing context, as `ct.latency` decides for each: an operand it reads, the data of a memory operand it reads, the
# data of an access no operand names, and a register no operand names that it reads, but one it accrues flags into
fun latency(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *codec.Decoded, fp: *footprint.Footprint, secret: u32) opt[ct.Refusal] {
    val c:  *ct.Class        = ins.inst.row.ct;
    val r:  *operand.Operand = ins.inst.row.operands.at;
    var op: u32              = 0;
    for (op < ins.inst.count && op < 32) {
        if ((r[op].role & operand.READ) != 0) {
            var held: bool  = (secret & (1::u32 << op)) != 0;
            var k:    usize = 0;
            for (k < w.touches.len) {
                val t: *Touch = ?w.touches.data[k];
                if (t.operand::u32 == op && reads_secret(w, p, t)) { held = true; }
                k = k + 1;
            }
            if (held) {
                val refused: opt[ct.Refusal] = ct.latency(c, w.timing, w.file, ct.Input.operand{op::u8});
                if (sel refused.some) { ret refused; }
            }
        }
        op = op + 1;
    }
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < w.touches.len) {
        val t: *Touch = ?w.touches.data[k];
        if (t.operand == field.NO_OPERAND && reads_secret(w, p, t)) {
            val refused: opt[ct.Refusal] = ct.latency(c, w.timing, w.file, ct.Input.access{});
            if (sel refused.some) { ret refused; }
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    var word: usize = 0;
    for (word < w.words) {
        # a row an instruction adds its flags to is read only to keep them, which its timing never depends on
        var pending: u64 = unaccrued(w, fp.reads.data[word] & ~w.named.data[word] & p.taint.data[word], word, fp.written.data[word]);
        for (pending != 0) {
            val row: u32 = word::u32 * 64 + bits.ctz(pending)::u32;
            pending = pending & (pending - 1);
            val refused: opt[ct.Refusal] = ct.latency(c, w.timing, w.file, ct.Input.register{register.id_of(?w.file.registers[row])});
            if (sel refused.some) { ret refused; }
        }
        word = word + 1;
    }
    ret opt[ct.Refusal].none{};
}

# the first operand of `ins` whose registers hold a secret, field.NO_OPERAND when none does
fun first_secret(secret: u32, count: u32) u8 {
    var op: u32 = 0;
    for (op < count && op < 32) {
        if ((secret & (1::u32 << op)) != 0) { ret op::u8; }
        op = op + 1;
    }
    ret field.NO_OPERAND;
}

# the control refusal of `ins`: a transfer that may fall through decided by a secret, or one to a target formed from
# one. `held` is whether what it reads but the values it pops is secret, and `stacked` whether a value it pops is.
# the values a transfer pops decide it only through the condition and the chooser its effect names, but for a
# conditional or indirect one that names neither, which every value it reads may decide
fun control(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *codec.Decoded, c: *effect.Control, held: bool, stacked: bool, secret: u32) opt[ct.Refusal] {
    if (c.transfer == effect.NONE || c.transfer == effect.MERGE) { ret opt[ct.Refusal].none{}; }
    if (c.conditional) {
        if (c.condition != 0) {
            if (popped_secret(p, c.condition)) { ret opt[ct.Refusal].some{ct.refusal(ct.CONTROL, field.NO_OPERAND)}; }
        }
        or (held || stacked) { ret opt[ct.Refusal].some{ct.refusal(ct.CONTROL, first_secret(secret, ins.inst.count))}; }
    }
    if (popped_secret(p, c.chooses)) { ret opt[ct.Refusal].some{ct.refusal(ct.CONTROL, field.NO_OPERAND)}; }
    if (c.target == effect.INDIRECT || (c.target == effect.UNTARGETED && c.transfer == effect.RETURN)) {
        if (c.operand == field.NO_OPERAND) {
            var decided: bool = held;
            if (c.target == effect.INDIRECT && c.chooses == 0) { decided = held || stacked; }
            if (decided)                                       { ret opt[ct.Refusal].some{ct.refusal(ct.CONTROL, field.NO_OPERAND)}; }
            ret opt[ct.Refusal].none{};
        }
        if (names_secret(w, p, ins, c.operand)) { ret opt[ct.Refusal].some{ct.refusal(ct.CONTROL, c.operand)}; }
        var k: usize = 0;
        for (k < w.touches.len) {
            val t: *Touch = ?w.touches.data[k];
            if (t.operand == c.operand && reads_secret(w, p, t)) { ret opt[ct.Refusal].some{ct.refusal(ct.CONTROL, c.operand)}; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
    }
    ret opt[ct.Refusal].none{};
}

# whether `a` and `b` are one type of a signature: one fixed type, one variable or one operand's types, or those less
# the last
fun same_ref(a: effect.TypeRef, b: effect.TypeRef) bool {
    if (sel a.fixed)    { ret sel b.fixed && b.fixed == a.fixed; }
    if (sel a.variable) { ret sel b.variable && b.variable == a.variable; }
    if (sel a.operand)  { ret sel b.operand && b.operand == a.operand; }
    if (sel a.less)     { ret sel b.less && b.less == a.less; }
    if (sel a.results)  { ret sel b.results; }
    ret false;
}

# whether the `pushed` values of type `ref` a jump pushes are the first of the `popped` values of type `pop` it pops,
# so they stay as they were
fun kept_of(ref: effect.TypeRef, pushed: usize, pop: effect.TypeRef, popped: usize) bool {
    if (sel ref.less) {
        if (sel pop.operand) { ret ref.less == pop.operand && pushed + 1 == popped; }
    }
    ret same_ref(pop, ref) && popped == pushed;
}

# whether type `ref` of a signature is one it pushes again, of `sig`'s pushes
fun pushed_again(sig: *effect.Signature, ref: effect.TypeRef) bool {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < sig.pushes.len) {
        if (same_ref(sig.pushes.at[i], ref)) { ret true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# how many values the shape `s` of an instruction of signature `sig` pops
fun pop_count(w: *Walk, s: *Shape, sig: *effect.Signature) usize {
    var n: usize = 0;
    var i: u32   = 0;
    for (i < sig.pops.len) {
        n = n + w.counts.data[s.counts + i]::usize;
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret n;
}

# the key of the entry operand `op` of `ins` names, none for an operand holding no id
fun entry_key(ins: *codec.Decoded, op: u8) opt[u64] {
    if (op::u32 >= ins.inst.count || op::u32 >= ins.inst.row.operands.len) { ret opt[u64].none{}; }
    val shape: *operand.Shape = ?ins.inst.row.operands.at[op].shape;
    val v:     operand.Value  = ins.inst.values[op];
    if (sel shape.id) {
        if (sel v.id) { ret opt[u64].some{key(shape.id.space, v.id)}; }
    }
    ret opt[u64].none{};
}

# whether an entry `ins` reads through its operands may hold a secret under `p`. an operand holding no id may name
# any entry
fun entries_read(p: *Point, ins: *codec.Decoded, fp: *footprint.Footprint) bool {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < fp.entries.len) {
        val n: *effect.Entry = ?fp.entries.at[i];
        if ((n.role & operand.READ) != 0) {
            val k: opt[u64] = entry_key(ins, n.operand);
            if (sel k.some) {
                if (entry_secret(p, k.some)) { ret true; }
            }
            or (any_entry(p)) { ret true; }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# the values of the pop of `sig` of type `ref` copied into `w.carried`, the deepest first, from the pops of shape `s`
# on top of `p`'s stack, none when the instruction pops no value of that type
fun carry(w: *Walk, p: *Point, s: *Shape, sig: *effect.Signature, ref: effect.TypeRef) err[A.Error] {
    vector.truncate[bool](?w.carried, 0);
    var at: usize = p.stack.len - pop_count(w, s, sig);
    var i:  u32   = 0;
    for (i < sig.pops.len) {
        val n: usize = w.counts.data[s.counts + i]::usize;
        if (same_ref(sig.pops.at[i], ref)) {
            var k: usize = 0;
            for (k < n) {
                val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[bool](?w.carried, p.stack.data[at + k]);
                if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
                k = k + 1;
            }
            ret err[A.Error].ok{};
        }
        at = at + n;
        i  = i + 1;
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# what an instruction of a typed stream leaves secret, applied to `p`: the entries it writes take `value`, and its pops
# are replaced on the stack, by the params an opening instruction passes into its block as they are, else by its
# pushes, each a value a jump pops of the same type and count as it pushes, as br_if leaves the values its label
# takes, or the first of those it pops where it pushes them less the last, as br_on_non_null, kept as it was, and every
# other taking `value`. a call, whose callee the walk does not read, leaves what it
# pushes, every entry and every address secret when anything is, unless `model` states its callee, when `value` is its
# join: what it pushes takes that, `modeled` has left the memory, and every entry a callee reaches takes it too
fun apply_stream(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *codec.Decoded, fp: *footprint.Footprint, s: *Shape, value: bool, model: *Call) err[A.Error] {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < fp.entries.len) {
        val n: *effect.Entry = ?fp.entries.at[i];
        if ((n.role & operand.WRITE) != 0) {
            val k: opt[u64] = entry_key(ins, n.operand);
            rewritten(p, k);
            if (sel k.some) {
                val set: err[A.Error] = set_entry(p, k.some, value);
                if (sel set.err) { ret set; }
            }
            # a write through an operand holding no id may reach any entry
            or (value) {
                p.except = true;
                vector.truncate[u64](?p.entries, 0);
            }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    val sig:    *effect.Signature = ?fp.signature;
    val bottom: usize             = p.stack.len - pop_count(w, s, sig);
    vector.truncate[bool](?w.popped, 0);
    var k: usize = bottom;
    for (k < p.stack.len) {
        val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[bool](?w.popped, p.stack.data[k]);
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    vector.truncate[bool](?p.stack, bottom);
    if (effect.opens(fp.structure)) {
        var at: usize = 0;
        i = 0;
        for (i < sig.pops.len) {
            val n: usize = w.counts.data[s.counts + i]::usize;
            if (pushed_again(sig, sig.pops.at[i])) {
                k = 0;
                for (k < n) {
                    val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[bool](?p.stack, w.popped.data[at + k]);
                    if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
                    k = k + 1;
                }
            }
            at = at + n;
            i  = i + 1;
        }
        ret err[A.Error].ok{};
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < sig.pushes.len) {
        val n:    usize          = w.counts.data[s.counts + sig.pops.len + i]::usize;
        val ref:  effect.TypeRef = sig.pushes.at[i];
        var from: usize          = NO_OFFSET;
        if (fp.control.transfer == effect.JUMP) {
            var at: usize = 0;
            var j:  u32   = 0;
            for (j < sig.pops.len) {
                val m: usize = w.counts.data[s.counts + j]::usize;
                if (kept_of(ref, n, sig.pops.at[j], m)) { from = at; }
                at = at + m;
                j  = j + 1;
            }
        }
        k = 0;
        for (k < n) {
            var held: bool = value;
            if (from != NO_OFFSET) { held = w.popped.data[from + k]; }
            val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[bool](?p.stack, held);
            if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    if (fp.control.transfer == effect.CALL && model != nil) {
        if (value) { ret share_entries(w, p); }
        ret err[A.Error].ok{};
    }
    if (fp.control.transfer == effect.CALL) {
        var secret: bool = value || p.anywhere || p.held.len > 0 || any_entry(p);
        k = 0;
        for (k < p.stack.len) {
            if (p.stack.data[k]) { secret = true; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        var word: usize = 0;
        for (word < w.words) {
            if (p.taint.data[word] != 0) { secret = true; }
            word = word + 1;
        }
        if (secret) {
            k = p.stack.len - push_count(w, s, sig);
            for (k < p.stack.len) {
                p.stack.data[k] = true;
                k               = k + 1;
            }
            p.except = true;
            vector.truncate[u64](?p.entries, 0);
            vector.truncate[Held](?p.public, 0);
            everywhere(p);
        }
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# how many values the shape `s` of an instruction of signature `sig` pushes
fun push_count(w: *Walk, s: *Shape, sig: *effect.Signature) usize {
    var n: usize = 0;
    var i: u32   = 0;
    for (i < sig.pushes.len) {
        n = n + w.counts.data[s.counts + sig.pops.len + i]::usize;
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret n;
}

# what `ins` leaves secret, applied to `p`: its writes take whether anything it reads is secret, but a register `moves`
# derives, which takes its inputs', in every row overlapping a register written, a row the write leaves part of keeping
# that part's old secret, and its stores hold the extent they write. a store through a memory operand whose data is
# several register operands of one width that together cover its extent, as aarch64 stp, writes them in operand order
# at ascending addresses, so each part takes its own register's secret (`Parts`), and a load of the same shape leaves
# each register what its own part holds. a register written holds no known offset from the
# stack pointer after it but where `moves` gives one. a call, whose callee the walk does not read, leaves every register
# and every address secret when anything is, and no register of a known offset, unless `model` states its callee, as
# `modeled` applies with `joined` its join
fun apply(w: *Walk, p: *Point, at: usize, ins: *codec.Decoded, fp: *footprint.Footprint, value: bool, model: *Call, joined: bool) err[A.Error] {
    val version: u64   = at::u64 * 2 + 1;
    var data:    Parts = NO_PARTS;
    var store:   usize = w.touches.len;
    var loaded:  Parts = NO_PARTS;
    var split:   bool  = false;
    var t_at:    usize = 0;
    for (t_at < w.touches.len) {
        val t: *Touch = ?w.touches.data[t_at];
        if (t.writes && store == w.touches.len) {
            val d: Parts = parts_of(w, p, ins, operand.READ, t.row);
            if (splits(?d, t)) {
                data  = d;
                store = t_at;
            }
        }
        if (t.reads && !t.writes && !split) { loaded = parts_of(w, p, ins, operand.WRITE, t.row); }
        if (t.reads && !t.writes && !split && splits(?loaded, t)) {
            var n: u32 = 0;
            for (n < loaded.count) {
                var part: Touch = @t;
                part.at.offset   = t.at.offset + (n::u64 * loaded.bytes)::i64;
                part.at.length   = loaded.bytes;
                loaded.secret[n] = reads_secret(w, p, ?part);
                n                = n + 1;
            }
            split = true;
        }
        t_at = t_at + 1;
    }
    val moved: err[A.Error] = moves(w, p, ins, fp);
    if (sel moved.err) { ret moved; }
    val formed: err[A.Error] = formings(w, p, ins);
    if (sel formed.err) { ret formed; }
    if (model != nil) {
        val saving: err[A.Error] = save_stack(w, p);
        if (sel saving.err) { ret saving; }
    }
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < w.file.register_count) {
        val written: bool = bit_of(fp.written.data, i) || bit_of(fp.clobbers.data, i);
        # a write through a register reading zero is discarded
        if (written && (w.file.registers[i].flags & register.ZERO) == 0) {
            var secret: bool = written_secret(w, i, value);
            if (split) {
                var n: u32 = 0;
                for (n < loaded.count) {
                    if (loaded.rows[n] == i) { secret = loaded.secret[n]; }
                    n = n + 1;
                }
            }
            val span: res[register.Span, A.Error] = register.overlapping(?w.overlaps, i);
            if (sel span.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{span.err}; }
            var k: u32 = 0;
            for (k < span.ok.count) {
                val o:   u32                = w.overlaps.rows.data[span.ok.first + k];
                val row: *register.Register = ?w.file.registers[o];
                if (stored(w, o)) {
                    if (footprint.kills(fp, register.id_of(row))) { set_bit(p.taint.data, o, secret); }
                    or (secret)                                   { set_bit(p.taint.data, o, true); }
                    p.versions.data[o] = version;
                    p.frames.data[o]   = UNKNOWN;
                    p.formed.data[o]   = UNFORMED;
                }
                k = k + 1;
            }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    var m: usize = 0;
    for (m < w.moved.len) {
        p.frames.data[w.moved.data[m].row] = w.moved.data[m].frame;
        m                                  = m + 1;
    }
    m = 0;
    for (m < w.forming.len) {
        p.formed.data[w.forming.data[m].row] = w.forming.data[m].formed;
        m                                    = m + 1;
    }
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < w.touches.len) {
        val t: *Touch = ?w.touches.data[k];
        if (t.writes && value && k == store) {
            var n: u32 = 0;
            for (n < data.count) {
                var part: Held = t.at;
                part.offset = t.at.offset + (n::u64 * data.bytes)::i64;
                part.length = data.bytes;
                if (exact(?part) && in_frame(w, ?part)) {
                    val err_wrote: err[A.Error] = gather(?p.written, part);
                    if (sel err_wrote.err) { ret err_wrote; }
                }
                if (data.secret[n]) {
                    unpublish(w, p, ?part);
                    val held: err[A.Error] = hold(w, p, part);
                    if (sel held.err) { ret held; }
                }
                or (exact(?part)) {
                    val made: err[A.Error] = publish(p, part);
                    if (sel made.err) { ret made; }
                }
                n = n + 1;
            }
        }
        or (t.writes && value) {
            if (exact(?t.at) && in_frame(w, ?t.at)) {
                val err_wrote: err[A.Error] = gather(?p.written, t.at);
                if (sel err_wrote.err) { ret err_wrote; }
            }
            unpublish(w, p, ?t.at);
            if (!located(?t.at)) { everywhere_typed(w, p); }
            or {
                val held: err[A.Error] = hold(w, p, t.at);
                if (sel held.err) { ret held; }
            }
        }
        or (t.writes && exact(?t.at)) {
            if (in_frame(w, ?t.at)) {
                val err_wrote: err[A.Error] = gather(?p.written, t.at);
                if (sel err_wrote.err) { ret err_wrote; }
            }
            val made: err[A.Error] = publish(p, t.at);
            if (sel made.err) { ret made; }
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    if (fp.control.transfer == effect.CALL && model != nil) {
        val made: err[A.Error] = modeled(w, p, version, model, joined);
        if (sel made.err) { ret made; }
    }
    or (fp.control.transfer == effect.CALL) {
        var secret: bool  = memory_secret(w, p);
        var word:   usize = 0;
        for (word < w.words) {
            if (p.taint.data[word] != 0) { secret = true; }
            word = word + 1;
        }
        i = 0;
        for (i < w.file.register_count) {
            if (stored(w, i)) {
                if (secret) { set_bit(p.taint.data, i, true); }
                p.versions.data[i] = version;
                p.frames.data[i]   = UNKNOWN;
                p.formed.data[i]   = UNFORMED;
            }
            i = i + 1;
        }
        if (secret) {
            everywhere(p);
            keep_private(w, p);
        }
    }
    val hooks: *config.Hooks = w.code.set.config;
    if (hooks != nil) {
        val est: config.Established = hooks.establish(ins.inst.row, operand.Values{at: ins.inst.values, len: ins.inst.count});
        if (sel est.sets)      { p.config = opt[config.State].some{est.sets}; }
        if (sel est.undecided) { p.config = opt[config.State].none{}; }
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# the data register operands of an instruction of one role, read or written whole, none a memory operand's, while
# each is of one width
# ---
# count:  how many, 0 where two differ in width or one is not a plain register of a row
# bytes:  the width of each
# rows:   the register row of each
# secret: whether each read may hold a secret under the point before the instruction
rec Parts {
    count:  u32;
    bytes:  u64;
    rows:   [16]u32;
    secret: [16]bool;
}

val NO_PARTS: Parts = Parts{count: 0, bytes: 0};

# the parts of an instruction of role `role` beside the register row `address` an access is addressed from, whose
# operand forms the address and holds no data
fun parts_of(w: *Walk, p: *Point, ins: *codec.Decoded, role: operand.Role, address: u32) Parts {
    var out: Parts        = NO_PARTS;
    val ops: row.Operands = ins.inst.row.operands;
    var op:  u32          = 0;
    for (op < ops.len && op < ins.inst.count) {
        val o: *operand.Operand = ?ops.at[op];
        val v: operand.Value    = ins.inst.values[op];
        if (sel o.shape.register && o.role == role) {
            if (!(sel v.register)) { ret NO_PARTS; }
            if (sel v.register) {
                val at: opt[u32] = row_index(w, v.register);
                if (sel at.none) { ret NO_PARTS; }
                if (at.some != address) {
                    var bits: u64 = o.width::u64;
                    if (bits == 0)                                     { bits = fixed_width(w, at.some); }
                    if (bits == 0 || bits % 8 != 0 || out.count == 16) { ret NO_PARTS; }
                    if (out.count > 0 && bits / 8 != out.bytes)        { ret NO_PARTS; }
                    out.rows[out.count]   = at.some;
                    out.secret[out.count] = tainted(w, p, v.register);
                    out.bytes             = bits / 8;
                    out.count             = out.count + 1;
                }
            }
        }
        op = op + 1;
    }
    ret out;
}

# the bits register row `at` holds where its class's width does not scale, 0 where it does
fun fixed_width(w: *Walk, at: u32) u64 {
    val q: quantity.Scaled = w.file.classes[w.file.registers[at].class].width;
    if (q.per != 0) { ret 0; }
    ret q.fixed::u64;
}

# whether access `t` moves the parts `d` names one after another: at a placed extent they cover exactly, two of them at
# least
fun splits(d: *Parts, t: *Touch) bool {
    if (d.count < 2)                     { ret false; }
    if (!located(?t.at) || t.at.indexed) { ret false; }
    ret t.at.length == d.count::u64 * d.bytes;
}

# the flags of word `k` of the rows an instruction reads only as flags some operand values leave as they were, as an
# x86 shift by a zero count leaves every flag: such a read reaches the flag's own write alone, which keeps its old
# secret as it is not killed, and no other value the instruction writes
fun kept_only(fp: *footprint.Footprint, k: usize) u64 {
    val kept: effect.Set = fp.flags.kept;
    if (k >= kept.len::usize) { ret 0; }
    var read: u64 = 0;
    if (k < fp.flags.read.len::usize) { read = fp.flags.read.words[k]; }
    ret kept.words[k] & ~read;
}

# rows `bits` of word `k` but those an instruction adds its flags to, as an fp status register, and writes (`written`,
# its written rows of word `k`): such a read reaches the row's own write alone, which keeps its old secret as an
# accrual does not kill it, and no other value it writes. a read of one the instruction does not write, as `frflags`
# or `mrs fpsr`, hands what it holds on and stays a read
fun unaccrued(w: *Walk, bits: u64, k: usize, written: u64) u64 {
    var left: u64 = bits;
    var b:    u32 = 0;
    for (b < 64 && left != 0) {
        val row: u32 = k::u32 * 64 + b;
        if ((bits & (1::u64 << b::u64)) != 0 && row < w.file.register_count) {
            if ((w.file.registers[row].flags & register.ACCRUED) != 0 && (written & (1::u64 << b::u64)) != 0) { left = left & ~(1::u64 << b::u64); }
        }
        b = b + 1;
    }
    ret left;
}

# the stack pointer's row and the rows lying within it, as they are under `p` where a call starts, into `w.saved`
fun save_stack(w: *Walk, p: *Point) err[A.Error] {
    vector.truncate[Saved](?w.saved, 0);
    if (w.stack == effect.NO_ROW) { ret err[A.Error].ok{}; }
    val span: res[register.Span, A.Error] = register.overlapping(?w.overlaps, w.stack);
    if (sel span.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{span.err}; }
    val sp: *register.Register = ?w.file.registers[w.stack];
    var k:  u32                = 0;
    for (k <= span.ok.count) {
        var o: u32 = w.stack;
        if (k < span.ok.count) { o = w.overlaps.rows.data[span.ok.first + k]; }
        if (o == w.stack || register.overwrites(w.file, sp, ?w.file.registers[o], opt[register.Extend].some{register.KEEP})) {
            val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Saved](?w.saved, Saved{row: o, taint: bit_of(p.taint.data, o), version: p.versions.data[o], frame: p.frames.data[o]});
            if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# the rows result piece `r` leaves in `p` after a call: its register and each row sharing storage with it public for a
# public piece and secret for a secret one where the call trusts its callee (`stated`), else as `joined`
fun result_rows(w: *Walk, p: *Point, r: *Result, stated: bool, joined: bool) err[A.Error] {
    val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, r.register);
    if (sel row.none) { ret err[A.Error].ok{}; }
    var secret: bool = joined;
    if (stated) { secret = r.secret; }
    if (secret) { ret taint_row(w, p, row.some); }
    val span: res[register.Span, A.Error] = register.overlapping(?w.overlaps, row.some);
    if (sel span.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{span.err}; }
    set_bit(p.taint.data, row.some, false);
    var k: u32 = 0;
    for (k < span.ok.count) {
        set_bit(p.taint.data, w.overlaps.rows.data[span.ok.first + k], false);
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# whether the register of a public piece of the function's own results, or a row sharing storage with it, holds a
# secret in `p`, where it returns or makes a tail call, or bytes of its result returned by reference its declaration
# states public may hold one, off the address register's value on entry
fun result_secret(w: *Walk, p: *Point) res[bool, A.Error] {
    var n: u32 = 0;
    for (n < w.results.len) {
        val r: *Result = ?w.results.at[n];
        n = n + 1;
        if (r.secret) { cnt; }
        val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, r.register);
        if (sel row.none)                   { cnt; }
        if (bit_of(p.taint.data, row.some)) { ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{true}; }
        val span: res[register.Span, A.Error] = register.overlapping(?w.overlaps, row.some);
        if (sel span.err) { ret res[bool, A.Error].err{span.err}; }
        var k: u32 = 0;
        for (k < span.ok.count) {
            if (bit_of(p.taint.data, w.overlaps.rows.data[span.ok.first + k])) { ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{true}; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
    }
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < w.results.memory.len) {
        val e:   *Extent  = ?w.results.memory.at[i];
        val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, e.base);
        i = i + 1;
        if (sel row.none) { ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{true}; }
        var h: Held = Held{base: row.some, version: ENTRY, symbol: operand.NO_SYMBOL, slot: false, offset: e.offset, length: e.length, indexed: false, apart: false};
        if (secret_at(w, p, ?h)) { ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{true}; }
    }
    ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{false};
}

# the rows of the registers `regs` names marked in `into`, cleared first: each row, and with `within` the rows lying
# within it, else every row sharing storage with it
fun mark_rows(w: *Walk, regs: *Registers, within: bool, into: *u64) err[A.Error] {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < w.words) {
        into[i] = 0;
        i       = i + 1;
    }
    var n: u32 = 0;
    for (n < regs.len) {
        val row: u32 = row_or_none(w, regs.at[n]);
        set_bit(into, row, true);
        val span: res[register.Span, A.Error] = register.overlapping(?w.overlaps, row);
        if (sel span.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{span.err}; }
        val by: *register.Register = ?w.file.registers[row];
        var k:  u32                = 0;
        for (k < span.ok.count) {
            val o: u32 = w.overlaps.rows.data[span.ok.first + k];
            if (!within || register.overwrites(w.file, by, ?w.file.registers[o], opt[register.Extend].some{register.KEEP})) { set_bit(into, o, true); }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        n = n + 1;
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# the extents `e` names placed under `p`, where a call starts, into `into`
fun place_extents(w: *Walk, p: *Point, e: *Extents, into: *vector.Vector[Held]) err[A.Error] {
    vector.truncate[Held](into, 0);
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < e.len) {
        val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Held](into, extent_held(w, p, ?e.at[i]));
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# extent `x` placed under `p`, where a call starts: off its base register's value, its local's, its symbol's address, or
# an absolute address the walk does not place
fun extent_held(w: *Walk, p: *Point, x: *Extent) Held {
    if (sel x.entry.some) { ret Held{base: x.entry.some.index, space: x.entry.some.space, version: ENTRY, symbol: operand.NO_SYMBOL, slot: false, offset: x.offset, length: x.length, indexed: false, apart: x.no_global}; }
    var h: Held = Held{base: effect.NO_ROW, version: ENTRY, symbol: x.symbol, slot: false, offset: x.offset, length: x.length, indexed: false, apart: false};
    if (x.base != register.NONE) { h = rebase(w, p, row_or_none(w, x.base), x.offset, x.length); }
    h.apart = x.no_global;
    ret h;
}

# whether every byte of `at` is one of an extent `w.kept` holds
fun in_kept(w: *Walk, at: *Held) bool {
    ret covered(at, ?w.kept);
}

# the join of a call and what it accepts
# ---
# secret:     whether an argument register, a value it pops, an extent it reads, or any memory it does not keep or entry a
#             callee reaches may hold a secret
# unaccepted: whether one of those the model does not state the callee accepts a secret in may: an argument register,
#             value it pops or read extent it does not accept, or, unless its reads are stated, memory it does not keep
#             that no accepted read holds whole, an address no statement types secret (`Point.untyped`) or an entry a
#             callee reaches
# pointed:    whether a pointer the callee's declaration states public points into a frame local that may hold a secret
rec Joined {
    secret:     bool;
    unaccepted: bool;
    pointed:    bool;
}

# whether model `c` accepts a secret in register `reg`
fun accepts(c: *Call, reg: register.Id) bool {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < c.accepted.len) {
        if (c.accepted.at[i] == reg) { ret true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# whether `x` and `y` name one entry or both none
fun same_entry(x: opt[Entry], y: opt[Entry]) bool {
    if (sel x.some) {
        if (sel y.some) { ret x.some.space == y.some.space && x.some.index == y.some.index; }
        ret false;
    }
    ret sel y.none;
}

# whether extents `x` and `y` are stated alike
fun same_extent(x: *Extent, y: *Extent) bool {
    ret x.base == y.base && x.symbol == y.symbol && x.offset == y.offset && x.length == y.length && x.no_global == y.no_global && same_entry(x.entry, y.entry);
}

# whether `positions` names the value at `depth`, the last bit standing for every value past it
fun names_depth(positions: operand.Positions, depth: usize) bool {
    var bit: usize = depth;
    if (bit > 31) { bit = 31; }
    ret ((positions >> bit::u32) & 1) != 0;
}

# whether model `c` names a popped value past the `popped` its call pops
fun named_past(c: *Call, popped: usize) bool {
    var within: operand.Positions = operand.ALL_POSITIONS;
    if (popped < 32) { within = (1::u32 << popped::u32) - 1; }
    ret (c.accepted_popped & ~within) != 0;
}

# whether model `c` accepts a secret in its read extent `x`
fun accepts_read(c: *Call, x: *Extent) bool {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < c.accepted_reads.len) {
        if (same_extent(?c.accepted_reads.at[i], x)) { ret true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

# whether an extent model `c` accepts a secret in holds every byte of `h` under `r`, where the call starts
fun accepted_whole(w: *Walk, r: *Point, c: *Call, h: *Held) res[bool, A.Error] {
    vector.truncate[Held](?w.accepted, 0);
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < c.accepted_reads.len) {
        val res_pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Held](?w.accepted, extent_held(w, r, ?c.accepted_reads.at[i]));
        if (sel res_pushed.err) { ret failed[bool](res_pushed.err); }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{covered(h, ?w.accepted)};
}

# the join of the call modeled by `c` under `r`, where it starts, popping `popped` values, and whether a secret reaches
# it through what it does not accept, its kept and written extents placed into `w.kept` and `w.wrote`. a callee whose
# reads are stated takes a secret in memory it does not keep and in an entry as secret, so those join it and are
# accepted
fun join(w: *Walk, r: *Point, c: *Call, popped: usize) res[Joined, A.Error] {
    val placed_kept: err[A.Error] = place_extents(w, r, ?c.kept, ?w.kept);
    if (sel placed_kept.err) { ret failed[Joined](placed_kept.err); }
    val placed_wrote: err[A.Error] = place_extents(w, r, ?c.writes, ?w.wrote);
    if (sel placed_wrote.err) { ret failed[Joined](placed_wrote.err); }
    var j: Joined = Joined{secret: false, unaccepted: false, pointed: false};
    var i: u32    = 0;
    for (i < c.arguments.len) {
        if (tainted(w, r, c.arguments.at[i])) {
            j.secret = true;
            if (!accepts(c, c.arguments.at[i])) { j.unaccepted = true; }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    var depth: usize = 0;
    for (depth < popped) {
        if (r.stack.data[r.stack.len - 1 - depth]) {
            j.secret = true;
            if (!names_depth(c.accepted_popped, depth)) { j.unaccepted = true; }
        }
        depth = depth + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < c.reads.len) {
        val h: Held = extent_held(w, r, ?c.reads.at[i]);
        if (secret_at(w, r, ?h)) {
            j.secret = true;
            if (!accepts_read(c, ?c.reads.at[i]) && !typed_held(w, r, ?h)) { j.unaccepted = true; }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    val shared: bool = shared_entry(w, r);
    if (r.anywhere || shared) {
        j.secret = true;
        if (!c.stated && (r.untyped || shared)) { j.unaccepted = true; }
    }
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < r.held.len) {
        if (!in_kept(w, ?r.held.data[k]) && !is_private(w, ?r.held.data[k])) {
            j.secret = true;
            if (!c.stated && !typed_held(w, r, ?r.held.data[k])) {
                val res_whole: res[bool, A.Error] = accepted_whole(w, r, c, ?r.held.data[k]);
                if (sel res_whole.err) { ret failed[Joined](res_whole.err); }
                if (!res_whole.ok)     { j.unaccepted = true; }
            }
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    vector.truncate[Held](?w.returned, 0);
    i = 0;
    for (i < c.results.memory.len) {
        val e:   *Extent  = ?c.results.memory.at[i];
        val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, e.base);
        if (sel row.some) {
            val h: Held = rebase(w, r, row.some, e.offset, e.length);
            if (!secret_at(w, r, ?h)) {
                val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Held](?w.returned, h);
                if (sel pushed.err) { ret failed[Joined](pushed.err); }
            }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < c.pointed.len) {
        val at: opt[u32] = row_index(w, c.pointed.at[i]);
        if (sel at.some) {
            val f: Frame = r.frames.data[at.some];
            if (on_stack(w, f) && pointed_secret(w, r, c, f.offset)) { j.pointed = true; }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret res[Joined, A.Error].ok{j};
}

# whether the frame local of `c`'s reads holding the byte at `offset` from the stack pointer's value on entry may hold
# a secret under `p`, the whole local, as a pointer into it may reach every byte of it, or that byte alone where no read
# names a local holding it
fun pointed_secret(w: *Walk, p: *Point, c: *Call, offset: i64) bool {
    var byte: Held = Held{base: w.stack, version: ENTRY, symbol: operand.NO_SYMBOL, slot: false, offset: offset, length: 1, indexed: false, apart: false};
    var i:    u32  = 0;
    for (i < c.reads.len) {
        val h: Held = extent_held(w, p, ?c.reads.at[i]);
        if (in_frame(w, ?h) && inside(?byte, ?h)) { ret secret_at(w, p, ?h); }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret secret_at(w, p, ?byte);
}

# the call modeled by `c`, whose own instruction `apply` has applied to `p`, leaving its callee's effects at `version`:
# a preserved row and a program counter's, the return point, keep what the instruction left and the stack pointer's
# rows what `w.saved` holds, a written row is secret but the rows of the result pieces its callee's declaration states
# (`result_rows`), as nothing states what a callee leaves in a register it may clobber, and a row it states neither is
# secret when anything is, as with no model, each of the others of the version and of no known offset. with `joined`
# every byte it does not keep may hold a secret, globals included, and every extent it writes does, but a typed frame
# extent a callee it trusts writes, which its own walk held to storing no secret through a pointer its type states
# public, and after a callee it does not trust no typed extent holds more than any other does, and what it writes
# where the walk does not place it in the frame may be a secret at an address no statement types
fun modeled(w: *Walk, p: *Point, version: u64, c: *Call, joined: bool) err[A.Error] {
    val keeping: err[A.Error] = mark_rows(w, ?c.preserved, true, w.keeping.data);
    if (sel keeping.err) { ret keeping; }
    val writing: err[A.Error] = mark_rows(w, ?c.written, false, w.writing.data);
    if (sel writing.err) { ret writing; }
    var secret: bool  = memory_secret(w, p);
    var word:   usize = 0;
    for (word < w.words) {
        if (p.taint.data[word] != 0) { secret = true; }
        word = word + 1;
    }
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < w.file.register_count) {
        val pc: bool = (w.file.registers[i].flags & register.PC) != 0;
        if (stored(w, i) && !pc && !bit_of(w.keeping.data, i)) {
            if (bit_of(w.writing.data, i)) { set_bit(p.taint.data, i, true); }
            or (secret)                    { set_bit(p.taint.data, i, true); }
            p.versions.data[i] = version;
            p.frames.data[i]   = UNKNOWN;
            p.formed.data[i]   = UNFORMED;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < w.saved.len) {
        val sv: *Saved = ?w.saved.data[k];
        set_bit(p.taint.data, sv.row, sv.taint);
        p.versions.data[sv.row] = sv.version;
        p.frames.data[sv.row]   = sv.frame;
        k                       = k + 1;
    }
    var n: u32 = 0;
    for (n < c.results.len) {
        val stated: err[A.Error] = result_rows(w, p, ?c.results.at[n], c.stated, joined);
        if (sel stated.err) { ret stated; }
        n = n + 1;
    }
    # the frame bytes the callee may write are written, by checked code or by code whose writes the model takes as it
    # states, and no longer what an earlier frame left there
    k = 0;
    for (k < w.wrote.len) {
        val h: *Held = ?w.wrote.data[k];
        if (in_frame(w, h) && !h.indexed && h.length != 0) {
            val err_wrote: err[A.Error] = gather(?p.written, @h);
            if (sel err_wrote.err) { ret err_wrote; }
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    if (!joined || c.keeps) { ret publish_returned(w, p); }
    if (!c.stated)          { p.untrusted = true; }
    var left: usize = 0;
    k = 0;
    for (k < p.public.len) {
        if (in_kept(w, ?p.public.data[k]) || is_private(w, ?p.public.data[k]) || (c.stated && is_typed(w, p, ?p.public.data[k]))) {
            p.public.data[left] = p.public.data[k];
            left                = left + 1;
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    vector.truncate[Held](?p.public, left);
    if (p.anywhere) {
        val narrowed: res[bool, A.Error] = narrow(w, ?p.spared, ?w.kept);
        if (sel narrowed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{narrowed.err}; }
    }
    or {
        everywhere_typed(w, p);
        k = 0;
        for (k < w.kept.len) {
            val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Held](?p.spared, w.kept.data[k]);
            if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
    }
    k = 0;
    for (k < w.wrote.len) {
        val h: Held = w.wrote.data[k];
        if (c.stated && is_typed(w, p, ?h)) {
            k = k + 1;
            cnt;
        }
        unpublish(w, p, ?h);
        if (!located(?h))                  { everywhere_typed(w, p); }
        or (!c.stated && !in_frame(w, ?h)) { everywhere(p); }
        or {
            val held: err[A.Error] = hold(w, p, h);
            if (sel held.err) { ret held; }
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret publish_returned(w, p);
}

# the bytes of a result returned by reference the trusted declaration states public, which the callee writes whether
# or not a secret joined the call
fun publish_returned(w: *Walk, p: *Point) err[A.Error] {
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < w.returned.len) {
        val made: err[A.Error] = publish(p, w.returned.data[k]);
        if (sel made.err) { ret made; }
        if (in_frame(w, ?w.returned.data[k])) {
            val err_wrote: err[A.Error] = gather(?p.written, w.returned.data[k]);
            if (sel err_wrote.err) { ret err_wrote; }
        }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

fun unread(message: str, at: usize) opt[Verdict] {
    ret opt[Verdict].some{Verdict.unread{Unread{message: message, offset: at::u64}}};
}

fun refused(r: ct.Refusal, at: usize) opt[Verdict] {
    ret opt[Verdict].some{Verdict.refused{Finding{offset: at::u64, refusal: r}}};
}

fun stays(at: usize) res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] {
    ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNBALANCED, at)};
}

# `p` reaching `to` from the instruction at `at`, unread when control joins there at another height of the stack
fun goes(w: *Walk, p: *Point, at: usize, to: usize) res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] {
    val reached: res[bool, A.Error] = reach(w, p, at, to);
    if (sel reached.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](reached.err); }
    if (!reached.ok)     { ret stays(at); }
    ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{opt[Verdict].none{}};
}

# where a branch to block `b` goes: a loop's start, else its close
fun label_of(b: *Block) usize {
    if (b.loops) { ret b.body; }
    ret b.close;
}

# the blocks the depths of the instruction of shape `s` at `at` name, each reached with `p` cut to its block's height
# and the values `w.carried` holds on top
fun branches(w: *Walk, p: *Point, at: usize, s: *Shape) res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < s.depths) {
        val b: *Block = ?w.blocks.data[w.targets.data[s.targets + i]];
        if (p.stack.len < b.base::usize) { ret stays(at); }
        val made: res[Point, A.Error] = copy(w, p);
        if (sel made.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](made.err); }
        var edge: Point = made.ok;
        vector.truncate[bool](?edge.stack, b.base::usize);
        var k: usize = 0;
        for (k < w.carried.len) {
            val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[bool](?edge.stack, w.carried.data[k]);
            if (sel pushed.err) {
                drop(?edge);
                ret failed[opt[Verdict]](pushed.err);
            }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        val went: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = goes(w, ?edge, at, label_of(b));
        drop(?edge);
        if (sel went.err)     { ret went; }
        if (sel went.ok.some) { ret went; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{opt[Verdict].none{}};
}

# the labels the clauses of the catching blocks from `s`'s catcher outward name, out to the first block taking every
# throw, each reached with `p` cut to its block's height and the clause's values on top, each secret when `secret`
fun raised(w: *Walk, p: *Point, at: usize, s: *Shape, secret: bool) res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] {
    var h: u32 = s.catcher;
    for (h != NO_BLOCK) {
        val catcher: Block = w.blocks.data[h];
        var i:       u32   = 0;
        for (i < catcher.catches) {
            val cl: Clause = w.clauses.data[catcher.clauses + i];
            val b:  *Block = ?w.blocks.data[cl.block];
            if (p.stack.len < b.base::usize) { ret stays(at); }
            val made: res[Point, A.Error] = copy(w, p);
            if (sel made.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](made.err); }
            var edge: Point = made.ok;
            vector.truncate[bool](?edge.stack, b.base::usize);
            var k: u32 = 0;
            for (k < cl.values) {
                val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[bool](?edge.stack, secret);
                if (sel pushed.err) {
                    drop(?edge);
                    ret failed[opt[Verdict]](pushed.err);
                }
                k = k + 1;
            }
            val went: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = goes(w, ?edge, at, label_of(b));
            drop(?edge);
            if (sel went.err)     { ret went; }
            if (sel went.ok.some) { ret went; }
            i = i + 1;
        }
        if (catcher.every) { brk; }
        h = catcher.outer;
    }
    ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{opt[Verdict].none{}};
}

# the instruction starts control reaches from `ins` at `at`, each reached with `p`: a typed stream's branch to the
# blocks its depths name or where the block it opens or splits goes on, a jump to its relative target, as its field
# holds it, the distance the builder laid out also for one it left to the linker to relax, but a tail call, `tail`, or
# a machine set's jump past the code's ends, which leave the function, the labels a catch takes what raises to, the
# values it leaves secret where `secret`, and the next instruction unless it jumps, returns or faults unconditionally
# or leaves the stack polymorphic
# ---
# ret: none when every one is in the code, else why the walk cannot follow it
fun successors(w: *Walk, p: *Point, at: usize, ins: *codec.Decoded, c: *effect.Control, s: *Shape, tail: bool, secret: bool) res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] {
    val next:  usize = at + ins.len;
    var falls: bool  = effect.falls(c);
    if (s != nil && s.stuck) { falls = false; }
    if (c.transfer == effect.JUMP && c.target == effect.DEPTH && s != nil) {
        val went: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = branches(w, p, at, s);
        if (sel went.err)     { ret went; }
        if (sel went.ok.some) { ret went; }
    }
    or (c.transfer == effect.JUMP && c.target == effect.STRUCTURED && s != nil && s.block != NO_BLOCK) {
        val b:  *Block = ?w.blocks.data[s.block];
        var to: usize  = b.close;
        if (effect.opens(ins.inst.row.effect.structure) && b.split != NO_OFFSET) { to = b.split + w.shapes.data[w.shaped.data[b.split]].len; }
        val went: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = goes(w, p, at, to);
        if (sel went.err)     { ret went; }
        if (sel went.ok.some) { ret went; }
    }
    or (c.transfer == effect.JUMP && !tail) {
        if (c.target != effect.DIRECT || c.operand == field.NO_OPERAND || c.operand::u32 >= ins.inst.count) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(INDIRECT, at)}; }
        val v: operand.Value = ins.inst.values[c.operand];
        if (!sel v.relative) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(NOWHERE, at)}; }
        var from:  i64           = at::i64;
        val shape: operand.Shape = ins.inst.row.operands.at[c.operand].shape;
        if (sel shape.relative && shape.relative.anchor == operand.END) { from = next::i64; }
        val to:  i64  = from + v.relative;
        val out: bool = to < 0 || to >= w.code.len::i64;
        if (s != nil && (out || w.shaped.data[to::usize] == NO_POINT)) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(NOWHERE, at)}; }
        if (!out) {
            val went: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = goes(w, p, at, to::usize);
            if (sel went.err)     { ret went; }
            if (sel went.ok.some) { ret went; }
        }
    }
    if (s != nil && effect.raises(c)) {
        val went: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = raised(w, p, at, s, secret);
        if (sel went.err)     { ret went; }
        if (sel went.ok.some) { ret went; }
    }
    if (falls && next < w.code.len) { ret falls_into(w, p, at, next); }
    ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{opt[Verdict].none{}};
}

# `h` added to the extents `p` knows public unless it knows it
fun publish(p: *Point, h: Held) err[A.Error] {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < p.public.len) {
        if (same(?p.public.data[i], ?h)) { ret err[A.Error].ok{}; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Held](?p.public, h);
    if (sel pushed.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{pushed.err}; }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# the extent `e` of the memory a declassify point names as the touch of the instruction walked formed from its base
# register and holding it whole would name it, or off its symbol as a touch the sites place holding it whole names it,
# a touch that writes for `writes` and else one that reads. none when no touch does, or `e` is of no register row or
# symbol, of no length, or off a symbol and stated to hold no global's bytes
fun held_by_touch(w: *Walk, e: *Extent, writes: bool) opt[Held] {
    if (e.symbol != operand.NO_SYMBOL && e.no_global) { ret opt[Held].none{}; }
    if (e.symbol != operand.NO_SYMBOL && e.base == register.NONE && e.length != 0) {
        val g: Held  = Held{base: effect.NO_ROW, version: ENTRY, symbol: e.symbol, slot: false, offset: e.offset, length: e.length, indexed: false, apart: false};
        var n: usize = 0;
        for (n < w.touches.len) {
            val t: *Touch = ?w.touches.data[n];
            if (((writes && t.writes) || (!writes && t.reads)) && inside(?g, ?t.at)) { ret opt[Held].some{g}; }
            n = n + 1;
        }
        ret opt[Held].none{};
    }
    val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, e.base);
    if (sel row.none)  { ret opt[Held].none{}; }
    if (e.length == 0) { ret opt[Held].none{}; }
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < w.touches.len) {
        val t: *Touch = ?w.touches.data[k];
        val h: Held   = Held{base: t.at.base, version: t.at.version, symbol: operand.NO_SYMBOL, slot: false, offset: e.offset + t.rebased, length: e.length, indexed: false, apart: e.no_global};
        if (t.row == row.some && ((writes && t.writes) || (!writes && t.reads)) && inside(?h, ?t.at)) { ret opt[Held].some{h}; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret opt[Held].none{};
}

# the frame slot `e` a declassify point names, off its base register's value under `pre`, the state where the
# instruction walked starts, when a touch of that instruction holds it whole, one that writes for `writes` and else one
# that reads, through whichever register. none when no touch does, or `e` is of no register row or of no length
fun held_by_frame(w: *Walk, pre: *Point, e: *Extent, writes: bool) opt[Held] {
    val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, e.base);
    if (sel row.none)  { ret opt[Held].none{}; }
    if (e.length == 0) { ret opt[Held].none{}; }
    var h: Held  = rebase(w, pre, row.some, e.offset, e.length);
    var k: usize = 0;
    h.apart = e.no_global;
    for (k < w.touches.len) {
        val t: *Touch = ?w.touches.data[k];
        if (((writes && t.writes) || (!writes && t.reads)) && inside(?h, ?t.at)) { ret opt[Held].some{h}; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret opt[Held].none{};
}

# whether `ins` reads, for `role` operand.READ, or writes, for operand.WRITE, the entry of key `k` through an operand
# holding its id
fun names_entry(ins: *codec.Decoded, fp: *footprint.Footprint, k: u64, role: operand.Role) bool {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < fp.entries.len) {
        val n: *effect.Entry = ?fp.entries.at[i];
        if ((n.role & role) != 0) {
            val got: opt[u64] = entry_key(ins, n.operand);
            if (sel got.some) {
                if (got.some == k) { ret true; }
            }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret false;
}

fun touched(ok: bool) res[bool, A.Error] {
    ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{ok};
}

# register row `row` made public in `p`, and every row a write through it extending as `extend` overwrites, as
# `register.overwrites` decides: KEEP for the rows lying within it, or what the write a point after it names leaves
fun publish_row(w: *Walk, p: *Point, row: u32, extend: opt[register.Extend]) err[A.Error] {
    set_bit(p.taint.data, row, false);
    val span: res[register.Span, A.Error] = register.overlapping(?w.overlaps, row);
    if (sel span.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{span.err}; }
    val by: *register.Register = ?w.file.registers[row];
    var k:  u32                = 0;
    for (k < span.ok.count) {
        val o: u32 = w.overlaps.rows.data[span.ok.first + k];
        if (register.overwrites(w.file, by, ?w.file.registers[o], extend)) { set_bit(p.taint.data, o, false); }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# the place of the declassify point `d` before `ins` made public in `r`, the state the instruction's reads are decided
# under: a register row it reads, an entry it reads through an operand holding its id, a value it pops, and with
# `memory` set, once `w.touches` holds its touches, an extent one it reads holds whole. a place of the other pass is
# left as it is
# ---
# ret: whether the instruction reads the place, false refusing the point
fun lift(w: *Walk, r: *Point, ins: *codec.Decoded, fp: *footprint.Footprint, s: *Shape, d: *Declassify, memory: bool) res[bool, A.Error] {
    val q: Place = d.place;
    if (sel q.memory) {
        if (!memory) { ret touched(true); }
        val h: opt[Held] = held_by_touch(w, ?q.memory, false);
        if (sel h.none) { ret touched(false); }
        val made: err[A.Error] = publish(r, h.some);
        if (sel made.err) { ret failed[bool](made.err); }
        ret touched(true);
    }
    if (sel q.frame) {
        if (!memory) { ret touched(true); }
        val h: opt[Held] = held_by_frame(w, r, ?q.frame, false);
        if (sel h.none) { ret touched(false); }
        val made: err[A.Error] = publish(r, h.some);
        if (sel made.err) { ret failed[bool](made.err); }
        ret touched(true);
    }
    if (memory) { ret touched(true); }
    if (sel q.register) {
        val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, q.register);
        if (sel row.none)                     { ret touched(false); }
        if (!bit_of(fp.reads.data, row.some)) { ret touched(false); }
        val made: err[A.Error] = publish_row(w, r, row.some, opt[register.Extend].some{register.KEEP});
        if (sel made.err) { ret failed[bool](made.err); }
        ret touched(true);
    }
    if (sel q.entry) {
        val k: u64 = key(q.entry.space, q.entry.index);
        if (!names_entry(ins, fp, k, operand.READ)) { ret touched(false); }
        val set: err[A.Error] = set_entry(r, k, false);
        if (sel set.err) { ret failed[bool](set.err); }
        ret touched(true);
    }
    if (sel q.value) {
        if (s == nil || q.value::usize >= pop_count(w, s, ?fp.signature)) { ret touched(false); }
        r.stack.data[r.stack.len - 1 - q.value::usize] = false;
        ret touched(true);
    }
    ret touched(false);
}

# the place of the declassify point `d` after `ins` made to hold no secret in `p`, the state the instruction leaves: a
# register row it writes, an entry it writes through an operand holding its id, a value of the `left` it leaves on top
# of the stack, and an extent one of its touches writes whole, known public until a secret may be stored there. a frame
# slot is placed off its base register under `pre`, the state where the instruction starts
# ---
# ret: whether the instruction writes the place, false refusing the point
fun clear(w: *Walk, p: *Point, pre: *Point, ins: *codec.Decoded, fp: *footprint.Footprint, d: *Declassify, left: usize) res[bool, A.Error] {
    val q: Place = d.place;
    if (sel q.memory) {
        val h: opt[Held] = held_by_touch(w, ?q.memory, true);
        if (sel h.none) { ret touched(false); }
        val made: err[A.Error] = publish(p, h.some);
        if (sel made.err) { ret failed[bool](made.err); }
        ret touched(true);
    }
    if (sel q.frame) {
        val h: opt[Held] = held_by_frame(w, pre, ?q.frame, true);
        if (sel h.none) { ret touched(false); }
        val made: err[A.Error] = publish(p, h.some);
        if (sel made.err) { ret failed[bool](made.err); }
        ret touched(true);
    }
    if (sel q.register) {
        val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, q.register);
        if (sel row.none)                                                              { ret touched(false); }
        if (!bit_of(fp.written.data, row.some) && !bit_of(fp.clobbers.data, row.some)) { ret touched(false); }
        var extend: opt[register.Extend] = opt[register.Extend].some{register.KEEP};
        var i:      usize                = 0;
        for (i < fp.writes.len) {
            if (fp.writes.data[i].at == q.register) {
                val wr: operand.Write = fp.writes.data[i].write;
                if (wr.result != 0 && wr.above == register.KEEP) { ret touched(false); }
                extend = wr.extend;
            }
            i = i + 1;
        }
        val made: err[A.Error] = publish_row(w, p, row.some, extend);
        if (sel made.err) { ret failed[bool](made.err); }
        ret touched(true);
    }
    if (sel q.entry) {
        val k: u64 = key(q.entry.space, q.entry.index);
        if (!names_entry(ins, fp, k, operand.WRITE)) { ret touched(false); }
        val set: err[A.Error] = set_entry(p, k, false);
        if (sel set.err) { ret failed[bool](set.err); }
        ret touched(true);
    }
    if (sel q.value) {
        if (q.value::usize >= left) { ret touched(false); }
        p.stack.data[p.stack.len - 1 - q.value::usize] = false;
        ret touched(true);
    }
    ret touched(false);
}

# whether the callee of the call walked may write register row `row`: every row but a program counter's and, with model
# `c`, what it preserves, as `modeled` leaves them. `c` is nil for no model
fun callee_writes(w: *Walk, c: *Call, row: u32) res[bool, A.Error] {
    if ((w.file.registers[row].flags & register.PC) != 0) { ret touched(false); }
    if (c == nil)                                         { ret touched(true); }
    val keeping: err[A.Error] = mark_rows(w, ?c.preserved, true, w.keeping.data);
    if (sel keeping.err) { ret failed[bool](keeping.err); }
    ret touched(!bit_of(w.keeping.data, row));
}

# the extent `e` as the call walked may write it, off its base register's value under `pre`, the state where the call
# starts, or off its symbol: with model `c` one it writes or does not keep, and with none any. none when it may not, or
# `e` is of no register row or symbol or of no length. `c` is nil for no model, and `join` has placed its extents
fun held_by_call(w: *Walk, pre: *Point, e: *Extent, c: *Call) opt[Held] {
    if (e.length == 0)      { ret opt[Held].none{}; }
    if (!entry_based(w, e)) { ret opt[Held].none{}; }
    if (e.base != register.NONE) {
        val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, e.base);
        if (sel row.none) { ret opt[Held].none{}; }
    }
    var h: Held = extent_held(w, pre, e);
    if (!located(?h)) { ret opt[Held].none{}; }
    if (c == nil)     { ret opt[Held].some{h}; }
    var k: usize = 0;
    for (k < w.wrote.len) {
        if (inside(?h, ?w.wrote.data[k])) { ret opt[Held].some{h}; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    if (in_kept(w, ?h)) { ret opt[Held].none{}; }
    ret opt[Held].some{h};
}

# the extent `h` made to hold a secret in `p`
# ---
# ret: whether there is one, false refusing the seed
fun stain(w: *Walk, p: *Point, h: opt[Held]) res[bool, A.Error] {
    if (sel h.none) { ret touched(false); }
    var at: Held = h.some;
    unpublish(w, p, ?at);
    val held: err[A.Error] = hold(w, p, at);
    if (sel held.err) { ret failed[bool](held.err); }
    ret touched(true);
}

# the place of the written seed `e` at `ins` made to hold a secret in `p`, the state the instruction leaves: a register
# row it writes, an entry it writes through an operand holding its id, a value of the `left` it leaves on top of the
# stack, and an extent one of its touches writes whole, each place `clear` takes after it. a call writes more than its
# footprint states, what `callee_writes` and `held_by_call` say, or any entry of a typed stream. `callee` is its model,
# nil for none, and a frame slot is placed off its base register under `pre`, the state where the instruction starts
# ---
# ret: whether the instruction writes the place, false refusing the seed
fun plant(w: *Walk, p: *Point, pre: *Point, ins: *codec.Decoded, fp: *footprint.Footprint, e: *Written, callee: *Call, left: usize) res[bool, A.Error] {
    val q:     Place = e.place;
    val calls: bool  = fp.control.transfer == effect.CALL || callee != nil;
    if (sel q.memory) {
        if (q.memory.base != register.NONE && q.memory.symbol != operand.NO_SYMBOL) { ret touched(false); }
        var h: opt[Held] = held_by_touch(w, ?q.memory, true);
        if (sel h.none && calls) { h = held_by_call(w, pre, ?q.memory, callee); }
        ret stain(w, p, h);
    }
    if (sel q.frame) {
        if (q.frame.symbol != operand.NO_SYMBOL) { ret touched(false); }
        var h: opt[Held] = held_by_frame(w, pre, ?q.frame, true);
        if (sel h.none && calls) { h = held_by_call(w, pre, ?q.frame, callee); }
        ret stain(w, p, h);
    }
    if (sel q.register) {
        val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, q.register);
        if (sel row.none)                                            { ret touched(false); }
        if ((w.file.registers[row.some].flags & register.ZERO) != 0) { ret touched(false); }
        var writes: bool = bit_of(fp.written.data, row.some) || bit_of(fp.clobbers.data, row.some);
        if (!writes && calls) {
            val by: res[bool, A.Error] = callee_writes(w, callee, row.some);
            if (sel by.err) { ret by; }
            writes = by.ok;
        }
        if (!writes) { ret touched(false); }
        val marked: err[A.Error] = taint_row(w, p, row.some);
        if (sel marked.err) { ret failed[bool](marked.err); }
        ret touched(true);
    }
    if (sel q.entry) {
        val k:      u64  = key(q.entry.space, q.entry.index);
        var writes: bool = names_entry(ins, fp, k, operand.WRITE);
        if (!writes && calls) { writes = callee == nil || !is_local(w, k); }
        if (!writes)          { ret touched(false); }
        val set: err[A.Error] = set_entry(p, k, true);
        if (sel set.err) { ret failed[bool](set.err); }
        ret touched(true);
    }
    if (sel q.value) {
        if (q.value::usize >= left) { ret touched(false); }
        p.stack.data[p.stack.len - 1 - q.value::usize] = true;
        ret touched(true);
    }
    ret touched(false);
}

# the declassify points before `ins` at `at` applied to `r`, its places of one pass as `lift` takes them
# ---
# ret: none when every one names a place the instruction reads, else the refusal of the first that does not
fun lifts(w: *Walk, r: *Point, at: usize, ins: *codec.Decoded, fp: *footprint.Footprint, s: *Shape, memory: bool) res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] {
    var i: u32 = w.declared.data[at];
    for (i != NO_POINT) {
        val d: *Declassify = ?w.public.at[i];
        if (sel d.side.before) {
            val ok: res[bool, A.Error] = lift(w, r, ins, fp, s, d, memory);
            if (sel ok.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](ok.err); }
            if (!ok.ok)     { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNTOUCHED, at)}; }
        }
        i = w.chain.data[i];
    }
    ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{opt[Verdict].none{}};
}

# the instruction at `at` walked from the state there. a declassify point before it makes its place public in a copy
# of that state its reads are decided under, one after it clears its place in the state it leaves, and a written seed
# there then makes its place secret in that state
# ---
# ret: a verdict when it ends the walk, none to go on
fun step(w: *Walk, at: usize, store: *vector.Vector[operand.Value], alts: *vector.Vector[requirement.Alternative], fp: *footprint.Footprint) res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] {
    val p: *Point = ?w.state;
    if (w.after.data[at] != NO_POINT || w.declared.data[at] != NO_POINT) {
        val err_pre: err[A.Error] = assign(?w.pre, p);
        if (sel err_pre.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](err_pre.err); }
    }
    val sowed: err[A.Error] = sow(w, p, at);
    if (sel sowed.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](sowed.err); }
    val got: res[codec.Decoded, field.Refusal] = codec.decode_grown(w.code.set.codec, w.ctx, w.code.data, w.code.len, at, store, alts);
    if (sel got.err) {
        if (sel got.err.cause.memory) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](got.err.cause.memory); }
        ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNDECODED, at)};
    }
    var ins: codec.Decoded = got.ok;
    w.at = at;
    compress.written(w.code.set.codec, w.code.set.compress, ?w.expanded, w.code.set.relax, w.ctx, ?ins.inst, ?w.written[0]);
    val cfg:    config.Configured                                = config.Configured{hooks: w.code.set.config, state: p.config};
    val values: operand.Values                                   = operand.Values{at: ins.inst.values, len: ins.inst.count};
    val foot:   res[query.Answer[*footprint.Footprint], A.Error] = footprint.of(fp, ins.inst.row, values, w.ctx, cfg);
    if (sel foot.err)          { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](foot.err); }
    if (sel foot.ok.undecided) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNDECIDED, at)}; }
    var stood: u32 = w.declared.data[at];
    for (stood != NO_POINT) {
        if (w.public.at[stood].length != ins.len::u64) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(MISPLACED, at)}; }
        stood = w.chain.data[stood];
    }
    var k: usize = at + 1;
    for (k < at + ins.len && k < w.code.len) {
        if (w.declared.data[k] != NO_POINT) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(MISPLACED, k)}; }
        if (w.called.data[k] != NO_POINT)   { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNCALLED, k)}; }
        if (w.sited.data[k] != NO_POINT)    { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSITED, k)}; }
        if (w.stated.data[k] != NO_POINT)   { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNACCESSED, k)}; }
        if (w.after.data[k] != NO_POINT)    { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, k)}; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    val jumps: bool = fp.control.transfer == effect.JUMP;
    var tail:  bool = jumps && fp.control.target == effect.FUNCTION;
    var n:     u32  = w.sited.data[at];
    for (n != NO_POINT && n < w.code.sites.len && w.code.sites.at[n].at == at::u64) {
        val made: u8 = built(w, w.code.sites.at[n].operand);
        if (made == field.NO_OPERAND)                                         { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSITED, at)}; }
        if (jumps && w.code.sites.at[n].leaves && made == fp.control.operand) { tail = true; }
        n = n + 1;
    }
    var model: *Call = nil;
    if (w.called.data[at] != NO_POINT) {
        model = ?w.calls.at[w.called.data[at]];
        if (fp.control.transfer != effect.CALL && !jumps)                     { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNCALLED, at)}; }
        if (w.stream != nil && jumps && fp.control.target != effect.FUNCTION) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNCALLED, at)}; }
        if (jumps)                                                            { tail = true; }
    }
    var shape:  *Shape = nil;
    var popped: usize  = 0;
    if (w.stream != nil) {
        shape  = ?w.shapes.data[w.shaped.data[at]];
        popped = pop_count(w, shape, ?fp.signature);
        if (p.stack.len < popped) { ret stays(at); }
    }
    if (model != nil && named_past(model, popped)) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNPOPPED, at)}; }
    var before: bool = false;
    var i:      u32  = w.declared.data[at];
    for (i != NO_POINT) {
        if (sel w.public.at[i].side.before) { before = true; }
        i = w.chain.data[i];
    }
    var r: *Point = p;
    if (before) {
        val made: err[A.Error] = assign(?w.lifted, p);
        if (sel made.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](made.err); }
        r = ?w.lifted;
    }
    if (before) {
        val lifting: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = lifts(w, r, at, ?ins, fp, shape, false);
        if (sel lifting.err)     { ret lifting; }
        if (sel lifting.ok.some) { ret lifting; }
    }
    var stacked: bool = false;
    k = r.stack.len - popped;
    for (k < r.stack.len) {
        if (r.stack.data[k]) { stacked = true; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    k = 0;
    for (k < w.words) {
        w.named.data[k] = 0;
        k               = k + 1;
    }
    var secret: u32 = 0;
    var op:     u32 = 0;
    for (op < ins.inst.count) {
        if (operand_secret(w, r, ?ins, op::u8, cfg, w.named.data) && op < 32) { secret = secret | (1::u32 << op); }
        op = op + 1;
    }
    val address: res[opt[ct.Refusal], A.Error] = touches(w, r, ?ins, fp);
    if (sel address.err)     { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](address.err); }
    if (sel address.ok.some) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{refused(address.ok.some, at)}; }
    if (!accessed(w))        { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNACCESSED, at)}; }
    resolve_pointers(w, at, ?ins);
    val carried: err[A.Error] = carry_pointers(w, r, at, ?ins);
    if (sel carried.err)                                   { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](carried.err); }
    if (w.stream == nil && switches_mode(w, at, ?ins, fp)) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{refused(ct.refusal(ct.SWITCHED, field.NO_OPERAND), at)}; }
    if (inlined(w, at)) {
        k = 0;
        for (k < w.touches.len) {
            if (lands_on_frame(w, ?w.touches.data[k])) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{refused(ct.refusal(ct.FRAMED, field.NO_OPERAND), at)}; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
    }
    if (before) {
        val lifting: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = lifts(w, r, at, ?ins, fp, shape, true);
        if (sel lifting.err)     { ret lifting; }
        if (sel lifting.ok.some) { ret lifting; }
    }
    var read: bool = entries_read(r, ?ins, fp);
    k = 0;
    for (k < w.words) {
        if (unaccrued(w, fp.reads.data[k] & r.taint.data[k] & ~kept_only(fp, k), k, fp.written.data[k]) != 0) { read = true; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    k = 0;
    for (k < w.touches.len) {
        if (reads_secret(w, r, ?w.touches.data[k])) { read = true; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    var c:        effect.Control  = fp.control;
    val transfer: opt[ct.Refusal] = control(w, r, ?ins, ?c, read, stacked, secret);
    if (sel transfer.some) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{refused(transfer.some, at)}; }
    if (w.timed) {
        val timing: opt[ct.Refusal] = latency(w, r, ?ins, fp, secret);
        if (sel timing.some) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{refused(timing.some, at)}; }
    }
    var joined: bool  = false;
    val callee: *Call = model;
    if (model != nil) {
        val j: res[Joined, A.Error] = join(w, r, model, popped);
        if (sel j.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](j.err); }
        joined = j.ok.secret;
        if (j.ok.unaccepted) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{refused(ct.refusal(ct.UNCHECKED, field.NO_OPERAND), at)}; }
        if (j.ok.pointed)    { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{refused(ct.refusal(ct.POINTED, field.NO_OPERAND), at)}; }
        if (tail)            { model = nil; }
    }
    val value: bool = read || stacked;
    if (value) {
        k = 0;
        for (k < w.touches.len) {
            val t: *Touch = ?w.touches.data[k];
            if (t.writes && t.seeded && !t.secret) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{refused(ct.refusal(ct.STORED, first_secret(secret, ins.inst.count)), at)}; }
            # a typed stream's producer states no store, its memory linear and placed nowhere
            if (t.writes && !t.seeded && w.stream == nil && unstated(w, t)) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{refused(ct.refusal(ct.UNSTATED, first_secret(secret, ins.inst.count)), at)}; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
    }
    if (shape != nil && c.target == effect.DEPTH) {
        val kept: err[A.Error] = carry(w, p, shape, ?fp.signature, effect.TypeRef.operand{c.operand});
        if (sel kept.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](kept.err); }
    }
    val applied: err[A.Error] = apply(w, p, at, ?ins, fp, value, model, joined);
    if (sel applied.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](applied.err); }
    val err_stated: err[A.Error] = state_pointers(w, p, at, fp, callee);
    if (sel err_stated.err)     { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](err_stated.err); }
    if (leaves_fixed(w, p, fp)) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{refused(ct.refusal(ct.FIXED, field.NO_OPERAND), at)}; }
    if (c.transfer == effect.RETURN || (tail && callee != nil)) {
        val left_secret: res[bool, A.Error] = result_secret(w, p);
        if (sel left_secret.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](left_secret.err); }
        if (left_secret.ok)      { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{refused(ct.refusal(ct.RESULT, field.NO_OPERAND), at)}; }
    }
    val bottom: usize = p.stack.len - popped;
    var left:   bool  = value;
    if (callee != nil) { left = joined; }
    if (shape != nil) {
        val streamed: err[A.Error] = apply_stream(w, p, ?ins, fp, shape, left, model);
        if (sel streamed.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](streamed.err); }
    }
    i = w.declared.data[at];
    for (i != NO_POINT) {
        val d: *Declassify = ?w.public.at[i];
        if (sel d.side.after) {
            val ok: res[bool, A.Error] = clear(w, p, ?w.pre, ?ins, fp, d, p.stack.len - bottom);
            if (sel ok.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](ok.err); }
            if (!ok.ok)     { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNTOUCHED, at)}; }
        }
        i = w.chain.data[i];
    }
    i = w.after.data[at];
    for (i != NO_POINT) {
        val sd: Seed = w.secrets.at[i];
        if (sel sd.after) {
            var e:  Written            = sd.after;
            val ok: res[bool, A.Error] = plant(w, p, ?w.pre, ?ins, fp, ?e, callee, p.stack.len - bottom);
            if (sel ok.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](ok.err); }
            if (!ok.ok)     { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, at)}; }
        }
        i = w.sowing.data[i];
    }
    ret successors(w, p, at, ?ins, ?c, shape, tail, left);
}

# register row `row` and every row overlapping it made secret in `p`, but one reading zero
fun taint_row(w: *Walk, p: *Point, row: u32) err[A.Error] {
    val span: res[register.Span, A.Error] = register.overlapping(?w.overlaps, row);
    if (sel span.err) { ret err[A.Error].err{span.err}; }
    var k: u32 = 0;
    for (k < span.ok.count) {
        val o: u32 = w.overlaps.rows.data[span.ok.first + k];
        if (stored(w, o)) { set_bit(p.taint.data, o, true); }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# the entry state the seeds make, a register's secret in every row overlapping it but one reading zero, a global's off
# its symbol, the frame seeds indexed by offset into `w.sown` and `w.sowing`, and the access and written seeds into
# `w.stated`, `w.after` and `w.sowing`, refused naming a register the file has no row of, an entry the stream does not
# hold, a frame slot, an access or a written place at one past the code, memory or a slot off a symbol, or a global of no
# symbol
fun seed(w: *Walk, secrets: *Secrets, p: *Point) res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < secrets.len) {
        val s: Seed = secrets.at[i];
        if (sel s.register) {
            val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, s.register);
            if (sel row.none) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, 0)}; }
            val marked: err[A.Error] = taint_row(w, p, row.some);
            if (sel marked.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](marked.err); }
        }
        if (sel s.memory) {
            if (s.memory.symbol != operand.NO_SYMBOL) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, 0)}; }
            if (sel s.memory.entry.some)              { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, 0)}; }
            var h: Held = Held{base: effect.NO_ROW, version: ENTRY, symbol: operand.NO_SYMBOL, slot: false, offset: s.memory.offset, length: s.memory.length, indexed: false, apart: false};
            if (s.memory.base != register.NONE) {
                val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, s.memory.base);
                if (sel row.none) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, 0)}; }
                h = rebase(w, p, row.some, s.memory.offset, s.memory.length);
            }
            h.apart = s.memory.no_global;
            val held: err[A.Error] = hold(w, p, h);
            if (sel held.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](held.err); }
        }
        if (sel s.symbol) {
            if (s.symbol.symbol == operand.NO_SYMBOL) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, 0)}; }
            val held: err[A.Error] = hold(w, p, Held{base: effect.NO_ROW, version: ENTRY, symbol: s.symbol.symbol, slot: false, offset: s.symbol.offset, length: s.symbol.length, indexed: false, apart: false});
            if (sel held.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](held.err); }
        }
        if (sel s.pointer) {
            if (s.pointer.at >= w.code.len::u64) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, s.pointer.at::usize)}; }
            val res_pointing: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Pointing](?w.pointing, Pointing{at: s.pointer.at, row: effect.NO_ROW, secret: s.pointer.secret});
            if (sel res_pointing.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](res_pointing.err); }
        }
        if (sel s.fixed) {
            val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, s.fixed);
            if (sel row.none) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, 0)}; }
            val err_marked: err[A.Error] = mark_overlapping(w, row.some, w.fixing.data);
            if (sel err_marked.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](err_marked.err); }
        }
        if (sel s.switch) {
            if (s.switch >= w.code.len::u64) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, s.switch::usize)}; }
            val res_switch: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u64](?w.switches, s.switch);
            if (sel res_switch.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](res_switch.err); }
        }
        if (sel s.saved) {
            if (w.stack == effect.NO_ROW || w.stream != nil || s.saved.length == 0) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, 0)}; }
            val err_saved: err[A.Error] = gather(?w.saves, Held{base: w.stack, version: ENTRY, symbol: operand.NO_SYMBOL, slot: false, offset: s.saved.offset, length: s.saved.length, indexed: false, apart: false});
            if (sel err_saved.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](err_saved.err); }
        }
        if (sel s.private) {
            if (w.stack == effect.NO_ROW || w.stream != nil || s.private.length == 0) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, 0)}; }
            val err_gathered: err[A.Error] = gather(?w.private, Held{base: w.stack, version: ENTRY, symbol: operand.NO_SYMBOL, slot: false, offset: s.private.offset, length: s.private.length, indexed: false, apart: false});
            if (sel err_gathered.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](err_gathered.err); }
        }
        if (sel s.local) {
            if (w.stack == effect.NO_ROW || w.stream != nil || s.local.length == 0) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, 0)}; }
            val h:          Held                = Held{base: w.stack, version: ENTRY, symbol: operand.NO_SYMBOL, slot: false, offset: s.local.offset, length: s.local.length, indexed: false, apart: false};
            val res_listed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Held](?w.objects, h);
            if (sel res_listed.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](res_listed.err); }
            if (s.local.public) {
                val err_typed: err[A.Error] = gather(?w.typed, h);
                if (sel err_typed.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](err_typed.err); }
            }
        }
        if (sel s.inline) {
            if (s.inline >= w.code.len::u64 || w.stream != nil) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, s.inline::usize)}; }
            val res_inlined: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u64](?w.inlined, s.inline);
            if (sel res_inlined.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](res_inlined.err); }
        }
        var next: u32 = NO_POINT;
        if (sel s.frame) {
            if (s.frame.extent.symbol != operand.NO_SYMBOL) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, 0)}; }
            val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, s.frame.extent.base);
            if (sel row.none)                  { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, 0)}; }
            if (s.frame.at >= w.code.len::u64) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, s.frame.at::usize)}; }
            next                           = w.sown.data[s.frame.at::usize];
            w.sown.data[s.frame.at::usize] = i;
        }
        if (sel s.access) {
            if (s.access.at >= w.code.len::u64) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, s.access.at::usize)}; }
            next                              = w.stated.data[s.access.at::usize];
            w.stated.data[s.access.at::usize] = i;
        }
        if (sel s.within) {
            if (s.within.at >= w.code.len::u64 || w.stack == effect.NO_ROW || w.stream != nil || s.within.length == 0) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, s.within.at::usize)}; }
            next                              = w.stated.data[s.within.at::usize];
            w.stated.data[s.within.at::usize] = i;
        }
        if (sel s.after) {
            val at: usize = s.after.at::usize;
            if (s.after.at >= w.code.len::u64) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, at)}; }
            val q: Place = s.after.place;
            if (sel q.entry) {
                if (w.stream == nil) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, at)}; }
                val there: opt[u32] = w.stream.space(w.ctx.stream, q.entry.space, q.entry.index);
                if (sel there.none) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, at)}; }
            }
            next             = w.after.data[at];
            w.after.data[at] = i;
        }
        val chained: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?w.sowing, next);
        if (sel chained.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](chained.err); }
        if (sel s.entry) {
            if (w.stream == nil) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, 0)}; }
            val there: opt[u32] = w.stream.space(w.ctx.stream, s.entry.space, s.entry.index);
            if (sel there.none) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSEEDABLE, 0)}; }
            val set: err[A.Error] = set_entry(p, key(s.entry.space, s.entry.index), true);
            if (sel set.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](set.err); }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{opt[Verdict].none{}};
}

# the frame seeds at `at` held in `p`, the state where the instruction there starts, each slot off its base register's
# value under it
fun sow(w: *Walk, p: *Point, at: usize) err[A.Error] {
    var i: u32 = w.sown.data[at];
    for (i != NO_POINT) {
        val sd: Seed = w.secrets.at[i];
        if (sel sd.frame) {
            val e:   Extent   = sd.frame.extent;
            val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, e.base);
            if (sel row.some) {
                var h: Held = rebase(w, p, row.some, e.offset, e.length);
                h.apart = e.no_global;
                val held: err[A.Error] = hold(w, p, h);
                if (sel held.err) { ret held; }
            }
        }
        i = w.sowing.data[i];
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# the height `height` of the operand stack less `n` values, none when that passes below `base`, its block's, and
# `base` in code no control reaches past a polymorphic stack, whose pops take values that are never there
fun lowered(height: u32, n: u32, base: u32, dead: bool) opt[u32] {
    if (height >= base + n) { ret opt[u32].some{height - n}; }
    if (dead)               { ret opt[u32].some{base}; }
    ret opt[u32].none{};
}

# whether every popped value the effect `e` and the control `c` name by depth is one of the `popped` an instruction pops
fun names_popped(e: *effect.Effect, c: *effect.Control, popped: u32) bool {
    if (c.condition::u32 > popped || c.chooses::u32 > popped) { ret false; }
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < e.memory.len) {
        val a: *effect.Access = ?e.memory.at[i];
        if (a.pop::u32 > popped) { ret false; }
        val count: effect.Count = a.width.count;
        if (sel count.popped) {
            if (count.popped::u32 >= popped) { ret false; }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret true;
}

# the counts of each type of signature `sig` of `ins` pushed onto `w.counts`, its pops' then its pushes', as the
# stream resolves each, 0 for the polymorphic stack
# ---
# ret: how many values it pops and pushes, none for a type the stream does not resolve
rec Counted {
    pops:   u32;
    pushes: u32;
}

fun counted(w: *Walk, ins: *codec.Decoded, sig: *effect.Signature) res[opt[Counted], A.Error] {
    var c: Counted = Counted{pops: 0, pushes: 0};
    var i: u32     = 0;
    for (i < sig.pops.len + sig.pushes.len) {
        var ref:    effect.TypeRef = effect.TypeRef.polymorphic{};
        var pushed: bool           = i >= sig.pops.len;
        if (pushed) { ref = sig.pushes.at[i - sig.pops.len]; }
        or          { ref = sig.pops.at[i]; }
        var n: u32 = 0;
        if (!sel ref.polymorphic) {
            val got: opt[u32] = w.stream.arity(w.ctx.stream, ?ins.inst, ref, pushed);
            if (sel got.none) { ret res[opt[Counted], A.Error].ok{opt[Counted].none{}}; }
            n = got.some;
        }
        val kept: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?w.counts, n);
        if (sel kept.err) { ret failed[opt[Counted]](kept.err); }
        if (pushed)       { c.pushes = c.pushes + n; }
        or                { c.pops = c.pops + n; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret res[opt[Counted], A.Error].ok{opt[Counted].some{c}};
}

# the blocks the depths of control `c` of `ins` name added to `w.targets`, by the blocks `open` holds open, innermost
# last
# ---
# ret: how many, none for a depth past every block open or an operand holding no depth
fun depths(w: *Walk, ins: *codec.Decoded, c: *effect.Control, open: *vector.Vector[u32]) res[opt[u32], A.Error] {
    if (c.target != effect.DEPTH)                                          { ret res[opt[u32], A.Error].ok{opt[u32].some{0}}; }
    if (c.operand == field.NO_OPERAND || c.operand::u32 >= ins.inst.count) { ret res[opt[u32], A.Error].ok{opt[u32].none{}}; }
    val v:    operand.Value  = ins.inst.values[c.operand];
    var one:  [1]operand.Value;
    var list: operand.Values = operand.Values{at: ?one[0], len: 1};
    one[0] = v;
    if (sel v.list) { list = v.list; }
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < list.len) {
        val d: operand.Value = list.at[i];
        if (!sel d.id)               { ret res[opt[u32], A.Error].ok{opt[u32].none{}}; }
        if (d.id::usize >= open.len) { ret res[opt[u32], A.Error].ok{opt[u32].none{}}; }
        val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?w.targets, open.data[open.len - 1 - d.id::usize]);
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret failed[opt[u32]](pushed.err); }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret res[opt[u32], A.Error].ok{opt[u32].some{list.len}};
}

# the catch clauses of the catching block `b` that `ins` at `at` opens onto `w.clauses`, each by the block the depth of
# its label names among those `open` holds, which the block is not yet one of
# ---
# ret: none when each names what the stream holds and a block open, else why the code cannot be followed
fun catches(w: *Walk, ins: *codec.Decoded, open: *vector.Vector[u32], b: *Block, at: usize) res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] {
    var listed: vector.Vector[stream.Catch] = vector.init[stream.Catch](w.a);
    fin { vector.dnit[stream.Catch](?listed); }
    val got: err[field.Refusal] = w.stream.catches(w.ctx.stream, ?ins.inst, ?listed);
    if (sel got.err) {
        if (sel got.err.cause.memory) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](got.err.cause.memory); }
        ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(got.err.message, at)};
    }
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < listed.len) {
        val c: *stream.Catch = ?listed.data[i];
        if (c.depth::usize >= open.len) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSTRUCTURED, at)}; }
        val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Clause](?w.clauses, Clause{block: open.data[open.len - 1 - c.depth::usize], values: c.values});
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](pushed.err); }
        b.catches = b.catches + 1;
        if (c.every) { b.every = true; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{opt[Verdict].none{}};
}

# how many values of the pops of signature `sig`, whose counts start at `first` in `w.counts`, a block takes as its
# params: those of each type the instruction opening it pushes again
fun params_of(w: *Walk, sig: *effect.Signature, first: u32) u32 {
    var n: u32 = 0;
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < sig.pops.len) {
        if (pushed_again(sig, sig.pops.at[i])) { n = n + w.counts.data[first + i]; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret n;
}

# the code of a typed stream read once in its own order, each instruction observed on the context's stream after it is
# read: how many values each type of its signature stands for, the blocks it opens, splits and closes, matched by
# their structure, the height of the operand stack below each block's params, and the blocks its depths name
# ---
# ret: none when every instruction reads and every block opened closes in order, else why the code cannot be followed
fun scan(w: *Walk, store: *vector.Vector[operand.Value], alts: *vector.Vector[requirement.Alternative]) res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] {
    var open: vector.Vector[u32] = vector.init[u32](w.a);
    fin { vector.dnit[u32](?open); }
    val root: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Block](?w.blocks, Block{open: NO_OFFSET, body: 0, split: NO_OFFSET, close: NO_OFFSET, base: 0, params: 0, results: 0, loops: false, catcher: NO_BLOCK, outer: NO_BLOCK, clauses: 0, catches: 0, every: false});
    if (sel root.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](root.err); }
    val outer: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?open, 0);
    if (sel outer.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](outer.err); }
    var height: u32   = 0;
    var dead:   bool  = false;
    var at:     usize = 0;
    for (at < w.code.len) {
        if (open.len == 0) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSTRUCTURED, at)}; }
        val got: res[codec.Decoded, field.Refusal] = codec.decode_grown(w.code.set.codec, w.ctx, w.code.data, w.code.len, at, store, alts);
        if (sel got.err) {
            if (sel got.err.cause.memory) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](got.err.cause.memory); }
            ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNDECODED, at)};
        }
        var ins:    codec.Decoded                = got.ok;
        val e:      *effect.Effect               = ins.inst.row.effect;
        val values: operand.Values               = operand.Values{at: ins.inst.values, len: ins.inst.count};
        val ctl:    query.Answer[effect.Control] = query.control(w.file, ins.inst.row.operands.at, e, values);
        if (sel ctl.undecided) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNDECIDED, at)}; }
        var c:     effect.Control             = ctl.decided;
        var shape: Shape                      = Shape{len: ins.len, counts: w.counts.len::u32, targets: w.targets.len::u32, depths: 0, block: NO_BLOCK, catcher: NO_BLOCK, stuck: false};
        val sized: res[opt[Counted], A.Error] = counted(w, ?ins, ?e.signature);
        if (sel sized.err)     { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](sized.err); }
        if (sel sized.ok.none) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNTYPED, at)}; }
        val n: Counted = sized.ok.some;
        if (!names_popped(e, ?c, n.pops)) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNBALANCED, at)}; }
        var i: u32 = 0;
        for (i < e.signature.pushes.len) {
            if (sel e.signature.pushes.at[i].polymorphic) { shape.stuck = true; }
            i = i + 1;
        }
        val named: res[opt[u32], A.Error] = depths(w, ?ins, ?c, ?open);
        if (sel named.err)     { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](named.err); }
        if (sel named.ok.none) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSTRUCTURED, at)}; }
        shape.depths = named.ok.some;
        val top: u32              = open.data[open.len - 1];
        val s:   effect.Structure = e.structure;
        shape.catcher = w.blocks.data[top].catcher;
        if (effect.opens(s)) {
            val params: u32      = params_of(w, ?e.signature, shape.counts);
            val below:  opt[u32] = lowered(height, n.pops, w.blocks.data[top].base, dead);
            if (sel below.none) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNBALANCED, at)}; }
            shape.block = w.blocks.len::u32;
            var block: Block = Block{open: at, body: at + ins.len, split: NO_OFFSET, close: NO_OFFSET, base: below.some, params: params, results: n.pushes, loops: s == effect.LOOPS, catcher: shape.catcher, outer: shape.catcher, clauses: w.clauses.len::u32, catches: 0, every: false};
            if (s == effect.CATCHES) {
                block.catcher = shape.block;
                val listed: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = catches(w, ?ins, ?open, ?block, at);
                if (sel listed.err)     { ret listed; }
                if (sel listed.ok.some) { ret listed; }
            }
            val opened: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Block](?w.blocks, block);
            if (sel opened.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](opened.err); }
            val nested: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?open, shape.block);
            if (sel nested.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](nested.err); }
            height = below.some + params;
            dead   = false;
        }
        or (s == effect.SPLITS) {
            val b: *Block = ?w.blocks.data[top];
            if (b.open == NO_OFFSET || b.loops || b.split != NO_OFFSET) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSTRUCTURED, at)}; }
            b.split     = at;
            shape.block = top;
            height      = b.base + b.params;
            dead        = false;
        }
        or (s == effect.CLOSES) {
            val b: *Block = ?w.blocks.data[top];
            b.close     = at;
            shape.block = top;
            vector.truncate[u32](?open, open.len - 1);
            height = b.base + b.results;
            dead   = false;
        }
        or {
            val below: opt[u32] = lowered(height, n.pops, w.blocks.data[top].base, dead);
            if (sel below.none) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNBALANCED, at)}; }
            height = below.some + n.pushes;
            if (shape.stuck) {
                height = w.blocks.data[top].base;
                dead   = true;
            }
        }
        w.shaped.data[at] = w.shapes.len::u32;
        val kept: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[Shape](?w.shapes, shape);
        if (sel kept.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](kept.err); }
        val seen: err[field.Refusal] = w.stream.observe(w.ctx.stream, ?ins.inst);
        if (sel seen.err) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(seen.err.message, at)}; }
        at = at + ins.len;
    }
    if (open.len != 0) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSTRUCTURED, at)}; }
    ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{opt[Verdict].none{}};
}

fun release(w: *Walk) {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < w.states.len) {
        drop(?w.states.data[i]);
        i = i + 1;
    }
    vector.dnit[Point](?w.states);
    vector.dnit[u64](?w.locals);
    vector.dnit[u32](?w.points);
    vector.dnit[u64](?w.queued);
    vector.dnit[u32](?w.heads);
    vector.dnit[usize](?w.fell);
    drop(?w.pre);
    vector.dnit[u64](?w.named);
    vector.dnit[Touch](?w.touches);
    vector.dnit[u32](?w.shaped);
    vector.dnit[Shape](?w.shapes);
    vector.dnit[u32](?w.counts);
    vector.dnit[u32](?w.targets);
    vector.dnit[Block](?w.blocks);
    vector.dnit[Clause](?w.clauses);
    vector.dnit[bool](?w.carried);
    vector.dnit[bool](?w.popped);
    register.release_overlaps(?w.overlaps);
    vector.dnit[Moved](?w.moved);
    vector.dnit[Derived](?w.derived);
    vector.dnit[u32](?w.sown);
    vector.dnit[u32](?w.sowing);
    vector.dnit[u32](?w.stated);
    vector.dnit[u32](?w.after);
    vector.dnit[Held](?w.private);
    vector.dnit[Held](?w.objects);
    vector.dnit[Held](?w.typed);
    vector.dnit[u32](?w.declared);
    vector.dnit[u32](?w.chain);
    vector.dnit[u32](?w.called);
    vector.dnit[u64](?w.keeping);
    vector.dnit[u64](?w.writing);
    vector.dnit[Held](?w.kept);
    vector.dnit[Held](?w.accepted);
    vector.dnit[Held](?w.wrote);
    vector.dnit[Held](?w.returned);
    vector.dnit[Saved](?w.saved);
    vector.dnit[u32](?w.sited);
    vector.dnit[Forming](?w.forming);
    drop(?w.state);
    drop(?w.lifted);
    compress.release(?w.expanded);
    vector.dnit[Pointing](?w.pointing);
    vector.dnit[u64](?w.fixing);
    vector.dnit[u64](?w.moding);
    vector.dnit[u64](?w.switches);
    vector.dnit[u64](?w.inlined);
    vector.dnit[Held](?w.saves);
    vector.dnit[Pointed](?w.stating);
}

# the declassify points indexed by offset into `w.declared` and `w.chain`, refused at one past the code
fun index_points(w: *Walk) res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < w.public.len) {
        val at: u64 = w.public.at[i].at;
        if (at >= w.code.len::u64) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(MISPLACED, at::usize)}; }
        val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?w.chain, w.declared.data[at::usize]);
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](pushed.err); }
        w.declared.data[at::usize] = i;
        i                          = i + 1;
    }
    ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{opt[Verdict].none{}};
}

# whether every register `regs` names has a row of the file
fun rowed(w: *Walk, regs: *Registers) bool {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < regs.len) {
        val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, regs.at[i]);
        if (sel row.none) { ret false; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret true;
}

# whether extent `e` names no entry, or a function's own with neither a base nor a symbol
fun entry_based(w: *Walk, e: *Extent) bool {
    if (sel e.entry.none) { ret true; }
    ret e.base == register.NONE && e.symbol == operand.NO_SYMBOL && is_local(w, key(e.entry.some.space, e.entry.some.index));
}

# whether every extent `e` names is off no register or one with a row of the file, none off both a register and a
# symbol, none off a symbol stated to hold no global's bytes, and each off an entry off a function's own alone
fun based(w: *Walk, e: *Extents) bool {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < e.len) {
        if (!entry_based(w, ?e.at[i]))                                            { ret false; }
        if (e.at[i].base != register.NONE && e.at[i].symbol != operand.NO_SYMBOL) { ret false; }
        if (e.at[i].symbol != operand.NO_SYMBOL && e.at[i].no_global)             { ret false; }
        if (e.at[i].base != register.NONE) {
            val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, e.at[i].base);
            if (sel row.none) { ret false; }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret true;
}

# whether rows `x` and `y` share storage
fun shares(w: *Walk, x: u32, y: u32) res[bool, A.Error] {
    val span: res[register.Span, A.Error] = register.overlapping(?w.overlaps, x);
    if (sel span.err) { ret failed[bool](span.err); }
    var k: u32 = 0;
    for (k < span.ok.count) {
        if (w.overlaps.rows.data[span.ok.first + k] == y) { ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{true}; }
        k = k + 1;
    }
    ret res[bool, A.Error].ok{x == y};
}

# the row of register `reg`, effect.NO_ROW for none
fun row_or_none(w: *Walk, reg: register.Id) u32 {
    val row: opt[u32] = row_index(w, reg);
    if (sel row.some) { ret row.some; }
    ret effect.NO_ROW;
}

fun naming(message: str) res[opt[str], A.Error] {
    ret res[opt[str], A.Error].ok{opt[str].some{message}};
}

# the refusal of call model `c` by what it names alone, none when it may model a call: a register of no row, an extent
# off both a register and a symbol, off a symbol stated to hold no global's bytes or off an entry with another base or
# of no function's own, a written register reading zero or sharing storage with a preserved one, an accepted register
# or read it does not name an argument or a read, and a preserved set without the stack pointer
fun malformed(w: *Walk, c: *Call) res[opt[str], A.Error] {
    if (!rowed(w, ?c.preserved) || !rowed(w, ?c.arguments) || !rowed(w, ?c.written)) { ret naming(UNWRITTEN); }
    if (!based(w, ?c.reads) || !based(w, ?c.writes) || !based(w, ?c.kept))           { ret naming(UNWRITTEN); }
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < c.accepted.len) {
        var named: bool = false;
        var k:     u32  = 0;
        for (k < c.arguments.len) {
            if (c.arguments.at[k] == c.accepted.at[i]) { named = true; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        if (!named) { ret naming(UNACCEPTED); }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < c.accepted_reads.len) {
        var named: bool = false;
        var k:     u32  = 0;
        for (k < c.reads.len) {
            if (same_extent(?c.reads.at[k], ?c.accepted_reads.at[i])) { named = true; }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        if (!named) { ret naming(UNACCEPTED); }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < c.written.len) {
        val row: u32 = row_or_none(w, c.written.at[i]);
        if ((w.file.registers[row].flags & register.ZERO) != 0) { ret naming(UNWRITTEN); }
        var k: u32 = 0;
        for (k < c.preserved.len) {
            val both: res[bool, A.Error] = shares(w, row, row_or_none(w, c.preserved.at[k]));
            if (sel both.err) { ret failed[opt[str]](both.err); }
            if (both.ok)      { ret naming(UNWRITTEN); }
            k = k + 1;
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    if (w.stack == effect.NO_ROW) { ret res[opt[str], A.Error].ok{opt[str].none{}}; }
    i = 0;
    for (i < c.preserved.len) {
        if (row_or_none(w, c.preserved.at[i]) == w.stack) { ret res[opt[str], A.Error].ok{opt[str].none{}}; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret naming(UNANCHORED);
}

# the keys of the entries of the spaces the stream states as a function's own into `w.locals`, as the context's stream
# holds them, entered into the function
fun index_locals(w: *Walk) err[A.Error] {
    if (w.stream == nil || w.code.len == 0) { ret err[A.Error].ok{}; }
    var s: u32 = 0;
    for (s < w.stream.locals.len) {
        val space: u16 = w.stream.locals.at[s];
        var index: u32 = 0;
        for {
            val there: opt[u32] = w.stream.space(w.ctx.stream, space, index);
            if (sel there.none) { brk; }
            val held: err[A.Error] = insert_key(?w.locals, key(space, index));
            if (sel held.err) { ret held; }
            index = index + 1;
        }
        s = s + 1;
    }
    ret err[A.Error].ok{};
}

# the call models indexed by offset into `w.called`, refused at one past the code, as a second at an offset, or by what
# one names alone
fun index_calls(w: *Walk) res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < w.calls.len) {
        val c:  *Call = ?w.calls.at[i];
        val at: u64   = c.at;
        if (at >= w.code.len::u64)                { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNCALLED, at::usize)}; }
        if (w.called.data[at::usize] != NO_POINT) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNCALLED, at::usize)}; }
        val bad: res[opt[str], A.Error] = malformed(w, c);
        if (sel bad.err)     { ret failed[opt[Verdict]](bad.err); }
        if (sel bad.ok.some) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(bad.ok.some, at::usize)}; }
        w.called.data[at::usize] = i;
        i                        = i + 1;
    }
    ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{opt[Verdict].none{}};
}

# the sites indexed by offset into `w.sited`, refused out of ascending order or at one past the code
fun index_sites(w: *Walk) res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] {
    var i: u32 = 0;
    for (i < w.code.sites.len) {
        val at: u64 = w.code.sites.at[i].at;
        if (at >= w.code.len::u64)                   { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSITED, at::usize)}; }
        if (i > 0 && w.code.sites.at[i - 1].at > at) { ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{unread(UNSITED, at::usize)}; }
        if (w.sited.data[at::usize] == NO_POINT)     { w.sited.data[at::usize] = i; }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    ret res[opt[Verdict], A.Error].ok{opt[Verdict].none{}};
}

fun walked(w: *Walk, secrets: *Secrets) res[Verdict, A.Error] {
    var i: usize = 0;
    for (i < w.code.len) {
        val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?w.points, NO_POINT);
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret failed[Verdict](pushed.err); }
        val res_head: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?w.heads, NO_POINT);
        if (sel res_head.err) { ret failed[Verdict](res_head.err); }
        val res_fell: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[usize](?w.fell, NO_OFFSET);
        if (sel res_fell.err) { ret failed[Verdict](res_fell.err); }
        if (i % 64 == 0) {
            val res_queued: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u64](?w.queued, 0);
            if (sel res_queued.err) { ret failed[Verdict](res_queued.err); }
        }
        val declared: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?w.declared, NO_POINT);
        if (sel declared.err) { ret failed[Verdict](declared.err); }
        val sown: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?w.sown, NO_POINT);
        if (sel sown.err) { ret failed[Verdict](sown.err); }
        val stated: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?w.stated, NO_POINT);
        if (sel stated.err) { ret failed[Verdict](stated.err); }
        val after: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?w.after, NO_POINT);
        if (sel after.err) { ret failed[Verdict](after.err); }
        val called: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?w.called, NO_POINT);
        if (sel called.err) { ret failed[Verdict](called.err); }
        val sited: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?w.sited, NO_POINT);
        if (sel sited.err) { ret failed[Verdict](sited.err); }
        if (w.stream != nil) {
            val shaped: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u32](?w.shaped, NO_POINT);
            if (sel shaped.err) { ret failed[Verdict](shaped.err); }
        }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    i = 0;
    for (i < w.words) {
        val pushed: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u64](?w.named, 0);
        if (sel pushed.err) { ret failed[Verdict](pushed.err); }
        val keeping: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u64](?w.keeping, 0);
        if (sel keeping.err) { ret failed[Verdict](keeping.err); }
        val writing: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u64](?w.writing, 0);
        if (sel writing.err) { ret failed[Verdict](writing.err); }
        val res_fixing: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u64](?w.fixing, 0);
        if (sel res_fixing.err) { ret failed[Verdict](res_fixing.err); }
        val res_moding: res[usize, A.Error] = vector.push[u64](?w.moding, 0);
        if (sel res_moding.err) { ret failed[Verdict](res_moding.err); }
        i = i + 1;
    }
    val err_modes: err[A.Error] = index_modes(w);
    if (sel err_modes.err) { ret failed[Verdict](err_modes.err); }
    var store: vector.Vector[operand.Value] = vector.init[operand.Value](w.a);
    fin { vector.dnit[operand.Value](?store); }
    var alts: vector.Vector[requirement.Alternative] = vector.init[requirement.Alternative](w.a);
    fin { vector.dnit[requirement.Alternative](?alts); }
    val made: res[Point, A.Error] = blank(w);
    if (sel made.err) { ret failed[Verdict](made.err); }
    var entry: Point = made.ok;
    fin { drop(?entry); }
    val locals: err[A.Error] = index_locals(w);
    if (sel locals.err) { ret failed[Verdict](locals.err); }
    val seeded: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = seed(w, secrets, ?entry);
    if (sel seeded.err)     { ret failed[Verdict](seeded.err); }
    if (sel seeded.ok.some) { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{seeded.ok.some}; }
    val indexed: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = index_points(w);
    if (sel indexed.err)     { ret failed[Verdict](indexed.err); }
    if (sel indexed.ok.some) { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{indexed.ok.some}; }
    val models: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = index_calls(w);
    if (sel models.err)     { ret failed[Verdict](models.err); }
    if (sel models.ok.some) { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{models.ok.some}; }
    val sites: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = index_sites(w);
    if (sel sites.err)     { ret failed[Verdict](sites.err); }
    if (sel sites.ok.some) { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{sites.ok.some}; }
    if (w.code.len == 0)   { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{Verdict.clear{}}; }
    if (w.stream != nil) {
        val read: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = scan(w, ?store, ?alts);
        if (sel read.err)     { ret failed[Verdict](read.err); }
        if (sel read.ok.some) { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{read.ok.some}; }
    }
    val reached: res[bool, A.Error] = reach(w, ?entry, NO_OFFSET, 0);
    if (sel reached.err) { ret failed[Verdict](reached.err); }
    val made_fp: res[footprint.Footprint, A.Error] = footprint.make(w.a, w.file);
    if (sel made_fp.err) { ret failed[Verdict](made_fp.err); }
    var fp: footprint.Footprint = made_fp.ok;
    fin { footprint.release(?fp); }
    for {
        val head: opt[usize] = dequeue(w);
        if (sel head.none) { brk; }
        var at: usize = head.some;
        w.heads.data[at] = at::u32;
        val err_held: err[A.Error] = assign(?w.state, ?w.states.data[w.points.data[at]]);
        if (sel err_held.err) { ret failed[Verdict](err_held.err); }
        for {
            w.next = NO_OFFSET;
            val stepped: res[opt[Verdict], A.Error] = step(w, at, ?store, ?alts, ?fp);
            if (sel stepped.err)     { ret failed[Verdict](stepped.err); }
            if (sel stepped.ok.some) { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{stepped.ok.some}; }
            if (w.next == NO_OFFSET) { brk; }
            at = w.next;
        }
    }
    # a point in code the walk never reaches, or within an instruction of code no path walks, is applied nowhere
    var n: u32 = 0;
    for (n < w.public.len) {
        val at: u64 = w.public.at[n].at;
        if (w.points.data[at::usize] == NO_POINT) { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{Verdict.unread{Unread{message: MISPLACED, offset: at}}}; }
        n = n + 1;
    }
    # a call model at an offset no path reaches models nothing
    n = 0;
    for (n < w.calls.len) {
        val at: u64 = w.calls.at[n].at;
        if (w.points.data[at::usize] == NO_POINT) { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{Verdict.unread{Unread{message: UNCALLED, offset: at}}}; }
        n = n + 1;
    }
    # a frame or written seed whose instruction no path reaches holds nowhere
    n = 0;
    for (n < secrets.len) {
        val s: Seed = secrets.at[n];
        if (sel s.frame) {
            if (w.points.data[s.frame.at::usize] == NO_POINT) { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{Verdict.unread{Unread{message: UNSEEDABLE, offset: s.frame.at}}}; }
        }
        if (sel s.after) {
            if (w.points.data[s.after.at::usize] == NO_POINT) { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{Verdict.unread{Unread{message: UNSEEDABLE, offset: s.after.at}}}; }
        }
        n = n + 1;
    }
    ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{Verdict.clear{}};
}

# the constant-time walk of `code` under the context the function runs under, from the secrets the caller seeds,
# public again only at the declassify points `public` states, NO_DECLASSIFIED for none, and each call walked through
# the model `calls` states at its offset, NO_CALLS for none, the conservative rule standing where none does, and each
# return and tail call held to leave no secret in a public piece of the function's own `results`, NO_RESULTS for none. a
# set whose timing is `none` is refused before any walk, worded UNCLASSIFIED, and one whose timing is not guaranteed
# is walked asking no row's latency, code it clears answered unguaranteed. code of a typed stream is read once in its
# own order first, observed on the context's stream, which it leaves as reading the function's body leaves it, and is
# answered unread when its set classifies its rows' timing, as no class states inputs among the values a row pops
# ---
# ret: the verdict, or the allocator's refusal of the walk's storage
pub fun check(a: *A.Allocator, code: *Code, ctx: *state.Context, secrets: *Secrets, public: *Declassified, calls: *Calls, results: *Results) res[Verdict, A.Error] {
    ret check_timed(a, code, ctx, ctx, secrets, public, calls, results);
}

# the walk `check` takes, with each row's timing classified under `timing`, a context holding the timing promises the
# caller assumes, while decoding, footprints, the stack row and the architecture stay under `ctx`, the build's own
# ---
# ret: the verdict, or the allocator's refusal of the walk's storage
pub fun check_timed(a: *A.Allocator, code: *Code, ctx: *state.Context, timing: *state.Context, secrets: *Secrets, public: *Declassified, calls: *Calls, results: *Results) res[Verdict, A.Error] {
    val answer: ct.Required = ct.required(code.set.ct);
    if (sel answer.refused)                              { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{Verdict.refused{Finding{offset: 0, refusal: answer.refused}}}; }
    if (code.set.codec.stream != nil && sel answer.held) { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{Verdict.unread{Unread{message: TIMED, offset: 0}}}; }
    var file: *register.File = code.set.codec.registers;
    if (file == nil) { file = ?NO_FILE; }
    val overlaps: res[register.Overlaps, A.Error] = register.overlaps_of(a, file);
    if (sel overlaps.err) { ret failed[Verdict](overlaps.err); }
    var expanded: compress.Expansions;
    if (!compress.expansions(a, code.set.codec, code.set.compress, ?expanded)) {
        var held: register.Overlaps = overlaps.ok;
        register.release_overlaps(?held);
        ret failed[Verdict](A.Error.exhausted{});
    }
    # read only once an instruction is decoded, which fills it
    var written: [operand.MAX_OPERANDS]u8;
    var w:       Walk = Walk{
        a:        a,
        code:     code,
        timed:    sel answer.held,
        ctx:      ctx,
        timing:   timing,
        file:     file,
        words:    effect.words(file)::usize,
        stream:   code.set.codec.stream,
        locals:   vector.init[u64](a),
        points:   vector.init[u32](a),
        states:   vector.init[Point](a),
        queued:   vector.init[u64](a),
        low:      0,
        heads:    vector.init[u32](a),
        fell:     vector.init[usize](a),
        next:     NO_OFFSET,
        pre:      empty(a),
        named:    vector.init[u64](a),
        touches:  vector.init[Touch](a),
        shaped:   vector.init[u32](a),
        shapes:   vector.init[Shape](a),
        counts:   vector.init[u32](a),
        targets:  vector.init[u32](a),
        blocks:   vector.init[Block](a),
        clauses:  vector.init[Clause](a),
        carried:  vector.init[bool](a),
        popped:   vector.init[bool](a),
        public:   public,
        declared: vector.init[u32](a),
        chain:    vector.init[u32](a),
        overlaps: overlaps.ok,
        stack:    stack_row(file, code, ctx),
        moved:    vector.init[Moved](a),
        derived:  vector.init[Derived](a),
        secrets:  secrets,
        results:  results,
        sown:     vector.init[u32](a),
        sowing:   vector.init[u32](a),
        stated:   vector.init[u32](a),
        after:    vector.init[u32](a),
        private:  vector.init[Held](a),
        objects:  vector.init[Held](a),
        typed:    vector.init[Held](a),
        calls:    calls,
        called:   vector.init[u32](a),
        keeping:  vector.init[u64](a),
        writing:  vector.init[u64](a),
        kept:     vector.init[Held](a),
        accepted: vector.init[Held](a),
        wrote:    vector.init[Held](a),
        returned: vector.init[Held](a),
        saved:    vector.init[Saved](a),
        arch:     arch_of(code, ctx),
        sited:    vector.init[u32](a),
        forming:  vector.init[Forming](a),
        state:    empty(a),
        lifted:   empty(a),
        expanded: expanded,
        written:  written,
        at:       0,
        pointing: vector.init[Pointing](a),
        fixing:   vector.init[u64](a),
        moding:   vector.init[u64](a),
        switches: vector.init[u64](a),
        inlined:  vector.init[u64](a),
        saves:    vector.init[Held](a),
        stating:  vector.init[Pointed](a),
    };
    val verdict: res[Verdict, A.Error] = walked(?w, secrets);
    release(?w);
    if (sel verdict.ok) {
        if (!w.timed && sel verdict.ok.clear) { ret res[Verdict, A.Error].ok{Verdict.unguaranteed{}}; }
    }
    ret verdict;
}
